window.LEVEL_DATA["C1"] = {"ai-02":{"intro":"Kuruluş hikâyeni, vurgulu yapılar ve ölçülü bir dille deneyimli bir gazeteciye anlatıyorsun.","text":[{"en":"Roughly one in five people on the planet lives with some degree of hearing loss, which adds up to well over a billion.","tr":"Dünyada kabaca her beş kişiden biri bir derece işitme kaybıyla yaşıyor; bu da bir milyarı rahatça aşan bir sayı ediyor."},{"en":"What struck us wasn't the number itself but how few of those people ever get tested.","tr":"Bizi asıl çarpan rakamın kendisi değil, bu insanların ne kadar azının test yaptırdığıydı."},{"en":"The bottleneck isn't the technology; it's the chronic shortage of audiologists.","tr":"Darboğaz teknoloji değil; kronik odyolog eksikliği."},{"en":"Outside the big cities, waiting several months for an appointment is not the exception but the rule.","tr":"Büyük şehirlerin dışında bir randevu için birkaç ay beklemek istisna değil, kural."},{"en":"Faced with that, we kept circling back to one deceptively simple question.","tr":"Bununla karşılaşınca, aldatıcı derecede basit bir soruya sürekli geri döndük."},{"en":"What if the test itself could be run by a machine, with no expert needing to be in the room?","tr":"Ya testin kendisi, odada bir uzmanın bulunmasına gerek kalmadan bir makine tarafından yapılabilseydi?"},{"en":"That question is, in a very real sense, what AIHEAR was built on.","tr":"Bu soru, gerçek anlamda AIHEAR'ın üzerine kurulduğu şey."},{"en":"We're now a team of six, and the mix is deliberate: three engineers, a doctor and two people on the business side.","tr":"Şu an altı kişilik bir ekibiz ve bu karışım bilinçli: üç mühendis, bir doktor ve iş tarafında iki kişi."},{"en":"Our mission is to make hearing tests accessible to everyone, regardless of where they happen to live.","tr":"Misyonumuz, işitme testlerini insanlar nerede yaşıyor olursa olsun herkes için erişilebilir kılmak."},{"en":"Not only is the problem far from unique to Turkey, but it is arguably most acute where healthcare is stretched thinnest.","tr":"Sorun Türkiye'ye özgü olmaktan çok uzak olmakla kalmıyor, sağlık sisteminin en zorlandığı yerlerde belki de en ağır hâlini alıyor."},{"en":"That's why, although we started in Turkey, we've always seen the market as global.","tr":"Bu yüzden Türkiye'de başlamış olsak da pazarı her zaman küresel olarak gördük."}],"vocab":[{"en":"add up to","tr":"toplamda ... etmek","ex":"One in five people adds up to over a billion.","def":"to make a particular total"},{"en":"what struck us","tr":"bizi asıl çarpan şey","ex":"What struck us was how few people get tested.","def":"the thing that made a strong impression on us"},{"en":"bottleneck","tr":"darboğaz","ex":"The real bottleneck is the shortage of audiologists.","def":"something that slows down or limits a process"},{"en":"chronic shortage","tr":"kronik eksiklik","ex":"There is a chronic shortage of audiologists.","def":"a lack of something that continues for a long time"},{"en":"not the exception but the rule","tr":"istisna değil, kural","ex":"Long waits are not the exception but the rule.","def":"something that is normal, not unusual"},{"en":"circle back to","tr":"...e geri dönmek","ex":"We kept circling back to the same question.","def":"to return to a topic again"},{"en":"in a very real sense","tr":"gerçek anlamda","ex":"In a very real sense, that question built the company.","def":"used to say that something is true in an important way"},{"en":"regardless of","tr":"...e bakılmaksızın","ex":"Everyone should get tested, regardless of where they live.","def":"without being affected by something"},{"en":"far from unique to","tr":"...e özgü olmaktan çok uzak","ex":"The problem is far from unique to Turkey.","def":"definitely not found in only one place"},{"en":"stretched thin","tr":"kaynakları çok zorlanmış","ex":"Healthcare is stretched thinnest in rural areas.","def":"having too few resources for what is needed"}],"grammar":{"title":"Cleft sentences for emphasis","tr":"Cleft cümleler (What ... was ... / It's ... that ...) bir bilgiyi öne çıkarıp vurgular. Hikâye anlatırken dinleyicinin dikkatini asıl noktaya çeker.","examples":["What struck us wasn't the number itself but how few people get tested.","That question is what AIHEAR was built on.","It's the shortage of audiologists that creates the bottleneck."]},"questions":[{"q":"What surprised the founders most?","options":["The number of people with hearing loss","How few people with hearing loss ever get tested","The cost of hearing aids"],"a":1},{"q":"According to the speaker, what is the real bottleneck?","options":["A chronic shortage of audiologists","The technology","The price of headphones"],"a":0},{"q":"What does 'not the exception but the rule' imply about waiting times?","options":["Long waits are rare","Only big cities have long waits","Long waits are normal outside big cities"],"a":2},{"q":"Why does the speaker describe the team mix as 'deliberate'?","options":["It happened by accident","It was chosen on purpose to cover technology, medicine and business","They couldn't find more engineers"],"a":1},{"q":"What is the speaker's attitude towards growing beyond Turkey?","options":["Hesitant","Indifferent","Reluctant because of costs","It was always part of the plan"],"a":3}],"gaps":[{"s":"The ___ isn't the technology; it's the shortage of audiologists.","a":"bottleneck","hint":"darboğaz"},{"s":"We kept circling ___ to one simple question.","a":"back","hint":"geri dönmek"},{"s":"We want tests to be accessible to everyone, ___ of where they live.","a":"regardless","hint":"...e bakılmaksızın"}],"order":[{"a":"That question is what AIHEAR was built on."},{"a":"We have always seen the market as global."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Darboğaz teknoloji değil, odyolog eksikliği.","en":"The bottleneck isn't the technology but the shortage of audiologists.","keys":["bottleneck","shortage of audiologists"]},{"tr":"Bizi asıl çarpan şey, ne kadar az insanın test yaptırdığıydı.","en":"What struck us was how few people get tested.","keys":["what struck us","few people"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Journalist","personaTr":"Gazeteci","scene":"Uluslararası bir iş dergisinden deneyimli bir gazeteci, kuruluş hikâyeni zorlayıcı sorularla dinliyor.","turns":[{"ai":"Hearing tests aren't exactly the most glamorous corner of health tech, so what drew you to it?","aiTr":"İşitme testleri sağlık teknolojisinin en göz alıcı köşesi sayılmaz; sizi buna ne çekti?","hint":"What struck us was how few of the billion-plus people with hearing loss ever get tested.","keys":["what struck us","get tested","hearing loss"]},{"ai":"Surely that's a funding problem rather than something technology can fix?","aiTr":"Bu, teknolojinin çözebileceği bir şeyden çok bir finansman sorunu değil mi?","hint":"Partly, but the real bottleneck is a chronic shortage of audiologists, and you can't train them fast enough.","keys":["bottleneck","shortage","audiologists"]},{"ai":"So how did that turn into a company?","aiTr":"Peki bu nasıl bir şirkete dönüştü?","hint":"We kept circling back to one question: what if a machine could run the test with no expert in the room?","keys":["circling back","what if","no expert"]},{"ai":"You're based in Turkey, so is this really a global business, or is that just pitch talk?","aiTr":"Türkiye'de yerleşiksiniz; bu gerçekten küresel bir iş mi, yoksa sadece sunum lafı mı?","hint":"Not only is the problem far from unique to Turkey, but it's often most acute where healthcare is stretched thinnest.","keys":["far from unique","most acute","stretched"]}]}},"ai-01":{"intro":"Cihazını deneyimli bir doktora derinlemesine ve ikna edici bir dille anlatıyorsun.","text":[{"en":"At its core, an audiometer does one thing: it measures how well someone can hear across different pitches and volumes.","tr":"Özünde bir odyometre tek bir şey yapar: birinin farklı perdelerde ve ses seviyelerinde ne kadar iyi duyduğunu ölçer."},{"en":"Conventionally, that means a trained audiologist, a soundproofed room and the best part of half an hour per patient.","tr":"Geleneksel olarak bu, eğitimli bir odyolog, ses yalıtımlı bir oda ve hasta başına neredeyse yarım saat demektir."},{"en":"What we've built is an autonomous audiometer, one that runs the entire test without an expert having to be in the room.","tr":"Bizim geliştirdiğimiz şey otonom bir odyometre; yani odada bir uzmanın bulunmasına gerek kalmadan tüm testi yürüten bir cihaz."},{"en":"The patient puts on a pair of headphones, follows the on-screen instructions and presses a button whenever they hear a tone.","tr":"Hasta bir kulaklık takar, ekrandaki talimatları izler ve bir ton duyduğu her an bir düğmeye basar."},{"en":"Rather than working through a fixed sequence, our AI interprets each response and calibrates the next tone in real time.","tr":"Yapay zekâmız sabit bir sırayı takip etmek yerine her yanıtı yorumlar ve bir sonraki tonu gerçek zamanlı olarak ayarlar."},{"en":"In practice, this means the test homes in on each patient's hearing thresholds far faster than a standard protocol would.","tr":"Pratikte bu, testin her hastanın işitme eşiklerini standart bir protokolden çok daha hızlı saptaması anlamına gelir."},{"en":"Once the test is complete, the device generates an audiogram that a clinician can review straight away.","tr":"Test tamamlandığında cihaz, bir klinisyenin hemen inceleyebileceği bir odyogram oluşturur."},{"en":"Not only does the whole process take under ten minutes, but it also frees up specialists for the cases that genuinely need them.","tr":"Tüm süreç on dakikadan kısa sürmekle kalmaz, uzmanları gerçekten onlara ihtiyaç duyan vakalar için de serbest bırakır."},{"en":"Crucially, the AI runs locally on the device rather than in the cloud.","tr":"En önemlisi, yapay zekâ bulutta değil, doğrudan cihazın üzerinde çalışır."},{"en":"Patient data therefore never leaves the clinic, and the device works just as well in a small town with no internet connection.","tr":"Bu nedenle hasta verileri kliniği asla terk etmez ve cihaz internet bağlantısı olmayan küçük bir kasabada da aynı şekilde çalışır."},{"en":"We push software updates roughly once a month, so the device keeps improving long after it has been installed.","tr":"Yazılım güncellemelerini yaklaşık ayda bir gönderiyoruz, böylece cihaz kurulduktan çok sonra da gelişmeye devam ediyor."}],"vocab":[{"en":"at its core","tr":"özünde","ex":"At its core, the device measures hearing.","def":"at the most basic or important level"},{"en":"soundproofed room","tr":"ses yalıtımlı oda","ex":"Most clinics test patients in a soundproofed room.","def":"a room built so that outside noise cannot get in"},{"en":"the best part of","tr":"neredeyse tamamı","ex":"A standard test takes the best part of half an hour.","def":"almost all of a period of time"},{"en":"calibrate","tr":"kalibre etmek, hassas ayarlamak","ex":"The AI calibrates the next tone in real time.","def":"to adjust something precisely so it gives accurate results"},{"en":"home in on","tr":"...i hızla saptamak","ex":"The test homes in on each patient's thresholds.","def":"to move quickly and directly towards a target"},{"en":"hearing threshold","tr":"işitme eşiği","ex":"The device finds the hearing threshold at each frequency.","def":"the quietest sound a person can hear"},{"en":"free up","tr":"serbest bırakmak, zaman açmak","ex":"Automation frees up specialists for complex cases.","def":"to make someone or something available for other uses"},{"en":"run locally","tr":"yerel olarak çalışmak","ex":"The AI runs locally on the device.","def":"to work on the device itself, not on a remote server"},{"en":"crucially","tr":"en önemlisi","ex":"Crucially, patient data never leaves the clinic.","def":"used to introduce the most important point"},{"en":"push an update","tr":"güncelleme göndermek","ex":"We push an update roughly once a month.","def":"to send new software to devices that are already in use"}],"grammar":{"title":"Inversion after 'Not only'","tr":"'Not only' cümle başına gelince yardımcı fiil özneden önce gelir (Not only does it...). Vurgu katar ve resmi sunumlarda etkili durur. İkinci kısım genelde 'but (it) also' ile devam eder.","examples":["Not only does the process take under ten minutes, but it also frees up specialists.","Not only is the data safer, but the device also works offline.","Not only did we cut the test time, but we also removed the need for an expert in the room."]},"questions":[{"q":"What does 'the best part of half an hour' mean?","options":["Exactly thirty minutes","Almost thirty minutes","The most useful thirty minutes"],"a":1},{"q":"How does the AI differ from a standard protocol?","options":["It interprets each response and calibrates the next tone","It plays every tone in a fixed order","It lets the patient choose the volume"],"a":0},{"q":"What does the speaker imply about specialists?","options":["They will no longer be needed","They don't trust the device","Their time is better spent on cases that genuinely need them"],"a":2},{"q":"Why does the speaker say 'crucially' before mentioning that the AI runs locally?","options":["They see privacy and offline use as a key advantage","They want to apologise for missing cloud features","They are unsure whether it works"],"a":0},{"q":"What is the speaker's attitude towards the product?","options":["Apologetic and unsure","Casual and joking","Critical of its design","Confident but precise"],"a":3}],"gaps":[{"s":"Conventionally, that means a trained audiologist and a ___ room.","a":"soundproofed","hint":"ses yalıtımlı"},{"s":"The test homes ___ on each patient's thresholds.","a":"in","hint":"hızla saptamak (home ___ on)"},{"s":"___ does the process take under ten minutes, but it also frees up specialists.","a":"Not only","hint":"sadece ... değil"},{"s":"The AI runs ___ on the device rather than in the cloud.","a":"locally","hint":"yerel olarak"}],"order":[{"a":"The AI runs locally on the device rather than in the cloud."},{"a":"Patient data never leaves the clinic."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Hasta verileri kliniği asla terk etmez.","en":"Patient data never leaves the clinic.","keys":["patient data","never leaves"]},{"tr":"Cihaz, odada bir uzman olmadan tüm testi yürütür.","en":"The device runs the entire test without an expert in the room.","keys":["without an expert","in the room"]},{"tr":"Uzmanları gerçekten ihtiyaç duyulan vakalar için serbest bırakır.","en":"It frees up specialists for the cases that really need them.","keys":["frees up","specialists"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Curious doctor","personaTr":"Meraklı doktor","scene":"Bir fuarda deneyimli bir İngiliz kulak burun boğaz uzmanı, cihazını eleştirel sorularla sınıyor.","turns":[{"ai":"I've seen a few 'AI audiometers' at these fairs, and frankly most of them are glorified hearing screeners.","aiTr":"Bu fuarlarda birkaç 'yapay zekâlı odyometre' gördüm ve açıkçası çoğu, abartılmış işitme tarama cihazlarından ibaret.","hint":"That's a fair point, but what we've built is a full autonomous audiometer: it runs the entire test and produces a proper audiogram.","keys":["autonomous audiometer","entire test","audiogram"]},{"ai":"How does it cope with patients who respond inconsistently?","aiTr":"Tutarsız yanıt veren hastalarla nasıl başa çıkıyor?","hint":"Rather than following a fixed sequence, the AI interprets each response and calibrates the next tone in real time, so it homes in on the true threshold.","keys":["calibrates","real time","fixed sequence"]},{"ai":"My worry is that it takes audiologists out of the picture altogether.","aiTr":"Benim endişem, odyologları tamamen devre dışı bırakması.","hint":"Not at all: it frees up audiologists for the cases that genuinely need them, and a clinician can still review every audiogram.","keys":["frees up","review","genuinely need"]},{"ai":"And where does all that patient data end up?","aiTr":"Peki tüm bu hasta verileri nereye gidiyor?","hint":"Nowhere, in fact: the AI runs locally on the device, so the data never leaves your clinic.","keys":["locally","never leaves","on the device"]}]}},"st-02":{"intro":"Küçük bir ekibi yönetme felsefeni; net sorumluluklar, suçlamasız bir kültür ve dinlemeyi öğrenmek üzerinden anlatıyorsun.","text":[{"en":"With only six of us, there's no room for the kind of miscommunication that bigger companies can absorb.","tr":"Sadece altı kişi olduğumuz için, büyük şirketlerin kaldırabileceği türden yanlış anlaşılmalara yerimiz yok."},{"en":"The one ritual we never skip is the Monday morning stand-up.","tr":"Asla atlamadığımız tek ritüel, pazartesi sabahı yaptığımız kısa toplantı."},{"en":"Everyone covers three things, namely what they've delivered, what's coming next and what's blocking them, and we keep it brisk.","tr":"Herkes üç şeyi anlatır, yani neyi teslim ettiğini, sırada ne olduğunu ve onu neyin engellediğini; toplantıyı da kısa ve tempolu tutarız."},{"en":"What I've learned the hard way is that a vague request almost always produces a vague result.","tr":"Acı tecrübeyle öğrendiğim şey, belirsiz bir isteğin neredeyse her zaman belirsiz bir sonuç doğurduğu."},{"en":"So every task now comes with a single owner and a hard deadline: not 'have a look at the report', but 'finish the test report by Friday'.","tr":"Bu yüzden artık her görevin tek bir sorumlusu ve kesin bir son tarihi var: 'rapora bir göz at' değil, 'test raporunu cumaya kadar bitir'."},{"en":"When something goes wrong, the focus is on fixing the process rather than finding a culprit.","tr":"Bir şeyler ters gittiğinde odak, bir suçlu bulmak değil süreci düzeltmektir."},{"en":"Were people to feel they'd be blamed for mistakes, they'd simply stop flagging problems early, which is the last thing a startup can afford.","tr":"İnsanlar hatalar yüzünden suçlanacaklarını hissetseydi, sorunları erkenden dile getirmeyi bırakırlardı; bu da bir girişimin kaldırabileceği en son şey."},{"en":"I give feedback often, positive and negative alike, and I actively ask for it in return.","tr":"Olumlu olsun olumsuz olsun sık sık geri bildirim veririm ve karşılığında da bunu aktif olarak isterim."},{"en":"Not long ago, one of our engineers pointed out that I tended to dominate meetings, which stung, if I'm honest.","tr":"Kısa süre önce mühendislerimizden biri toplantılarda konuşmayı tekeline alma eğiliminde olduğumu söyledi; dürüst olmak gerekirse bu biraz canımı yaktı."},{"en":"She was right, though, and since then I've made a point of listening more than I talk.","tr":"Yine de haklıydı ve o zamandan beri konuştuğumdan daha çok dinlemeye özen gösteriyorum."},{"en":"Having hired people who know their craft far better than I do, I see my job as trusting them and clearing obstacles out of their way.","tr":"İşini benden çok daha iyi bilen insanları işe aldığım için, görevimi onlara güvenmek ve önlerindeki engelleri kaldırmak olarak görüyorum."}],"vocab":[{"en":"absorb","tr":"kaldırmak, sindirmek","ex":"Bigger companies can absorb a bit of miscommunication.","def":"to deal with a cost or problem without serious damage"},{"en":"keep it brisk","tr":"kısa ve tempolu tutmak","ex":"We keep the stand-up brisk.","def":"to keep something quick and energetic"},{"en":"learn the hard way","tr":"acı tecrübeyle öğrenmek","ex":"I've learned the hard way that vague requests produce vague results.","def":"to learn something through a bad experience"},{"en":"hard deadline","tr":"kesin son tarih","ex":"Every task comes with a hard deadline.","def":"a deadline that cannot be moved"},{"en":"culprit","tr":"suçlu, sorumlu","ex":"We fix the process rather than finding a culprit.","def":"the person or thing responsible for a problem"},{"en":"flag a problem","tr":"bir sorunu dile getirmek","ex":"People stop flagging problems early if they fear blame.","def":"to point out a problem so that others notice it"},{"en":"the last thing you can afford","tr":"kaldırabileceğin en son şey","ex":"Hidden problems are the last thing a startup can afford.","def":"something that would be very harmful for you"},{"en":"dominate a meeting","tr":"toplantıda konuşmayı tekeline almak","ex":"I tended to dominate meetings.","def":"to talk so much that others cannot contribute"},{"en":"make a point of","tr":"özellikle özen göstermek","ex":"I've made a point of listening more than I talk.","def":"to deliberately make sure you always do something"},{"en":"know your craft","tr":"işini iyi bilmek","ex":"I've hired people who know their craft.","def":"to be highly skilled at your work"}],"grammar":{"title":"Inverted conditionals: 'Were people to…'","tr":"Resmî ve vurgulu bir şart cümlesi için 'if' düşer ve 'were' özneden önce gelir: 'Were people to feel…' = 'If people felt…'. Ciddi konuşmalarda ve yazıda kullanılır.","examples":["Were people to feel they'd be blamed, they'd stop flagging problems.","Were we to skip the stand-up, things would slip.","Were I to dominate every meeting, nobody would speak up."]},"questions":[{"q":"What is the one ritual the team never skips?","options":["The Friday review","The Monday morning stand-up","A monthly team dinner"],"a":1},{"q":"Why does the speaker insist on a single owner and a hard deadline?","options":["Because vague requests tend to produce vague results","Because investors require it","Because the engineers asked for it"],"a":0},{"q":"What does the speaker imply about blaming people for mistakes?","options":["It makes people work harder","It is necessary in a small team","It would make people hide problems until it is too late"],"a":2},{"q":"How did the speaker react to the engineer's criticism?","options":["Angrily and defensively","It hurt a little, but they accepted she was right","With complete indifference"],"a":1},{"q":"What is the speaker's overall attitude to leadership?","options":["Leaders should control every detail","Leaders should avoid giving feedback","Leaders should trust skilled people and remove obstacles"],"a":2}],"gaps":[{"s":"I've learned the ___ way that vague requests produce vague results.","a":"hard","hint":"acı tecrübeyle"},{"s":"The focus is on fixing the process rather than finding a ___.","a":"culprit","hint":"suçlu"},{"s":"People would simply stop ___ problems early.","a":"flagging","hint":"dile getirmek"},{"s":"I've made a ___ of listening more than I talk.","a":"point","hint":"özen göstermek"}],"order":[{"a":"The one ritual we never skip is the Monday stand-up."},{"a":"I've made a point of listening more than I talk."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Belirsiz bir istek neredeyse her zaman belirsiz bir sonuç doğurur.","en":"A vague request almost always produces a vague result.","keys":["vague request","vague result"]},{"tr":"Suçlu aramak yerine süreci düzeltmeye odaklanırız.","en":"We focus on fixing the process rather than finding a culprit.","keys":["fixing the process","culprit"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"New engineer","personaTr":"Yeni işe başlayan mühendis","scene":"Önceki işinde katı bir yönetim görmüş yeni mühendis, burada işlerin nasıl yürüdüğünü anlamaya çalışıyor.","turns":[{"ai":"I'm still finding my feet here; how do you like to run things?","aiTr":"Hâlâ buraya alışmaya çalışıyorum; işleri nasıl yürütmeyi seviyorsun?","hint":"The one ritual we never skip is the Monday stand-up, where everyone covers what they've delivered, what's next and what's blocking them.","keys":["stand-up","ritual","blocking"]},{"ai":"How specific should I expect tasks to be?","aiTr":"Görevlerin ne kadar net olmasını beklemeliyim?","hint":"Very specific: every task comes with a single owner and a hard deadline, because I've learned the hard way that vague requests produce vague results.","keys":["single owner","hard deadline","vague"]},{"ai":"Honestly, at my last job, mistakes got people into real trouble.","aiTr":"Açıkçası, önceki işimde hatalar insanların başını ciddi derde sokuyordu.","hint":"Here the focus is on fixing the process rather than finding a culprit, so please flag problems early.","keys":["culprit","fixing the process","flag"]},{"ai":"Would you actually want to hear it if I disagreed with how you run meetings?","aiTr":"Toplantıları yönetme biçimine katılmasam bunu gerçekten duymak ister misin?","hint":"Absolutely; one of our engineers pointed out that I tended to dominate meetings, and since then I've made a point of listening more.","keys":["absolutely","dominate","made a point"]}]}},"te-01":{"intro":"Bir sağlık teknolojisi panelinde yapay zekânın gerçek değerini, risklerini ve erişim üzerindeki etkisini nüanslı bir dille tartışıyorsun.","text":[{"en":"Much of the public debate about AI in medicine fixates on whether algorithms will replace doctors, which, to my mind, misses the point.","tr":"Tıpta yapay zekâ üzerine kamusal tartışmanın büyük kısmı algoritmaların doktorların yerini alıp almayacağına takılıp kalıyor; bence bu, asıl meseleyi kaçırmak."},{"en":"Where AI genuinely excels is in high-volume, repetitive work, where fatigue tends to creep in.","tr":"Yapay zekânın gerçekten öne çıktığı yer, yorgunluğun sinsice devreye girdiği yüksek hacimli ve tekrarlı işler."},{"en":"Screening thousands of scans overnight, a well-trained model can flag suspicious findings for a radiologist to prioritize the following morning.","tr":"İyi eğitilmiş bir model, bir gecede binlerce taramayı inceleyerek radyoloğun ertesi sabah öncelik vermesi için şüpheli bulguları işaretleyebilir."},{"en":"Not only does this speed up diagnosis, but it also frees up specialists for the cases that demand their judgment.","tr":"Bu yalnızca teşhisi hızlandırmakla kalmıyor, uzmanları da muhakemelerini gerektiren vakalar için serbest bırakıyor."},{"en":"That said, a model is only ever as good as the data it was trained on.","tr":"Bununla birlikte bir model, her zaman ancak eğitildiği veri kadar iyidir."},{"en":"Should certain patient groups be underrepresented in that data, its performance for them may quietly deteriorate.","tr":"Bazı hasta grupları bu veride yeterince temsil edilmiyorsa, modelin onlar için performansı sessizce kötüleşebilir."},{"en":"It is precisely for this reason that a clinician must remain accountable for the final decision.","tr":"Tam da bu nedenle nihai karardan bir klinisyen sorumlu olmaya devam etmeli."},{"en":"To my mind, though, the real prize lies less in diagnosis than in access.","tr":"Yine de bana göre asıl kazanç teşhisten çok erişimde yatıyor."},{"en":"Roughly one in five people lives with some degree of hearing loss, yet the vast majority are never tested, largely because audiologists are in short supply.","tr":"Yaklaşık her beş kişiden biri bir derece işitme kaybıyla yaşıyor, ancak büyük çoğunluğu hiç test edilmiyor; bunun başlıca nedeni odyologların az olması."},{"en":"In smaller towns, that bottleneck translates into waiting lists that stretch for months.","tr":"Küçük kasabalarda bu darboğaz, aylarca süren bekleme listelerine dönüşüyor."},{"en":"By running the test autonomously, adjusting it in real time and producing an audiogram in under ten minutes, our device takes the specialist out of the routine part of the process.","tr":"Cihazımız testi otonom olarak yürütüp gerçek zamanlı ayarlayarak ve on dakikadan kısa sürede odyogram üreterek, uzmanı sürecin rutin kısmından çıkarıyor."},{"en":"The audiologist's expertise isn't sidelined; it's redeployed where it matters most.","tr":"Odyoloğun uzmanlığı kenara itilmiyor; en çok önem taşıdığı yere yönlendiriliyor."}],"vocab":[{"en":"fixate on","tr":"...e takılıp kalmak","ex":"The debate fixates on whether AI will replace doctors.","def":"to give too much attention to one thing"},{"en":"miss the point","tr":"asıl meseleyi kaçırmak","ex":"Asking whether AI will replace doctors misses the point.","def":"to fail to understand the most important part"},{"en":"excel","tr":"çok başarılı olmak, öne çıkmak","ex":"AI excels at high-volume, repetitive work.","def":"to be extremely good at something"},{"en":"creep in","tr":"sinsice ortaya çıkmak","ex":"After hours of screening, fatigue starts to creep in.","def":"to start to appear gradually, often without being noticed"},{"en":"free up","tr":"serbest bırakmak, zaman açmak","ex":"AI frees up specialists for complex cases.","def":"to make time or people available for something else"},{"en":"underrepresented","tr":"yeterince temsil edilmemiş","ex":"Some patient groups are underrepresented in the data.","def":"present in smaller numbers than they should be"},{"en":"deteriorate","tr":"kötüleşmek","ex":"Performance may deteriorate for some groups.","def":"to become worse"},{"en":"accountable for","tr":"...den sorumlu, hesap verebilir","ex":"A clinician must remain accountable for the final decision.","def":"responsible for something and expected to explain it"},{"en":"in short supply","tr":"kıt, az bulunan","ex":"Audiologists are in short supply in small towns.","def":"not available in large enough amounts"},{"en":"sideline","tr":"kenara itmek","ex":"AI doesn't sideline the audiologist.","def":"to make someone less important or active"}],"grammar":{"title":"Cleft sentences for emphasis","tr":"Cümlenin bir kısmını vurgulamak için 'It is … that …' ya da 'Where/What … is …' yapısı kullanılır. Konuşmacının asıl söylemek istediği şey öne çıkar.","examples":["It is precisely for this reason that a clinician must remain accountable.","Where AI genuinely excels is in high-volume, repetitive work.","What really matters is access."]},"questions":[{"q":"What does the speaker think about the 'AI will replace doctors' debate?","options":["It is the most important question","It misses the point","It has been settled","It only matters in radiology"],"a":1},{"q":"What is the main risk when some patient groups are underrepresented in training data?","options":["The model becomes slower","The model refuses to work","Its performance for those groups may decline without anyone noticing"],"a":2},{"q":"Why must a clinician remain accountable for the final decision?","options":["Because a model's reliability depends on its training data","Because AI is too expensive","Because patients prefer human doctors"],"a":0},{"q":"What does the word 'quietly' in 'may quietly deteriorate' imply?","options":["The decline will be small","The problem is easy to fix","The model will warn the user","The problem may go unnoticed"],"a":3},{"q":"What is the speaker's attitude toward audiologists?","options":["They will soon be unnecessary","Their expertise should be focused where it matters most","They cause the long waiting lists","They oppose AI"],"a":1}],"gaps":[{"s":"Where AI genuinely ___ is in high-volume, repetitive work.","a":"excels","hint":"öne çıkmak"},{"s":"___ certain patient groups be underrepresented, its performance may deteriorate.","a":"Should","hint":"eğer (devrik koşul)"},{"s":"Audiologists are in short ___.","a":"supply","hint":"kıt (in short …)"},{"s":"The audiologist's expertise isn't ___; it's redeployed.","a":"sidelined","hint":"kenara itilmek"}],"order":[{"a":"A model is only as good as its training data."},{"a":"The real prize lies less in diagnosis than in access."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Tam da bu nedenle nihai karardan bir klinisyen sorumlu olmalı.","en":"It is precisely for this reason that a clinician must remain accountable for the final decision.","keys":["precisely for this reason","accountable"]},{"tr":"Bu yalnızca teşhisi hızlandırmakla kalmıyor, uzmanlara da zaman açıyor.","en":"Not only does this speed up diagnosis, but it also frees up specialists.","keys":["not only does","frees up"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Panel moderator","personaTr":"Panel moderatörü","scene":"Bir sağlık teknolojisi konferansında panel moderatörü sana zor sorular soruyor.","turns":[{"ai":"Many clinicians fear AI will make them redundant. Are they right to worry?","aiTr":"Pek çok klinisyen yapay zekânın onları gereksiz kılacağından korkuyor. Endişelenmekte haklılar mı?","hint":"To my mind, that misses the point. AI excels at high-volume, repetitive work, which frees up specialists for the cases that demand their judgment.","keys":["misses the point","frees up","repetitive"]},{"ai":"What about bias? Training data is rarely as diverse as the real world.","aiTr":"Peki önyargı? Eğitim verisi nadiren gerçek dünya kadar çeşitlidir.","hint":"It's a real risk. Should certain groups be underrepresented, performance may quietly deteriorate, which is why a clinician must remain accountable.","keys":["underrepresented","accountable","deteriorate"]},{"ai":"Where do you see the biggest impact over the next few years?","aiTr":"Önümüzdeki birkaç yılda en büyük etkiyi nerede görüyorsunuz?","hint":"Less in diagnosis than in access: one in five people has some hearing loss, yet most are never tested because audiologists are in short supply.","keys":["access","in short supply","one in five"]},{"ai":"And how does your own device fit into that picture?","aiTr":"Peki sizin cihazınız bu tabloya nasıl oturuyor?","hint":"It runs the test autonomously and produces an audiogram in under ten minutes, so the audiologist's expertise is redeployed where it matters most.","keys":["autonomously","audiogram","under ten minutes","redeployed"]}]}},"te-03":{"intro":"Zorlu bir hatanın hikâyesini bir teknoloji etkinliğinde etkileyici bir dille anlatıyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Me","en":"Last week, a handful of clinics flagged something odd: our device was reporting hearing loss at high frequencies in patients who seemed perfectly fine.","tr":"Geçen hafta birkaç klinik tuhaf bir şeye dikkat çekti: cihazımız, gayet sağlıklı görünen hastalarda yüksek frekanslarda işitme kaybı raporluyordu."},{"who":"Me","en":"What made it so puzzling was that identical units were working flawlessly in every other clinic.","tr":"İşi bu kadar kafa karıştırıcı yapan, aynı cihazların diğer tüm kliniklerde kusursuz çalışmasıydı."},{"who":"Me","en":"Our first instinct was to blame the headphones, but swapping them out made no difference whatsoever.","tr":"İlk refleksimiz suçu kulaklıklara atmaktı, ama onları değiştirmek hiçbir fark yaratmadı."},{"who":"Me","en":"Rather than chase another hunch, we pulled the logs from every device and compared the affected clinics with the unaffected ones.","tr":"Bir başka önseziyi kovalamak yerine her cihazın kayıtlarını çektik ve sorun yaşayan klinikleri yaşamayanlarla karşılaştırdık."},{"who":"Me","en":"Only when we lined up the data side by side did the pattern emerge.","tr":"Örüntü ancak verileri yan yana koyduğumuzda ortaya çıktı."},{"who":"Me","en":"Every faulty result had come from a room cooled by an ageing air conditioner.","tr":"Hatalı sonuçların hepsi eski bir klimayla soğutulan odalardan gelmişti."},{"who":"Me","en":"As it turned out, these older units emit a high-pitched whine at precisely the frequencies we test, effectively masking the tones the patient is meant to hear.","tr":"Meğer bu eski klimalar tam da test ettiğimiz frekanslarda tiz bir vızıltı çıkarıyormuş ve hastanın duyması gereken tonları fiilen bastırıyormuş."},{"who":"Me","en":"In other words, the device wasn't failing; it was faithfully recording what the patient could actually hear.","tr":"Yani cihaz arızalı değildi; hastanın gerçekte ne duyabildiğini sadakatle kaydediyordu."},{"who":"Me","en":"The fix itself was almost anticlimactic: a brief ambient-noise check that runs before every test and warns the user if the room is too loud.","tr":"Çözümün kendisi neredeyse hayal kırıklığı yaratacak kadar basitti: her testten önce çalışan ve oda fazla gürültülüyse kullanıcıyı uyaran kısa bir ortam gürültüsü kontrolü."},{"who":"Me","en":"We rolled it out in the next monthly update, and the results have been consistent across all sites ever since.","tr":"Bunu bir sonraki aylık güncellemede kullanıma sunduk ve o günden beri sonuçlar tüm merkezlerde tutarlı."},{"who":"Me","en":"What this episode reinforced for me is that intuition is no substitute for data.","tr":"Bu olayın bana bir kez daha gösterdiği şu: sezgi, verinin yerini tutmaz."}],"vocab":[{"en":"flag something","tr":"bir şeye dikkat çekmek, işaretlemek","ex":"A handful of clinics flagged something odd.","def":"to point out a possible problem"},{"en":"puzzling","tr":"kafa karıştırıcı","ex":"What made it so puzzling was that the other units worked.","def":"difficult to understand or explain"},{"en":"swap something out","tr":"bir şeyi (yenisiyle) değiştirmek","ex":"Swapping out the headphones made no difference.","def":"to replace one part with another"},{"en":"chase a hunch","tr":"bir önsezinin peşinden gitmek","ex":"Rather than chase a hunch, we pulled the logs.","def":"to follow a feeling that has no evidence yet"},{"en":"pull the logs","tr":"kayıtları çekmek","ex":"We pulled the logs from every device.","def":"to download the records a system keeps"},{"en":"emerge","tr":"ortaya çıkmak","ex":"The pattern only emerged when we compared the data.","def":"to become clear or known"},{"en":"high-pitched whine","tr":"tiz vızıltı","ex":"The old units emit a high-pitched whine.","def":"a thin, high, continuous sound"},{"en":"anticlimactic","tr":"beklenenden sönük, sıradan","ex":"The fix itself was almost anticlimactic.","def":"less exciting than you expected"},{"en":"roll something out","tr":"kullanıma sunmak","ex":"We rolled the fix out in the next monthly update.","def":"to release something to all users"},{"en":"no substitute for","tr":"...nin yerini tutmamak","ex":"Intuition is no substitute for data.","def":"not as good as the real thing"}],"grammar":{"title":"Inversion after 'Only when'","tr":"'Only when', 'Only after', 'Not only' gibi ifadeler cümlenin başına gelince yardımcı fiil öznenin önüne geçer (did the pattern emerge). Vurgulu ve etkili bir anlatım için kullanılır.","examples":["Only when we lined up the data side by side did the pattern emerge.","Only after the update did the results become consistent.","Not only did the fix work, but it took just one update."]},"questions":[{"q":"Why was the problem initially so puzzling?","options":["The device had never been tested before","Identical devices worked perfectly in other clinics","The clinics refused to share data"],"a":1},{"q":"What does the speaker imply by saying the device 'wasn't failing'?","options":["It was accurately recording what patients could hear in a noisy room","The clinics had used it incorrectly","The headphones were the real fault"],"a":0},{"q":"How does the speaker seem to feel about the fix?","options":["Proud of how complex it was","Worried it might not last","Slightly amused at how simple it turned out to be"],"a":2},{"q":"What led to the breakthrough?","options":["Comparing data from affected and unaffected clinics","Replacing the headphones","A complaint from a patient"],"a":0},{"q":"What is the speaker's main takeaway?","options":["Hardware should be replaced every year","Intuition is no substitute for data","Clinics should not use air conditioners"],"a":1}],"gaps":[{"s":"Rather than chase another ___, we pulled the logs from every device.","a":"hunch","hint":"önsezi"},{"s":"Only when we lined up the data side by side did the pattern ___.","a":"emerge","hint":"ortaya çıkmak"},{"s":"We ___ it out in the next monthly update.","a":"rolled","hint":"kullanıma sunduk"},{"s":"Intuition is no ___ for data.","a":"substitute","hint":"yerini tutan şey"}],"order":[{"a":"Swapping out the headphones made no difference whatsoever."},{"a":"Intuition is no substitute for looking at the data."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Örüntü ancak verileri karşılaştırdığımızda ortaya çıktı.","en":"Only when we compared the data did the pattern emerge.","keys":["only when","did the pattern emerge"]},{"tr":"Kulaklıkları değiştirmek hiçbir fark yaratmadı.","en":"Swapping out the headphones made no difference.","keys":["swapping out","made no difference"]},{"tr":"Sezgi, verinin yerini tutmaz.","en":"Intuition is no substitute for data.","keys":["no substitute for"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Clinic director","personaTr":"Klinik direktörü","scene":"Sorun yaşayan bir kliniğin direktörü ne olduğunu ve bunun tekrar yaşanmayacağına nasıl güvenebileceğini sorguluyor.","turns":[{"ai":"Frankly, it was unsettling to see hearing loss reported in patients who clearly didn't have it — what exactly went wrong?","aiTr":"Açıkçası, belli ki işitme kaybı olmayan hastalarda işitme kaybı raporlandığını görmek huzursuz ediciydi — tam olarak ne ters gitti?","hint":"I completely understand. As it turned out, older air conditioners emit a high-pitched whine that masked the test tones.","keys":["as it turned out","masked","air conditioners","high-pitched"]},{"ai":"Why didn't your team catch this sooner?","aiTr":"Ekibiniz bunu neden daha önce fark etmedi?","hint":"Our first instinct was to blame the headphones, and only when we compared data from every clinic did the real cause emerge.","keys":["first instinct","only when","emerge","compared"]},{"ai":"What safeguards have you put in place since then?","aiTr":"O zamandan beri ne gibi önlemler aldınız?","hint":"We rolled out an ambient-noise check that runs before every test and warns the user if the room is too loud.","keys":["rolled out","noise check","warns"]},{"ai":"And what would you say your team learned from all this?","aiTr":"Peki sizce ekibiniz tüm bunlardan ne öğrendi?","hint":"What it reinforced for us is that intuition is no substitute for data.","keys":["no substitute","intuition","data"]}]}},"te-04":{"intro":"Bir mimari kararı mühendisinle derinlemesine tartışıp müşterinin bakış açısıyla sonuca bağlıyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Engineer","en":"Before we commit to a hardware spec, we need to settle where the model actually lives: on the device or in the cloud.","tr":"Bir donanım spesifikasyonuna bağlanmadan önce modelin aslında nerede çalışacağını netleştirmemiz gerekiyor: cihazda mı, bulutta mı?"},{"who":"Me","en":"Talk me through the case for the cloud first.","tr":"Önce bulutun lehine olan argümanları bana anlat."},{"who":"Engineer","en":"We'd be able to run a much heavier model, and we could iterate on it daily without touching a single unit in the field.","tr":"Çok daha ağır bir model çalıştırabilir ve sahadaki tek bir cihaza dokunmadan onu her gün geliştirebilirdik."},{"who":"Engineer","en":"The catch is that every test would hinge on a stable connection, which is far from a given in small-town clinics.","tr":"İşin püf noktası şu: her test sabit bir bağlantıya bağlı olurdu ve küçük kasaba kliniklerinde bu hiç de garanti değil."},{"who":"Engineer","en":"More to the point, a number of hospitals flatly refuse to let patient data leave the building, whatever safeguards we put in place.","tr":"Daha da önemlisi, bazı hastaneler, ne tür güvenlik önlemleri alırsak alalım, hasta verisinin binadan çıkmasını kesinlikle reddediyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"And keeping everything on the device?","tr":"Peki her şeyi cihazda tutarsak?"},{"who":"Engineer","en":"Running it locally keeps the data in the room and lets the test work offline, though it does push up the cost of each unit.","tr":"Yerelde çalıştırmak veriyi odada tutar ve testin çevrimdışı çalışmasını sağlar, ama her cihazın maliyetini de artırır."},{"who":"Engineer","en":"We'd also have to slim the model down to fit the hardware, which is doable but not trivial.","tr":"Ayrıca modeli donanıma sığacak şekilde küçültmemiz gerekir; bu yapılabilir ama basit bir iş değil."},{"who":"Me","en":"What strikes me is that privacy comes up in practically every conversation I've had with hospital IT teams.","tr":"Dikkatimi çeken şu: hastane bilgi işlem ekipleriyle yaptığım neredeyse her görüşmede gizlilik konusu açılıyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"Given that, I'd rather absorb a slightly higher hardware cost than hand our customers a reason to say no.","tr":"Bunu göz önünde bulundurursak, müşterilerimize hayır demeleri için bir sebep vermektense biraz daha yüksek bir donanım maliyetini üstlenmeyi tercih ederim."},{"who":"Me","en":"So let's run the model on the device and push updates once a month whenever a unit connects.","tr":"O halde modeli cihazda çalıştıralım ve bir cihaz bağlandığında ayda bir güncelleme gönderelim."},{"who":"Engineer","en":"Agreed — it's a genuine trade-off, but privacy is the one thing we can't afford to get wrong.","tr":"Katılıyorum — bu gerçek bir ödünleşim, ama gizlilik, hata yapmayı göze alamayacağımız tek konu."}],"vocab":[{"en":"commit to something","tr":"bir şeye bağlanmak, karar kılmak","ex":"Before we commit to a hardware spec, let's decide.","def":"to make a firm decision to do or use something"},{"en":"talk someone through something","tr":"birine bir şeyi adım adım anlatmak","ex":"Talk me through the case for the cloud.","def":"to explain something to someone step by step"},{"en":"iterate on","tr":"yinelemeli olarak geliştirmek","ex":"We could iterate on the model daily.","def":"to improve something through repeated small changes"},{"en":"the catch is","tr":"işin püf noktası / sorun şu ki","ex":"The catch is that every test needs a connection.","def":"used to introduce the hidden problem with something that seems good"},{"en":"hinge on","tr":"...ye bağlı olmak","ex":"Every test would hinge on a stable connection.","def":"to depend completely on something"},{"en":"far from a given","tr":"hiç de garanti olmamak","ex":"A stable connection is far from a given in small towns.","def":"not something you can expect or assume"},{"en":"flatly refuse","tr":"kesinlikle reddetmek","ex":"Some hospitals flatly refuse to let data leave the building.","def":"to refuse completely and directly"},{"en":"slim something down","tr":"bir şeyi küçültmek, hafifletmek","ex":"We'd have to slim the model down.","def":"to make something smaller or lighter"},{"en":"absorb a cost","tr":"bir maliyeti üstlenmek","ex":"I'd rather absorb a higher hardware cost.","def":"to pay for an extra cost yourself instead of passing it on"},{"en":"can't afford to get something wrong","tr":"hata yapmayı göze alamamak","ex":"Privacy is the one thing we can't afford to get wrong.","def":"to be too important to risk a mistake"}],"grammar":{"title":"Cleft sentences: What strikes me is…","tr":"'What + özne + fiil + is...' yapısındaki cleft (bölünmüş) cümleler bir bilgiyi öne çıkarıp vurgulamak için kullanılır. Toplantılarda ana noktanızı güçlü biçimde sunmanızı sağlar.","examples":["What strikes me is that privacy comes up in every conversation.","What we need to settle is where the model lives.","What hospitals care about most is privacy."]},"questions":[{"q":"What does the engineer see as the main appeal of the cloud?","options":["A heavier model and the freedom to iterate quickly","Lower hardware costs","Better privacy for hospitals"],"a":0},{"q":"What does 'far from a given' imply about small-town clinics?","options":["They have fast and stable internet","They prefer cloud solutions","Their internet connection can't be relied on"],"a":2},{"q":"What is the speaker's attitude towards the extra hardware cost?","options":["Willing to accept it as the price of customer trust","Strongly opposed to it","Unaware of it"],"a":0},{"q":"Why does the speaker mention conversations with hospital IT teams?","options":["To complain about hospital bureaucracy","To show that privacy is a real and repeated customer concern","To suggest selling to IT companies instead"],"a":1},{"q":"What does the engineer's final remark suggest?","options":["The engineer still prefers the cloud","The engineer wants more time to decide","The engineer accepts the decision despite the costs"],"a":2}],"gaps":[{"s":"Every test would ___ on a stable connection.","a":"hinge","hint":"bağlı olmak"},{"s":"We'd also have to ___ the model down to fit the hardware.","a":"slim","hint":"küçültmek"},{"s":"I'd rather ___ a slightly higher hardware cost.","a":"absorb","hint":"üstlenmek"}],"order":[{"a":"Privacy comes up in practically every conversation."},{"a":"Let's run the model on the device."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Dikkatimi çeken şu: gizlilik her görüşmede gündeme geliyor.","en":"What strikes me is that privacy comes up in every conversation.","keys":["what strikes me","comes up"]},{"tr":"İşin püf noktası şu: her test bir bağlantıya bağlı olurdu.","en":"The catch is that every test would hinge on a connection.","keys":["the catch is","hinge on"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Hospital IT director","personaTr":"Hastane bilgi işlem direktörü","scene":"Büyük bir hastanenin bilgi işlem direktörü mimari kararlarınızı sorguluyor; ikna edici ve net olmalısın.","turns":[{"ai":"Our data protection officer will want to know exactly where patient data ends up — what should I tell them?","aiTr":"Veri koruma sorumlumuz hasta verisinin tam olarak nereye gittiğini bilmek isteyecek — ona ne söylemeliyim?","hint":"You can tell them it never leaves the room, because the model runs entirely on the device.","keys":["never leaves","on the device","entirely"]},{"ai":"Wouldn't a cloud model be more accurate, though?","aiTr":"Ama bulut modeli daha doğru olmaz mıydı?","hint":"We could run a heavier model in the cloud, but we'd rather slim it down than ask you to send patient data off-site.","keys":["slim it down","heavier model","off-site"]},{"ai":"Some of our satellite clinics have patchy internet — is that going to be an issue?","aiTr":"Bazı bağlı kliniklerimizin interneti kesik kesik — bu sorun olur mu?","hint":"Not at all; since the test works offline, it doesn't hinge on a stable connection.","keys":["works offline","hinge on","not at all"]},{"ai":"Then how do you keep the model from going stale?","aiTr":"O zaman modelin eskimesini nasıl önlüyorsunuz?","hint":"We push an update once a month whenever a unit connects, so it stays current without any effort on your side.","keys":["once a month","push an update","connects"]}]}},"sc-01":{"intro":"Çalışmanın tasarımını bilimsel bir üslupla, vurgulu yapılar ve kesin terimlerle sunuyorsun.","text":[{"en":"Certification hinged on a single question: could our device deliver the same results as a trained audiologist?","tr":"Sertifikasyon tek bir soruya bağlıydı: cihazımız eğitimli bir odyologla aynı sonuçları verebilir miydi?"},{"en":"To answer it rigorously, we partnered with two university hospitals to design a clinical study.","tr":"Bu soruyu titizlikle yanıtlamak için iki üniversite hastanesiyle ortaklık kurup bir klinik çalışma tasarladık."},{"en":"Our hypothesis was that the autonomous test and the expert assessment would agree in at least 90 percent of cases.","tr":"Hipotezimiz, otonom test ile uzman değerlendirmesinin vakaların en az yüzde 90'ında uyuşacağıydı."},{"en":"We recruited 200 participants aged 18 to 75, deliberately spanning a wide age range.","tr":"Bilinçli olarak geniş bir yaş aralığını kapsayacak şekilde 18-75 yaş arası 200 katılımcı topladık."},{"en":"Each participant underwent two tests on the same day, one administered by our device and the other by an audiologist.","tr":"Her katılımcı aynı gün iki testten geçti: birini cihazımız, diğerini bir odyolog uyguladı."},{"en":"Crucially, the audiologist was blinded to the device's output, which ruled out any risk of confirmation bias.","tr":"En önemlisi, odyolog cihazın çıktısını bilmiyordu; bu da her türlü doğrulama yanlılığı riskini ortadan kaldırdı."},{"en":"Not only did the results match in 94 percent of cases, but they also comfortably exceeded our pre-defined threshold.","tr":"Sonuçlar vakaların yüzde 94'ünde eşleşmekle kalmadı, önceden belirlediğimiz eşiği de rahatça aştı."},{"en":"Where discrepancies did occur, they were marginal and in no instance altered the diagnosis.","tr":"Tutarsızlık görülen yerlerde farklar çok küçüktü ve hiçbir vakada teşhisi değiştirmedi."},{"en":"What gave the findings real weight, though, was their publication in a medical journal last spring.","tr":"Yine de bulgulara asıl ağırlık kazandıran, geçen bahar bir tıp dergisinde yayımlanmalarıydı."},{"en":"Having passed independent scrutiny, the study now forms the backbone of our certification file.","tr":"Bağımsız bir incelemeden geçen çalışma, artık sertifikasyon dosyamızın bel kemiğini oluşturuyor."}],"vocab":[{"en":"hinge on","tr":"...e bağlı olmak","ex":"Certification hinged on a single question.","def":"to depend completely on something"},{"en":"rigorously","tr":"titizlikle","ex":"We wanted to answer the question rigorously.","def":"carefully and thoroughly, following strict rules"},{"en":"undergo a test","tr":"bir testten geçmek","ex":"Each participant underwent two tests on the same day.","def":"to have a medical test or procedure done to you"},{"en":"administer a test","tr":"bir test uygulamak","ex":"One test was administered by our device.","def":"to give or carry out a test"},{"en":"be blinded to","tr":"...den habersiz tutulmak","ex":"The audiologist was blinded to the device's output.","def":"in research, to be kept from knowing information that could affect your judgement"},{"en":"rule out","tr":"olasılığını ortadan kaldırmak","ex":"Blinding ruled out the risk of bias.","def":"to remove the possibility of something"},{"en":"confirmation bias","tr":"doğrulama yanlılığı","ex":"Blinding protects against confirmation bias.","def":"the tendency to see what you already expect to see"},{"en":"pre-defined threshold","tr":"önceden belirlenmiş eşik","ex":"The results exceeded our pre-defined threshold of 90 percent.","def":"a minimum level of success decided before a study starts"},{"en":"discrepancy","tr":"tutarsızlık, uyuşmazlık","ex":"The discrepancies were marginal.","def":"a difference between two things that should be the same"},{"en":"form the backbone of","tr":"...in bel kemiğini oluşturmak","ex":"The study forms the backbone of our certification file.","def":"to be the most important part that supports something"}],"grammar":{"title":"Cleft sentences: What... was...","tr":"Cleft (bölünmüş) cümleler bir bilgiyi öne çıkarmak için kullanılır: 'What ... was ...' ya da 'It was ... that ...'. Bilimsel sunumlarda en önemli noktayı zarifçe vurgulamanı sağlar.","examples":["What gave the findings real weight was their publication in a medical journal.","What we needed to prove was that the device matches an audiologist.","It was the blind design that made the comparison credible."]},"questions":[{"q":"What did certification depend on?","options":["Whether the device could match a trained audiologist","Whether the device was cheaper","Whether hospitals would buy it"],"a":0},{"q":"Why was the audiologist blinded to the device's output?","options":["To speed up the testing","To protect patient privacy","To rule out confirmation bias"],"a":2},{"q":"What does \"comfortably exceeded our pre-defined threshold\" imply?","options":["The team lowered its target","The result was well above the 90 percent target","The result was barely acceptable"],"a":1},{"q":"What does the writer suggest gave the findings credibility?","options":["The size of the team","Positive customer reviews","Support from investors","Publication in a medical journal"],"a":3},{"q":"What is the overall tone of the text?","options":["Measured and confident","Anxious and defensive","Casual and humorous"],"a":0}],"gaps":[{"s":"Certification ___ on a single question.","a":"hinged","hint":"bağlıydı"},{"s":"The audiologist was ___ to the device's output.","a":"blinded","hint":"habersiz tutuldu"},{"s":"The discrepancies were ___ and in no instance altered the diagnosis.","a":"marginal","hint":"çok küçük"},{"s":"The study now forms the ___ of our certification file.","a":"backbone","hint":"bel kemiği"}],"order":[{"a":"Each participant underwent two tests on the same day."},{"a":"The study now forms the backbone of our certification file."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Odyolog cihazın çıktısından habersiz tutuldu.","en":"The audiologist was blinded to the device's output.","keys":["blinded to","output"]},{"tr":"Farklar hiçbir vakada teşhisi değiştirmedi.","en":"In no instance did the differences alter the diagnosis.","keys":["in no instance","diagnosis"]},{"tr":"Bulgulara asıl ağırlık kazandıran şey yayımlanmalarıydı.","en":"What gave the findings real weight was their publication.","keys":["real weight","publication"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Professor of audiology","personaTr":"Odyoloji profesörü","scene":"Bir konferansta bir profesör çalışmanızın yöntemini ve sınırlılıklarını sorguluyor.","turns":[{"ai":"Your paper caught my eye. What exactly were you setting out to demonstrate?","aiTr":"Makaleniz dikkatimi çekti. Tam olarak neyi göstermeyi amaçlıyordunuz?","hint":"We set out to show that our autonomous test agrees with a trained audiologist in at least 90 percent of cases.","keys":["set out to","at least 90 percent","agrees"]},{"ai":"How did you guard against bias in the expert assessments?","aiTr":"Uzman değerlendirmelerinde yanlılığa karşı nasıl önlem aldınız?","hint":"The audiologists were blinded to the device's output, which ruled out confirmation bias.","keys":["blinded","ruled out","bias"]},{"ai":"Ninety-four percent is impressive, but what about the cases that didn't match?","aiTr":"Yüzde doksan dört etkileyici, ama eşleşmeyen vakalar ne olacak?","hint":"Where discrepancies occurred, they were marginal and never altered the diagnosis.","keys":["discrepancies","marginal","diagnosis"]},{"ai":"What would you say are the study's main limitations?","aiTr":"Sizce çalışmanın başlıca sınırlılıkları neler?","hint":"One limitation is that our sample only covered adults aged 18 to 75, so we can't yet generalise to children or older patients.","keys":["limitation","18 to 75","generalise"]}]}},"te-02":{"intro":"Teknik durum tespiti yapan bir uzmana, yapay zekâ destekli geliştirme sürecinizi mühendislik diliyle ve ayrıntılı olarak anlatıyorsun.","text":[{"en":"Two years ago, every line of our codebase was written by hand; today, AI coding assistants produce a substantial share of our first drafts.","tr":"İki yıl önce kod tabanımızın her satırı elle yazılıyordu; bugün ilk taslaklarımızın önemli bir kısmını yapay zekâ kod asistanları üretiyor."},{"en":"Our engineers now spend less time typing and more time specifying, reviewing and testing.","tr":"Mühendislerimiz artık daha az yazıyor, daha çok tanımlama, inceleme ve test yapıyor."},{"en":"Describing a feature in plain English, an engineer can get a working first pass within minutes rather than hours.","tr":"Bir mühendis bir özelliği sade İngilizceyle anlatarak, saatler yerine dakikalar içinde çalışan bir ilk taslak elde edebiliyor."},{"en":"The assistants are also remarkably good at explaining legacy code and surfacing bugs that would otherwise slip through.","tr":"Asistanlar ayrıca eski kodu açıklamakta ve aksi halde gözden kaçacak hataları ortaya çıkarmakta dikkat çekici derecede iyi."},{"en":"The upshot is that tasks which used to take a week routinely ship in a day or two.","tr":"Sonuç olarak eskiden bir hafta süren işler artık rutin olarak bir iki günde yayına çıkıyor."},{"en":"What makes AI-generated code dangerous, however, is precisely that it looks plausible.","tr":"Ancak yapay zekânın ürettiği kodu tehlikeli kılan şey, tam da akla yatkın görünmesi."},{"en":"It compiles, it survives a cursory glance, and it can still harbor a subtle logic error that only surfaces in production.","tr":"Derleniyor, üstünkörü bir bakıştan geçiyor ve yine de ancak canlı ortamda ortaya çıkan ince bir mantık hatası barındırabiliyor."},{"en":"Given that our software runs on a regulated medical device, that's a risk we simply can't afford to take.","tr":"Yazılımımızın mevzuata tabi bir tıbbi cihazda çalıştığı düşünülürse, bu bizim kesinlikle göze alamayacağımız bir risk."},{"en":"Every change therefore goes through human code review and an automated test suite, and it's documented so that it remains traceable.","tr":"Bu nedenle her değişiklik insan kod incelemesinden ve otomatik bir test paketinden geçiyor, ayrıca izlenebilir kalması için belgeleniyor."},{"en":"Rarely does a week go by without a reviewer catching something the assistant got confidently wrong.","tr":"İncelemeyi yapan birinin, asistanın kendinden emin bir şekilde yanlış yaptığı bir şeyi yakalamadığı hafta nadiren geçiyor."},{"en":"Used with that discipline, the tools are a genuine force multiplier for a team of only three engineers.","tr":"Bu disiplinle kullanıldığında araçlar, yalnızca üç mühendislik bir ekip için gerçek bir güç çarpanı."},{"en":"In effect, they give us the output of three extra engineers without the payroll.","tr":"Aslında bize maaş bordrosu olmadan üç ekstra mühendisin üretimini sağlıyorlar."}],"vocab":[{"en":"codebase","tr":"kod tabanı","ex":"Our codebase has grown quickly this year.","def":"all the source code of a software product"},{"en":"first pass","tr":"ilk deneme, ilk taslak","ex":"The assistant gives us a working first pass in minutes.","def":"a first attempt that will be improved later"},{"en":"legacy code","tr":"eski (miras) kod","ex":"It's good at explaining legacy code.","def":"old code that is still used but hard to understand or change"},{"en":"slip through","tr":"gözden kaçmak","ex":"Some bugs slip through even careful reviews.","def":"to get past checks without being noticed"},{"en":"ship","tr":"yayına almak, teslim etmek","ex":"Most features now ship in a day or two.","def":"to release a product or feature to users"},{"en":"plausible","tr":"akla yatkın, inandırıcı","ex":"AI-generated code often looks plausible.","def":"seeming reasonable or likely to be true"},{"en":"cursory","tr":"üstünkörü","ex":"A cursory glance is not enough.","def":"quick and not thorough"},{"en":"harbor","tr":"barındırmak","ex":"The code can harbor a subtle logic error.","def":"to contain something hidden, usually something bad"},{"en":"test suite","tr":"test paketi","ex":"Every change runs through our test suite.","def":"a collection of automated tests that are run together"},{"en":"force multiplier","tr":"güç çarpanı","ex":"AI tools are a force multiplier for small teams.","def":"something that greatly increases what a team can achieve"}],"grammar":{"title":"Participle clauses","tr":"'-ing' ya da V3 ile başlayan yan cümleler, iki cümleyi kısa ve resmî biçimde birleştirir: 'Describing a feature…' (anlatarak), 'Used with that discipline…' (kullanıldığında), 'Given that…' (düşünülürse).","examples":["Describing a feature in plain English, an engineer can get a working first pass within minutes.","Used with that discipline, the tools are a genuine force multiplier.","Given that our software runs on a medical device, that's a risk we can't take."]},"questions":[{"q":"How has the engineers' work changed?","options":["They type more code than before","They spend more time specifying, reviewing and testing","They no longer test code","They only fix legacy code"],"a":1},{"q":"According to the speaker, what makes AI-generated code dangerous?","options":["It is slow to write","It rarely compiles","It looks plausible even when it is wrong"],"a":2},{"q":"What does 'Rarely does a week go by without a reviewer catching something' imply?","options":["Reviews regularly catch AI mistakes","Reviews are rarely necessary","The assistant almost never makes mistakes"],"a":0},{"q":"What is the speaker's attitude toward AI coding assistants?","options":["Uncritical enthusiasm","Total distrust","Indifference","Enthusiastic but disciplined"],"a":3},{"q":"Why does every change need to be documented?","options":["To impress investors","So that it remains traceable on a regulated device","Because the assistants require it"],"a":1}],"gaps":[{"s":"AI coding assistants produce a substantial ___ of our first drafts.","a":"share","hint":"pay, kısım"},{"s":"___ a feature in plain English, an engineer can get a working first pass within minutes.","a":"Describing","hint":"anlatarak"},{"s":"It can still ___ a subtle logic error that only surfaces in production.","a":"harbor","hint":"barındırmak"},{"s":"___ with that discipline, the tools are a genuine force multiplier.","a":"Used","hint":"kullanıldığında"}],"order":[{"a":"Every change goes through human code review."},{"a":"That's a risk we simply can't afford to take."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Eskiden bir hafta süren işler artık rutin olarak bir iki günde yayına çıkıyor.","en":"Tasks that used to take a week routinely ship in a day or two.","keys":["used to take a week","ship"]},{"tr":"Yapay zekânın ürettiği kodu tehlikeli kılan şey, tam da akla yatkın görünmesi.","en":"What makes AI-generated code dangerous is precisely that it looks plausible.","keys":["what makes","looks plausible"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Technical due diligence lead","personaTr":"Teknik durum tespiti sorumlusu","scene":"Bir yatırım fonunun teknik danışmanı geliştirme sürecinizi ayrıntılı biçimde sorguluyor.","turns":[{"ai":"How much of your codebase is actually written by AI these days?","aiTr":"Bugünlerde kod tabanınızın ne kadarı gerçekten yapay zekâ tarafından yazılıyor?","hint":"A substantial share of our first drafts, but our engineers spend their time specifying, reviewing and testing every change.","keys":["first drafts","reviewing","substantial share"]},{"ai":"AI-generated code can look perfectly fine and still be wrong. How do you guard against that?","aiTr":"Yapay zekânın ürettiği kod gayet iyi görünüp yine de yanlış olabilir. Buna karşı nasıl önlem alıyorsunuz?","hint":"Every change goes through human code review and an automated test suite, and it's documented so that it remains traceable.","keys":["code review","test suite","traceable"]},{"ai":"Does the review process actually catch things, or is it a formality?","aiTr":"İnceleme süreci gerçekten bir şeyler yakalıyor mu, yoksa sadece formalite mi?","hint":"It genuinely catches things. Rarely does a week go by without a reviewer spotting something the assistant got confidently wrong.","keys":["rarely does a week","confidently wrong","catches"]},{"ai":"Bottom line: what does this mean for your burn rate?","aiTr":"Kısacası, bu sizin nakit yakma hızınız için ne anlama geliyor?","hint":"Used with that discipline, the tools give us the output of three extra engineers without the payroll.","keys":["three extra engineers","without the payroll","output"]}]}},"sc-02":{"intro":"Hibe sürecini ve hibenin stratejik değerini ileri düzey yapılarla, ikna edici bir dille anlatıyorsun.","text":[{"en":"Investors tend to dominate the conversation about startup funding, yet grants can be just as decisive in the early stages.","tr":"Girişim finansmanı konuşulurken yatırımcılar genelde öne çıkar, oysa hibeler de erken aşamada aynı derecede belirleyici olabilir."},{"en":"What makes them so attractive is that the money doesn't have to be repaid and no equity changes hands.","tr":"Onları bu kadar cazip kılan, paranın geri ödenmek zorunda olmaması ve hiçbir hissenin el değiştirmemesidir."},{"en":"Last year, we applied for a European innovation grant earmarked for health technology.","tr":"Geçen yıl sağlık teknolojisine ayrılmış bir Avrupa inovasyon hibesine başvurduk."},{"en":"The application was exhaustive, requiring us to set out the problem, our solution, the team and a fully costed budget.","tr":"Başvuru son derece kapsamlıydı; sorunu, çözümümüzü, ekibi ve tüm kalemleri hesaplanmış bir bütçeyi ortaya koymamızı gerektiriyordu."},{"en":"Above all, we had to make a compelling case for impact, quantifying how many people stood to benefit from our device.","tr":"Her şeyden önce etki konusunda ikna edici bir gerekçe sunmamız ve cihazımızdan kaç kişinin fayda görebileceğini sayılarla göstermemiz gerekiyordu."},{"en":"With roughly one in five people affected by some degree of hearing loss, that part of the argument largely made itself.","tr":"Yaklaşık her beş kişiden biri bir derece işitme kaybı yaşadığı için argümanın o kısmı büyük ölçüde kendiliğinden ortaya çıktı."},{"en":"Only after a four-month review were we invited to defend the proposal in front of a jury.","tr":"Ancak dört aylık bir değerlendirmeden sonra teklifimizi bir jüri önünde savunmaya davet edildik."},{"en":"We came away with 250,000 euros, ring-fenced for research and clinical validation.","tr":"Yalnızca araştırma ve klinik doğrulama için ayrılmış 250.000 euroyla ayrıldık."},{"en":"Had we relied solely on investors, we would have had to give away considerably more equity at a far lower valuation.","tr":"Yalnızca yatırımcılara dayansaydık, çok daha düşük bir değerlemeyle çok daha fazla hisse vermek zorunda kalırdık."},{"en":"Grants are undeniably a slog, but for de-risking early research, there are few better instruments.","tr":"Hibeler inkâr edilemez biçimde meşakkatlidir, ama erken araştırmanın riskini azaltmak için bundan iyi araç azdır."}],"vocab":[{"en":"earmarked for","tr":"...e ayrılmış","ex":"The grant was earmarked for health technology.","def":"officially kept for a particular purpose"},{"en":"change hands","tr":"el değiştirmek","ex":"With a grant, no equity changes hands.","def":"to pass from one owner to another"},{"en":"exhaustive","tr":"son derece kapsamlı","ex":"The application was exhaustive.","def":"very thorough and complete, covering every detail"},{"en":"set out","tr":"ortaya koymak, açıkça anlatmak","ex":"We had to set out the problem and our solution.","def":"to explain something clearly and in an organised way"},{"en":"fully costed budget","tr":"tüm kalemleri hesaplanmış bütçe","ex":"The jury expects a fully costed budget.","def":"a budget in which every cost has been calculated"},{"en":"make a compelling case","tr":"ikna edici bir gerekçe sunmak","ex":"We had to make a compelling case for impact.","def":"to give strong, convincing reasons for something"},{"en":"stand to benefit","tr":"fayda görecek konumda olmak","ex":"Millions of people stand to benefit from the device.","def":"to be likely to gain something"},{"en":"ring-fenced","tr":"yalnızca belirli bir amaca ayrılmış","ex":"The money is ring-fenced for clinical validation.","def":"kept for one purpose and not allowed to be spent on anything else"},{"en":"a slog","tr":"meşakkatli, uzun uğraş","ex":"Writing the application was a real slog.","def":"a long, tiring piece of work"},{"en":"de-risk","tr":"riskini azaltmak","ex":"Grants help de-risk early research.","def":"to make something less risky, especially for investors"}],"grammar":{"title":"Inversion: Only after... / Had we...","tr":"Resmi İngilizcede bazı ifadelerden sonra özne ile yardımcı fiil yer değiştirir: 'Only after ... were we invited'. 'If' atılarak 'Had we relied...' denince de üçüncü tip koşul daha resmi ve vurgulu olur.","examples":["Only after a four-month review were we invited to meet the jury.","Had we relied solely on investors, we would have given away more equity.","Only then did we realise how demanding the process was."]},"questions":[{"q":"According to the writer, what makes grants so attractive?","options":["They are quick to obtain","The money isn't repaid and no equity changes hands","They come with a board seat"],"a":1},{"q":"Why did the impact section \"largely make itself\"?","options":["The jury already knew the company","The budget was unusually small","Hearing loss affects roughly one in five people"],"a":2},{"q":"What does \"Only after a four-month review were we invited\" emphasise?","options":["The wait before the interview was long","The interview came quickly","The review was optional"],"a":0},{"q":"What does the writer imply about relying only on investors?","options":["It would have been quicker and cheaper","Investors would have refused","It would have been impossible","It would have diluted the founders far more"],"a":3},{"q":"What is the writer's overall attitude towards grants?","options":["Entirely negative","Positive but realistic about the effort","Indifferent"],"a":1}],"gaps":[{"s":"The money is ___ for research and clinical validation.","a":"ring-fenced","hint":"yalnızca bu amaca ayrılmış"},{"s":"We had to make a ___ case for impact.","a":"compelling","hint":"ikna edici"},{"s":"___ we relied solely on investors, we would have given away more equity.","a":"Had","hint":"-seydik (if yerine)"},{"s":"Grants are undeniably a ___.","a":"slog","hint":"meşakkatli iş"}],"order":[{"a":"Grants can be just as decisive in the early stages."},{"a":"We were invited to defend the proposal in front of a jury."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Para geri ödenmek zorunda değil ve hiçbir hisse el değiştirmiyor.","en":"The money doesn't have to be repaid and no equity changes hands.","keys":["repaid","changes hands"]},{"tr":"Ancak dört aylık bir değerlendirmeden sonra jüriye davet edildik.","en":"Only after a four-month review were we invited to meet the jury.","keys":["only after","were we invited"]},{"tr":"Bu tutar yalnızca araştırma ve klinik doğrulamaya ayrılmış.","en":"The amount is ring-fenced for research and clinical validation.","keys":["ring-fenced","clinical validation"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Grant jury member","personaTr":"Hibe jürisi üyesi","scene":"Teklifini deneyimli bir jüri önünde savunuyorsun. Sorular zorlayıcı, cevapların net ve ikna edici olmalı.","turns":[{"ai":"Let's start with the big picture: why should public money go into a hearing test?","aiTr":"Büyük resimle başlayalım: neden kamu parası bir işitme testine gitsin?","hint":"Because roughly one in five people has some hearing loss, yet most are never tested simply because there aren't enough audiologists.","keys":["one in five","never tested","audiologists"]},{"ai":"Your budget is ambitious. Walk us through where the money would go.","aiTr":"Bütçeniz iddialı. Paranın nereye gideceğini adım adım anlatın.","hint":"The bulk of it would go into research and clinical validation, which is precisely what stands between us and certification.","keys":["bulk","clinical validation","certification"]},{"ai":"What's to stop you raising this from investors instead?","aiTr":"Bunu yatırımcılardan toplamanıza ne engel?","hint":"Nothing, in principle, but had we gone down that route, we'd have given away far more equity before the technology was de-risked.","keys":["had we","equity","de-risked"]},{"ai":"Finally, what makes your team credible?","aiTr":"Son olarak, ekibinizi güvenilir kılan ne?","hint":"What sets us apart is the mix: three engineers, a doctor and two business people, plus a working prototype already in its third version.","keys":["sets us apart","prototype","third version"]}]}},"ai-04":{"intro":"Bir risk sermayesi ortağına AB mevzuatını, klinik kanıtları ve takvim riskini profesyonel bir dille anlatıyorsun.","text":[{"en":"Under the EU's Medical Device Regulation, nothing reaches patients without a CE mark, and our audiometer is no exception.","tr":"AB Tıbbi Cihaz Tüzüğü'ne göre hiçbir şey CE işareti olmadan hastaya ulaşamaz ve odyometremiz de bir istisna değil."},{"en":"Classified as Class IIa, it falls into the medium-risk category, which means a notified body must audit both the device and the company behind it.","tr":"Sınıf IIa olarak sınıflandırıldığı için orta risk kategorisine giriyor; bu da onaylanmış bir kuruluşun hem cihazı hem de arkasındaki şirketi denetlemesi gerektiği anlamına geliyor."},{"en":"What the notified body really scrutinizes is our clinical evidence: does the device do what we claim, safely and consistently?","tr":"Onaylanmış kuruluşun asıl titizlikle incelediği şey klinik kanıtlarımız: Cihaz iddia ettiğimiz şeyi güvenli ve tutarlı biçimde yapıyor mu?"},{"en":"Our blind study across two university hospitals, involving 200 participants aged 18 to 75, matched a trained audiologist's results in 94% of cases.","tr":"İki üniversite hastanesinde, 18-75 yaş arası 200 katılımcıyla yürüttüğümüz kör çalışmada sonuçlarımız vakaların %94'ünde eğitimli bir odyoloğunkilerle eşleşti."},{"en":"Crucially, the remaining 6% showed only minor discrepancies, none of which altered the diagnosis.","tr":"Daha da önemlisi, kalan %6'da yalnızca küçük farklar vardı ve hiçbiri teşhisi değiştirmedi."},{"en":"Having published those findings in a medical journal last spring, we now have independent backing for our core claims.","tr":"Bu bulguları geçen bahar bir tıp dergisinde yayımladığımız için artık temel iddialarımızı destekleyen bağımsız bir dayanağımız var."},{"en":"Not only do we need solid clinical data, but we also have to demonstrate a robust quality management system and maintain exhaustive technical documentation.","tr":"Sadece sağlam klinik verilere ihtiyacımız yok; aynı zamanda güçlü bir kalite yönetim sistemi gösterip kapsamlı teknik dokümantasyon da tutmamız gerekiyor."},{"en":"Since our software is updated roughly once a month, every change has to be validated and traceable, which adds a layer of complexity most investors underestimate.","tr":"Yazılımımız yaklaşık ayda bir güncellendiği için her değişikliğin doğrulanmış ve izlenebilir olması gerekiyor; bu da çoğu yatırımcının hafife aldığı bir karmaşıklık katmanı ekliyor."},{"en":"We've brought in a seasoned regulatory consultant to help us navigate the process and avoid the usual pitfalls.","tr":"Süreçte yolumuzu bulmamıza ve bilinen tuzaklardan kaçınmamıza yardım etmesi için deneyimli bir mevzuat danışmanıyla çalışmaya başladık."},{"en":"The real bottleneck, though, is notified body capacity, so timelines can slip through no fault of our own.","tr":"Asıl darboğaz ise onaylanmış kuruluşların kapasitesi; bu yüzden takvimler bizim hiçbir hatamız olmadan kayabiliyor."},{"en":"We're targeting certification by the end of next year, and we've built some slack into the plan to mitigate that risk.","tr":"Sertifikasyonu gelecek yılın sonuna kadar almayı hedefliyoruz ve bu riski azaltmak için plana biraz pay bıraktık."},{"en":"Painful as the process is, it's ultimately what protects patients, and it's a moat that latecomers will find hard to cross.","tr":"Süreç ne kadar zahmetli olsa da sonuçta hastaları koruyan şey bu ve geç gelen rakiplerin aşmakta zorlanacağı bir savunma hattı."}],"vocab":[{"en":"fall into a category","tr":"bir kategoriye girmek","ex":"Our audiometer falls into the medium-risk category.","def":"to belong to a particular group"},{"en":"scrutinize","tr":"titizlikle incelemek","ex":"The notified body will scrutinize our clinical evidence.","def":"to examine something very carefully"},{"en":"discrepancy","tr":"tutarsızlık, fark","ex":"The remaining 6% showed only minor discrepancies.","def":"a difference between things that should be the same"},{"en":"robust","tr":"sağlam, güçlü","ex":"We need a robust quality management system.","def":"strong and unlikely to fail"},{"en":"traceable","tr":"izlenebilir","ex":"Every software change must be traceable.","def":"having a clear record that shows where something came from and what was done"},{"en":"seasoned","tr":"deneyimli","ex":"We hired a seasoned regulatory consultant.","def":"having a lot of experience"},{"en":"navigate the process","tr":"süreçte yolunu bulmak","ex":"Our consultant helps us navigate the process.","def":"to find your way through a complicated system"},{"en":"bottleneck","tr":"darboğaz","ex":"Notified body capacity is the real bottleneck.","def":"a point where progress slows down because of limited capacity"},{"en":"slip","tr":"kaymak, gecikmek","ex":"Timelines can slip for reasons we can't control.","def":"(of a deadline or schedule) to be delayed"},{"en":"mitigate a risk","tr":"bir riski azaltmak","ex":"We've built slack into the plan to mitigate that risk.","def":"to make a risk less likely or less serious"}],"grammar":{"title":"Inversion after 'Not only'","tr":"'Not only' cümlenin başına gelince soru düzeni kullanılır (yardımcı fiil + özne). İkinci kısım genellikle 'but … also' ile gelir. Resmî ve vurgulu bir üsluptur.","examples":["Not only do we need solid clinical data, but we also have to demonstrate a robust quality system.","Not only does the device save time, but it also reduces costs.","Rarely does a certification process run exactly to plan."]},"questions":[{"q":"Why must a notified body be involved?","options":["Because the device will be sold in the US","Because the device is classified as Class IIa","Because the company is based outside the EU","Because the study was blind"],"a":1},{"q":"What point is the speaker making about the remaining 6% of cases?","options":["They reveal a serious flaw","They were excluded from the study","They had no clinical significance","They need to be retested"],"a":2},{"q":"What does the speaker imply most investors underestimate?","options":["The complexity of validating frequent software updates","The cost of the hardware","The size of the market"],"a":0},{"q":"How does the speaker feel about possible delays?","options":["Unconcerned, because the consultant guarantees the date","Resigned, because nothing can be done","Angry at the notified body","Realistic, and has planned for them"],"a":3},{"q":"What does the speaker mean by calling certification 'a moat'?","options":["It is a legal trap","It protects the company from new competitors","It slows the company down for no reason"],"a":1}],"gaps":[{"s":"Every software change has to be validated and ___.","a":"traceable","hint":"izlenebilir"},{"s":"The real ___ is notified body capacity.","a":"bottleneck","hint":"darboğaz"},{"s":"We've built some slack into the plan to ___ that risk.","a":"mitigate","hint":"azaltmak"},{"s":"___ only do we need solid clinical data, but we also need a robust quality system.","a":"Not","hint":"sadece … değil (devrik yapı)"}],"order":[{"a":"The remaining 6% showed only minor discrepancies."},{"a":"We have brought in a seasoned regulatory consultant."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Onaylanmış kuruluşun asıl titizlikle incelediği şey klinik kanıtlarımız.","en":"What the notified body really scrutinizes is our clinical evidence.","keys":["scrutinizes","clinical evidence"]},{"tr":"Takvimler bizim hiçbir hatamız olmadan kayabilir.","en":"Timelines can slip through no fault of our own.","keys":["slip","no fault of our own"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"VC partner","personaTr":"Risk sermayesi fonu ortağı","scene":"Bir yatırım fonunun ortağı, yatırım öncesi incelemede sertifikasyon riskini ayrıntılı biçimde sorguluyor.","turns":[{"ai":"Walk me through what stands between you and the European market.","aiTr":"Sizinle Avrupa pazarı arasında ne olduğunu adım adım anlatın.","hint":"Essentially, the CE mark. Being Class IIa, the device has to be audited by a notified body, which will scrutinize our clinical evidence and our quality system.","keys":["notified body","Class IIa","CE mark","clinical evidence"]},{"ai":"How confident are you that your clinical data will hold up under scrutiny?","aiTr":"Klinik verilerinizin bu incelemeye dayanacağından ne kadar eminsiniz?","hint":"Fairly confident. Our blind study across two university hospitals matched a trained audiologist in 94% of cases, and it was published in a medical journal last spring.","keys":["94","blind","published","two university hospitals"]},{"ai":"Monthly software updates sound like a regulatory headache. How do you handle that?","aiTr":"Aylık yazılım güncellemeleri mevzuat açısından baş ağrısı gibi duruyor. Bunu nasıl yönetiyorsunuz?","hint":"It does add complexity, admittedly. Every change is validated and fully traceable within our quality management system.","keys":["validated","traceable","quality management"]},{"ai":"And if the timeline slips, what's your plan B?","aiTr":"Peki takvim kayarsa B planınız ne?","hint":"We've built some slack into the plan, and our consultant helps us avoid the usual pitfalls, so we can mitigate that risk.","keys":["slack","mitigate","pitfalls"]}]}},"st-03":{"intro":"Şirketin geleceğini etkileyen bir kararı, ödünleşimleri ve kendi bakış açını net ve olgun bir dille anlatıyorsun.","text":[{"en":"Last month, we faced what was probably the most consequential decision since we founded AIHEAR.","tr":"Geçen ay, AIHEAR'ı kurduğumuzdan beri muhtemelen sonuçları en büyük olan kararla yüz yüze geldik."},{"en":"On the table were two options: build our own sales operation and sell directly to hospitals, or partner with a distributor who already knew the market.","tr":"Masada iki seçenek vardı: kendi satış yapımızı kurup doğrudan hastanelere satmak ya da pazarı zaten bilen bir distribütörle ortaklık kurmak."},{"en":"Going direct was undeniably attractive, since we'd keep the full margin and stay close to our customers.","tr":"Doğrudan satış inkâr edilemez biçimde cazipti, çünkü kâr marjının tamamı bizde kalacak ve müşterilerimize yakın olacaktık."},{"en":"The catch was that it would have taken us months, if not years, to build the relationships a distributor already has.","tr":"İşin kötü yanı, bir distribütörün zaten sahip olduğu ilişkileri kurmamızın aylar, hatta yıllar sürecek olmasıydı."},{"en":"The distributor's terms, a 20% commission for the first year, felt steep at first glance.","tr":"Distribütörün şartları, yani ilk yıl için yüzde 20 komisyon, ilk bakışta fahiş geldi."},{"en":"We spent two weeks weighing the trade-offs, with every member of the team having their say.","tr":"İki hafta boyunca artıları ve eksileri tarttık ve ekipteki herkes fikrini söyledi."},{"en":"Our engineers were adamant that they didn't want to be pulled away from the product to chase sales.","tr":"Mühendislerimiz satış peşinde koşmak için üründen uzaklaştırılmak istemediklerinde kesinlikle ısrarcıydı."},{"en":"What ultimately tipped the balance, though, was speed.","tr":"Yine de sonunda dengeyi değiştiren şey hız oldu."},{"en":"For a startup like ours, time is the one resource you can't buy more of, and a better-funded competitor could easily beat us to market.","tr":"Bizim gibi bir girişim için zaman, fazlasını satın alamayacağın tek kaynak ve daha çok fonu olan bir rakip pazara bizden önce kolayca girebilir."},{"en":"Had we gone direct, we'd still be hiring salespeople instead of shipping devices.","tr":"Doğrudan satışa geçseydik, şu an cihaz göndermek yerine hâlâ satış elemanı işe alıyor olurduk."},{"en":"It was a genuinely hard call, but I'm convinced it was the right one.","tr":"Gerçekten zor bir karardı ama doğru olduğuna inanıyorum."}],"vocab":[{"en":"consequential","tr":"sonuçları büyük olan, önemli","ex":"It was the most consequential decision since we founded AIHEAR.","def":"having important results or effects"},{"en":"go direct","tr":"doğrudan satışa geçmek","ex":"Going direct was undeniably attractive.","def":"to sell to customers yourself, without a middleman"},{"en":"the catch","tr":"işin kötü yanı, püf noktası","ex":"The catch was that it would take months.","def":"a hidden problem or disadvantage"},{"en":"steep","tr":"fahiş, çok yüksek","ex":"A 20% commission felt steep at first.","def":"(of a price or cost) very high"},{"en":"weigh the trade-offs","tr":"artıları ve eksileri tartmak","ex":"We spent two weeks weighing the trade-offs.","def":"to compare what you gain and lose with each option"},{"en":"have your say","tr":"fikrini söyleme fırsatı bulmak","ex":"Every member of the team had their say.","def":"to get the chance to give your opinion"},{"en":"adamant","tr":"kararlı, ısrarcı","ex":"Our engineers were adamant.","def":"completely sure and not willing to change your mind"},{"en":"tip the balance","tr":"dengeyi değiştirmek, belirleyici olmak","ex":"What tipped the balance was speed.","def":"to be the factor that decides the result"},{"en":"beat someone to market","tr":"pazara birinden önce girmek","ex":"A better-funded competitor could beat us to market.","def":"to launch a product before a competitor does"},{"en":"a hard call","tr":"zor bir karar","ex":"It was a genuinely hard call.","def":"a difficult decision"}],"grammar":{"title":"Inversion: 'Had we gone direct…'","tr":"Üçüncü tip şart cümlesinde 'if' düşer ve 'had' başa gelir: 'Had we gone direct' = 'If we had gone direct'. Daha resmî ve vurgulu duyulur. Benzer şekilde yer ifadesiyle de devrik yapı kurulabilir: 'On the table were two options.'","examples":["Had we gone direct, we'd still be hiring salespeople.","Had we waited, a competitor could have beaten us to market.","On the table were two options."]},"questions":[{"q":"What was the main appeal of going direct?","options":["Keeping the full margin and staying close to customers","Avoiding certification","Hiring fewer engineers"],"a":0},{"q":"What does 'the catch' refer to?","options":["The distributor's commission","How long it would take to build relationships","The engineers' salaries"],"a":1},{"q":"What was the engineers' attitude toward selling?","options":["Enthusiastic","Indifferent","Firmly against being pulled into it"],"a":2},{"q":"What does the speaker imply with 'Had we gone direct, we'd still be hiring salespeople'?","options":["They regret not hiring more salespeople","The direct route would have slowed them down considerably","Salespeople are easy to find"],"a":1},{"q":"How would you describe the speaker's attitude to the decision?","options":["Uncertain and regretful","Defensive and angry","Convinced, while admitting it was difficult"],"a":2}],"gaps":[{"s":"The ___ was that it would have taken us months.","a":"catch","hint":"işin kötü yanı"},{"s":"We spent two weeks weighing the ___.","a":"trade-offs","hint":"artılar ve eksiler"},{"s":"Our engineers were ___ that they didn't want to chase sales.","a":"adamant","hint":"kesinlikle ısrarcı"},{"s":"A better-funded competitor could beat us to ___.","a":"market","hint":"pazar"}],"order":[{"a":"What ultimately tipped the balance was speed."},{"a":"It was a genuinely hard call."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Doğrudan satışa geçseydik hâlâ satış elemanı işe alıyor olurduk.","en":"Had we gone direct, we'd still be hiring salespeople.","keys":["gone direct","hiring salespeople"]},{"tr":"Sonunda dengeyi değiştiren şey hızdı.","en":"What ultimately tipped the balance was speed.","keys":["tipped the balance","speed"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Co-founder","personaTr":"Kurucu ortak","scene":"Kurucu ortağın, distribütör kararının tüm zayıf noktalarını seninle son bir kez masaya yatırmak istiyor.","turns":[{"ai":"I keep coming back to the margins; aren't we leaving money on the table with a distributor?","aiTr":"Aklım hep kâr marjlarında; distribütörle masada para bırakmıyor muyuz?","hint":"Going direct is attractive, but the catch is that it would take us months, if not years, to build the relationships a distributor already has.","keys":["catch","relationships","months"]},{"ai":"Twenty percent still feels steep to me.","aiTr":"Yüzde yirmi bana hâlâ fahiş geliyor.","hint":"It felt steep at first glance, but it's only for the first year, and time is the one resource we can't buy more of.","keys":["first year","steep","resource"]},{"ai":"Shouldn't the engineers help with sales, at least in the beginning?","aiTr":"En azından başta mühendisler satışa yardım etmemeli mi?","hint":"They were adamant that they didn't want to be pulled away from the product, and frankly, I agree with them.","keys":["adamant","product","pulled away"]},{"ai":"Be honest: do you have any doubts about it?","aiTr":"Dürüst ol: bu konuda hiç şüphen var mı?","hint":"It was a genuinely hard call, but had we gone direct, we'd still be hiring salespeople instead of shipping devices.","keys":["hard call","gone direct","shipping devices"]}]}},"li-01":{"intro":"Pasaport kontrolünde ve otelde doğal, rahat ve ince bir kibarlıkla konuşuyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Officer","en":"Good morning, and what brings you here?","tr":"Günaydın, sizi buraya ne getirdi?"},{"who":"Me","en":"I'm attending a medical technology conference, so it's strictly a business trip this time.","tr":"Bir medikal teknoloji konferansına katılıyorum, yani bu sefer tamamen iş amaçlı bir seyahat."},{"who":"Officer","en":"And how long are you planning on staying?","tr":"Peki ne kadar kalmayı planlıyorsunuz?"},{"who":"Me","en":"Just four days, with my return flight booked for Friday.","tr":"Sadece dört gün; dönüş uçuşum cumaya ayırtılmış durumda."},{"who":"Officer","en":"That all seems to be in order, so enjoy your stay.","tr":"Her şey yolunda görünüyor; iyi konaklamalar."},{"who":"Me","en":"Good evening, I should have a reservation under the name {name}.","tr":"İyi akşamlar, {name} adına bir rezervasyonum olması gerekiyor."},{"who":"Receptionist","en":"Yes, here we are, and if I could just take a quick look at your passport, that would be great.","tr":"Evet, işte burada; pasaportunuza kısaca bir göz atabilirsem harika olur."},{"who":"Me","en":"Of course, and while you're doing that, would you happen to know whether breakfast is included?","tr":"Tabii; siz o arada bakarken, kahvaltının dahil olup olmadığını acaba biliyor musunuz?"},{"who":"Receptionist","en":"It is, served between 7 and 10, and should you need anything earlier, just give reception a call.","tr":"Dahil, 7 ile 10 arası servis ediliyor; daha erken bir şeye ihtiyacınız olursa resepsiyonu aramanız yeterli."},{"who":"Receptionist","en":"You're in 512 on the fifth floor, and your key card is all set.","tr":"Beşinci kattaki 512'desiniz, anahtar kartınız da hazır."},{"who":"Me","en":"Perfect, and before I head up, could I trouble you for the wifi password?","tr":"Mükemmel; yukarı çıkmadan önce wifi şifresini rica edebilir miyim?"}],"vocab":[{"en":"What brings you here?","tr":"Sizi buraya ne getirdi?","ex":"Good morning, and what brings you here?","def":"a friendly way to ask why someone is visiting"},{"en":"strictly business","tr":"tamamen iş amaçlı","ex":"It's strictly a business trip this time.","def":"only for work, with no holiday part"},{"en":"plan on doing","tr":"...yapmayı planlamak","ex":"How long are you planning on staying?","def":"to intend to do something"},{"en":"be in order","tr":"usulüne uygun olmak","ex":"That all seems to be in order.","def":"to be correct and acceptable"},{"en":"I should have a reservation","tr":"bir rezervasyonum olması gerek","ex":"I should have a reservation under the name {name}.","def":"a polite way to say you expect a booking to exist"},{"en":"would you happen to know","tr":"acaba biliyor musunuz","ex":"Would you happen to know whether breakfast is included?","def":"a very polite way to ask a question"},{"en":"should you need","tr":"ihtiyaç duyarsanız","ex":"Should you need anything, just call reception.","def":"a formal way to say 'if you need'"},{"en":"all set","tr":"hazır","ex":"Your key card is all set.","def":"ready to use"},{"en":"head up","tr":"yukarı çıkmak","ex":"Before I head up, I need the wifi password.","def":"to go up, for example to your room"},{"en":"Could I trouble you for...?","tr":"...rica edebilir miyim?","ex":"Could I trouble you for the wifi password?","def":"a very polite way to ask for something"}],"grammar":{"title":"Formal inversion: Should you need...","tr":"Resmi ve kibar İngilizcede 'If you need...' yerine 'Should you need...' denir: 'if' düşer, 'should' başa gelir. Otel, havalimanı ve iş yazışmalarında sık duyulur.","examples":["Should you need anything earlier, just give reception a call.","Should the flight be delayed, I'll let you know.","Should you have any questions, the front desk is open all night."]},"questions":[{"q":"What does \"it's strictly a business trip this time\" imply?","options":["The speaker never travels for fun","The speaker may have visited for pleasure before","The speaker dislikes business trips"],"a":1},{"q":"How long will the speaker stay?","options":["Four days","Two days","A week"],"a":0},{"q":"What does the officer's comment \"That all seems to be in order\" convey?","options":["Suspicion about the speaker","Confusion about the dates","Satisfaction with the answers"],"a":2},{"q":"Why does the speaker say \"I should have a reservation\"?","options":["They are sure the booking failed","They want to change hotels","They want to cancel the booking","To signal politely that they expect a booking to exist"],"a":3},{"q":"What is the overall tone of the hotel exchange?","options":["Courteous and relaxed","Tense and impatient","Cold and bureaucratic"],"a":0}],"gaps":[{"s":"Good morning, and what ___ you here?","a":"brings","hint":"getiriyor"},{"s":"___ you need anything earlier, just give reception a call.","a":"Should","hint":"-ırsa (if yerine)"},{"s":"Could I ___ you for the wifi password?","a":"trouble","hint":"rahatsız etmek"},{"s":"Would you ___ to know whether breakfast is included?","a":"happen","hint":"acaba (kalıp)"}],"order":[{"a":"And how long are you planning on staying?"},{"a":"Your key card is all set."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Bu sefer tamamen iş amaçlı bir seyahat.","en":"It's strictly a business trip this time.","keys":["strictly","business trip"]},{"tr":"Kahvaltının dahil olup olmadığını acaba biliyor musunuz?","en":"Would you happen to know whether breakfast is included?","keys":["happen to know","whether"]},{"tr":"Daha erken bir şeye ihtiyacınız olursa resepsiyonu aramanız yeterli.","en":"Should you need anything earlier, just give reception a call.","keys":["should you need","reception"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Hotel receptionist","personaTr":"Otel resepsiyonisti","scene":"Berlin'de gece geç saatte otele varıyorsun. Resepsiyonist samimi ve kibar; sen de öyle.","turns":[{"ai":"Good evening and welcome. You've cut it fine, our restaurant's just closed. Are you checking in?","aiTr":"İyi akşamlar, hoş geldiniz. Kıl payı yetiştiniz, restoranımız az önce kapandı. Giriş mi yapıyorsunuz?","hint":"I am, yes; I should have a reservation under the name {name}.","keys":["should have","reservation","under the name"]},{"ai":"Ah yes, there you are. If I could just see your passport?","aiTr":"Ah evet, buldum. Pasaportunuzu bir görebilir miyim?","hint":"Of course, here you are; and would you happen to know whether breakfast is included?","keys":["here you are","happen to know","breakfast"]},{"ai":"It is, from 7 till 10. You're in 512 on the fifth floor. Is there anything else I can do for you?","aiTr":"Dahil, 7'den 10'a kadar. Beşinci kattaki 512'desiniz. Sizin için yapabileceğim başka bir şey var mı?","hint":"Could I trouble you for the wifi password? I've got a presentation to polish before tomorrow.","keys":["trouble you","wifi password","presentation"]},{"ai":"It's on the back of your key card. Should you need a taxi tomorrow, just let us know.","aiTr":"Anahtar kartınızın arkasında yazıyor. Yarın taksiye ihtiyacınız olursa bize haber vermeniz yeterli.","hint":"That's very kind; could you book one to the conference centre for 8 o'clock?","keys":["book","conference","8 o'clock"]}]}},"co-01":{"intro":"Bir konferansta sektörden biriyle tanışıyor, girişimini net bir sorun ve çözüm çerçevesinde, akıcı ve etkileyici biçimde tanıtıyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Me","en":"Excuse me, I don't believe we've met — I'm {name}.","tr":"Affedersiniz, sanırım tanışmadık; ben {name}."},{"who":"Sarah","en":"Nice to meet you, {name} — I'm Sarah, and I'm with a hospital group in the UK.","tr":"Tanıştığımıza memnun oldum {name}; ben Sarah, İngiltere'de bir hastane grubunda çalışıyorum."},{"who":"Me","en":"I'm the founder of AIHEAR, a Turkish medtech startup working on one very specific problem: the global shortage of audiologists.","tr":"Çok belirli bir sorun üzerinde çalışan Türk medtech girişimi AIHEAR'ın kurucusuyum: dünya çapındaki odyolog eksikliği."},{"who":"Sarah","en":"That's certainly one we feel, so what's your angle on it?","tr":"Bu kesinlikle bizim de hissettiğimiz bir sorun; peki siz konuya nasıl yaklaşıyorsunuz?"},{"who":"Me","en":"We've developed an autonomous audiometer that runs the entire hearing test without a specialist in the room.","tr":"Odada bir uzman olmadan tüm işitme testini yapan otonom bir odyometre geliştirdik."},{"who":"Me","en":"Essentially, the patient puts on headphones, presses a button whenever they hear a tone, and the AI adapts the test as it goes.","tr":"Özetle hasta kulaklığı takıyor, bir ses duyduğunda düğmeye basıyor ve yapay zekâ testi anında uyarlıyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"What comes out at the end, in under ten minutes, is a full audiogram.","tr":"Sonunda, on dakikadan kısa sürede, eksiksiz bir odyogram çıkıyor."},{"who":"Sarah","en":"Now that would make a dent in our waiting lists, which in some areas stretch to several months.","tr":"İşte bu, bazı bölgelerde birkaç aya kadar uzayan bekleme listelerimizi gözle görülür biçimde azaltır."},{"who":"Me","en":"That's precisely the bottleneck we set out to remove, particularly for clinics that simply can't hire more audiologists.","tr":"Ortadan kaldırmak için yola çıktığımız darboğaz tam olarak bu, özellikle de daha fazla odyolog işe alamayan klinikler için."},{"who":"Me","en":"Rather than keep you from the next session, may I leave you my card and pick this up afterwards?","tr":"Sizi bir sonraki oturumdan alıkoymak yerine, kartımı bırakıp konuya sonra devam edebilir miyiz?"},{"who":"Sarah","en":"Please do — I'd genuinely like to hear how it performed in your clinical study.","tr":"Lütfen; klinik çalışmanızda nasıl bir performans gösterdiğini gerçekten duymak isterim."},{"who":"Me","en":"Then I'll find you over coffee and bring the results with me.","tr":"O zaman kahve molasında sizi bulurum ve sonuçları da yanımda getiririm."}],"vocab":[{"en":"be with a company","tr":"bir şirkette çalışmak","ex":"I'm with a hospital group in the UK.","def":"to work for a particular organisation"},{"en":"medtech","tr":"medikal teknoloji","ex":"AIHEAR is a Turkish medtech startup.","def":"short for medical technology"},{"en":"angle on something","tr":"bir konuya yaklaşım","ex":"What's your angle on the problem?","def":"a particular way of approaching a problem"},{"en":"autonomous","tr":"otonom, kendi kendine çalışan","ex":"We've developed an autonomous audiometer.","def":"able to work without human control"},{"en":"as it goes","tr":"ilerledikçe, anında","ex":"The AI adapts the test as it goes.","def":"while the activity is happening"},{"en":"make a dent in","tr":"gözle görülür biçimde azaltmak","ex":"This could make a dent in our waiting lists.","def":"to reduce something by a noticeable amount"},{"en":"stretch to","tr":"...e kadar uzamak","ex":"Waiting lists stretch to several months.","def":"to last or reach as far as a certain length"},{"en":"bottleneck","tr":"darboğaz","ex":"The shortage of audiologists is the bottleneck.","def":"a point where a process slows down because of a limit"},{"en":"set out to","tr":"...mek için yola çıkmak","ex":"We set out to remove that bottleneck.","def":"to start doing something with a clear aim"},{"en":"keep someone from","tr":"birini ...den alıkoymak","ex":"I don't want to keep you from the next session.","def":"to stop someone from going somewhere or doing something"}],"grammar":{"title":"Reduced relative clauses: a startup working on …","tr":"'which is working' yerine sadece '-ing' kullanarak cümleyi kısaltabilirsin. Kendini tanıtırken bu yapı seni akıcı ve profesyonel gösterir.","examples":["AIHEAR is a Turkish medtech startup working on the shortage of audiologists.","Clinics struggling with long waiting lists need faster tests.","We met a hospital group looking for new diagnostic tools."]},"questions":[{"q":"How does the founder frame the company in the introduction?","options":["As a general health app","As focused on one specific problem","As a hearing aid maker"],"a":1},{"q":"What does Sarah imply with 'That's certainly one we feel'?","options":["Her hospital group also struggles with a lack of audiologists","She dislikes the idea","She thinks the problem is exaggerated"],"a":0},{"q":"What does 'make a dent in our waiting lists' mean?","options":["Make them longer","Publish them online","Reduce them noticeably"],"a":2},{"q":"Why does the founder suggest continuing later?","options":["To respect Sarah's time before the next session","They are bored with the conversation","They have nothing more to say"],"a":0},{"q":"What does Sarah's interest in the clinical study suggest?","options":["She is only being polite","She has already decided to buy","She is genuinely interested and wants evidence"],"a":2}],"gaps":[{"s":"That's certainly one we feel, so what's your ___ on it?","a":"angle","hint":"yaklaşım"},{"s":"Now that would make a ___ in our waiting lists.","a":"dent","hint":"gözle görülür azalma"},{"s":"That's precisely the bottleneck we set ___ to remove.","a":"out","hint":"yola çıkmak"},{"s":"The AI adapts the test as it ___.","a":"goes","hint":"ilerledikçe"}],"order":[{"a":"What comes out at the end is a full audiogram."},{"a":"May I leave you my card?"}],"translate":[{"tr":"Bu, bekleme listelerimizi gözle görülür biçimde azaltır.","en":"It would make a dent in our waiting lists.","keys":["make a dent","waiting lists"]},{"tr":"Konuya oturumdan sonra devam edelim.","en":"Let's pick this up after the session.","keys":["pick this up"]},{"tr":"İngiltere'de bir hastane grubunda çalışıyorum.","en":"I'm with a hospital group in the UK.","keys":["with a hospital group"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Head of operations at a clinic chain","personaTr":"Bir klinik zincirinin operasyon direktörü","scene":"Konferans arasında İrlanda'dan bir klinik zinciri yöneticisiyle tanışıyorsun; kısa ama etkileyici bir tanıtım yap.","turns":[{"ai":"I don't believe we've met. I'm Emma, and I head up operations for a clinic chain in Ireland.","aiTr":"Sanırım tanışmadık. Ben Emma; İrlanda'da bir klinik zincirinin operasyonlarını yönetiyorum.","hint":"Lovely to meet you, Emma. I'm {name}, founder of AIHEAR, a Turkish medtech startup working on the shortage of audiologists.","keys":["founder","medtech","shortage","audiologists"]},{"ai":"That's certainly a problem we feel. What's your angle on it?","aiTr":"Bu kesinlikle bizim de hissettiğimiz bir sorun. Siz nasıl yaklaşıyorsunuz?","hint":"We've developed an autonomous audiometer that runs the entire hearing test without a specialist in the room.","keys":["autonomous","audiometer","specialist","without"]},{"ai":"And how does it actually work for the patient?","aiTr":"Peki hasta açısından aslında nasıl işliyor?","hint":"The patient presses a button whenever they hear a tone, the AI adapts as it goes, and in under ten minutes you get an audiogram.","keys":["button","adapts","audiogram","ten minutes"]},{"ai":"I'd love to hear more, but I'm due at the next panel.","aiTr":"Daha fazlasını duymak isterdim ama bir sonraki panelde olmam gerekiyor.","hint":"Of course. May I leave you my card, and we can pick this up afterwards?","keys":["card","pick this up","afterwards"]}]}},"st-01":{"intro":"Olası bir ortağa girişimini ikna edici, net ve doğal bir dille anlatıyor, pazardaki boşluğu vurguluyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Partner","en":"I've heard a bit about AIHEAR, but I'd love to hear it in your own words.","tr":"AIHEAR hakkında biraz bir şeyler duydum ama senin ağzından dinlemeyi çok isterim."},{"who":"Me","en":"In a nutshell, we're a Turkish medtech startup that has built an autonomous, AI-assisted audiometer.","tr":"Kısacası, otonom ve yapay zekâ destekli bir odyometre geliştirmiş bir Türk medikal teknoloji girişimiyiz."},{"who":"Me","en":"Put simply, it does what an audiologist does, but without needing one in the room.","tr":"Basitçe söylemek gerekirse, bir odyoloğun yaptığını yapıyor ama odada bir odyoloğa ihtiyaç duymadan."},{"who":"Me","en":"The patient presses a button whenever they hear a tone, while the AI adapts the test in real time and produces an audiogram in under ten minutes.","tr":"Hasta her ton duyduğunda bir düğmeye basıyor; bu sırada yapay zekâ testi gerçek zamanlı uyarlıyor ve on dakikadan kısa sürede bir odyogram çıkarıyor."},{"who":"Partner","en":"And where exactly do you see the gap in the market?","tr":"Peki pazardaki boşluğu tam olarak nerede görüyorsun?"},{"who":"Me","en":"What most people don't realise is that roughly one in five people has some degree of hearing loss, yet most are never tested.","tr":"Çoğu insanın fark etmediği şey, yaklaşık her beş kişiden birinin bir dereceye kadar işitme kaybı yaşadığı, ama çoğunun hiç test edilmediği."},{"who":"Me","en":"The bottleneck isn't the technology; it's the chronic shortage of audiologists, especially in smaller towns where people wait months for an appointment.","tr":"Darboğaz teknoloji değil; özellikle insanların randevu için aylarca beklediği küçük şehirlerdeki kronik odyolog eksikliği."},{"who":"Partner","en":"So who's actually buying it at this stage?","tr":"Peki bu aşamada onu gerçekten kim satın alıyor?"},{"who":"Me","en":"Mainly hospitals, clinics and hearing aid shops, and we already have five paying customers on board.","tr":"Ağırlıklı olarak hastaneler, klinikler ve işitme cihazı mağazaları; şimdiden beş ücretli müşterimiz var."},{"who":"Me","en":"Not only does it free up specialists' time, but it also lets clinics test far more patients a day.","tr":"Hem uzmanlara zaman kazandırıyor hem de kliniklerin günde çok daha fazla hastayı test etmesini sağlıyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"Behind it is a team of six: three engineers, a doctor and two of us handling the commercial side.","tr":"Arkasında altı kişilik bir ekip var: üç mühendis, bir doktor ve ticari tarafı yürüten iki kişi."},{"who":"Me","en":"Having won over our first customers, we're now looking for the right partners to take AIHEAR into Europe, which is really why I wanted to catch you today.","tr":"İlk müşterilerimizi kazandıktan sonra şimdi AIHEAR'ı Avrupa'ya taşıyacak doğru ortakları arıyoruz; bugün seni yakalamak istememin asıl nedeni de bu."}],"vocab":[{"en":"in a nutshell","tr":"kısacası","ex":"In a nutshell, we're a Turkish medtech startup.","def":"in a few words"},{"en":"autonomous","tr":"otonom, kendi kendine çalışan","ex":"We've built an autonomous, AI-assisted audiometer.","def":"able to work without a person controlling it"},{"en":"adapt in real time","tr":"gerçek zamanlı uyarlamak","ex":"The AI adapts the test in real time.","def":"to change something immediately as things happen"},{"en":"gap in the market","tr":"pazardaki boşluk","ex":"Where do you see the gap in the market?","def":"a need that no product is meeting yet"},{"en":"bottleneck","tr":"darboğaz","ex":"The bottleneck is the shortage of audiologists.","def":"the one thing that slows down the whole process"},{"en":"chronic shortage","tr":"kronik eksiklik","ex":"There's a chronic shortage of audiologists.","def":"a lack of something that continues for a long time"},{"en":"on board","tr":"dahil, bizimle birlikte","ex":"We already have five paying customers on board.","def":"involved in and supporting a project"},{"en":"free up","tr":"(zaman/kaynak) açmak","ex":"It frees up specialists' time.","def":"to make time or resources available for something else"},{"en":"the commercial side","tr":"ticari taraf","ex":"Two of us handle the commercial side.","def":"the part of a business that deals with sales and money"},{"en":"win over","tr":"ikna edip kazanmak","ex":"We've won over our first customers.","def":"to persuade someone to support or buy from you"}],"grammar":{"title":"Inversion after 'Not only'","tr":"'Not only' cümlenin başına gelince yardımcı fiil özneden önce gelir (does it, is it, have we). Vurgu katar ve ikna edici konuşmada çok etkilidir.","examples":["Not only does it free up specialists' time, but it also lets clinics test more patients.","Not only is the test fast, but it's also accurate.","Not only have we built the device, but we've also won our first customers."]},"questions":[{"q":"What does the speaker identify as the real bottleneck?","options":["The cost of the technology","The shortage of audiologists","A lack of patients"],"a":1},{"q":"Why does the speaker begin with 'What most people don't realise'?","options":["To admit a weakness in the product","To change the subject","To highlight a problem the listener may underestimate"],"a":2},{"q":"How would you describe the speaker's attitude when presenting the company?","options":["Confident and concise","Nervous and apologetic","Bored and distant"],"a":0},{"q":"What does 'having won over our first customers' suggest?","options":["The company has no sales yet","There is early proof that clinics will pay for the product","The customers got the device for free"],"a":1},{"q":"What does the speaker most likely want from the listener?","options":["Investment for the clinical study","A job at their clinic chain","Help entering the European market as a partner"],"a":2}],"gaps":[{"s":"The ___ isn't the technology; it's the shortage of audiologists.","a":"bottleneck","hint":"darboğaz"},{"s":"We already have five paying customers on ___.","a":"board","hint":"dahil, bizimle"},{"s":"It ___ up specialists' time.","a":"frees","hint":"zaman açmak"},{"s":"In a ___, we're a Turkish medtech startup.","a":"nutshell","hint":"kısacası"}],"order":[{"a":"Most people with hearing loss are never tested."},{"a":"We already have five paying customers on board."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Kısacası, otonom bir odyometre geliştirdik.","en":"In a nutshell, we've built an autonomous audiometer.","keys":["in a nutshell","autonomous audiometer"]},{"tr":"Asıl darboğaz odyolog eksikliği.","en":"The real bottleneck is the shortage of audiologists.","keys":["bottleneck","shortage of audiologists"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Potential partner","personaTr":"Olası iş ortağı","scene":"Berlin'deki bir sağlık teknolojisi konferansında, Almanya'da bir klinik zinciri yöneten biriyle kahve içiyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"I've heard a bit about AIHEAR, but I'd love to hear it in your own words.","aiTr":"AIHEAR hakkında biraz bir şeyler duydum ama senin ağzından dinlemeyi çok isterim.","hint":"In a nutshell, we've built an autonomous, AI-assisted audiometer that does what an audiologist does, without needing one in the room.","keys":["in a nutshell","audiometer","audiologist"]},{"ai":"Hearing tests aren't new, though; where exactly is the gap in the market?","aiTr":"Ama işitme testleri yeni değil; pazardaki boşluk tam olarak nerede?","hint":"What most people don't realise is that one in five people has some hearing loss, and the real bottleneck is the shortage of audiologists.","keys":["bottleneck","shortage","one in five"]},{"ai":"Is anyone actually paying for it yet, or is it still a prototype?","aiTr":"Şu an gerçekten para ödeyen var mı, yoksa hâlâ bir prototip mi?","hint":"We already have five paying customers on board, and not only does it free up specialists' time, but it also lets clinics test far more patients.","keys":["five paying customers","on board","free up"]},{"ai":"So what would you want from a partner like us?","aiTr":"Peki bizim gibi bir ortaktan ne beklersin?","hint":"We're looking for the right partners to take AIHEAR into Europe, which is really why I wanted to catch you today.","keys":["partners","Europe","take AIHEAR"]}]}},"co-02":{"intro":"Konferanstaki sohbeti, resmî ama sıcak ve ikna edici bir takip e-postasıyla somut bir demoya dönüştürüyorsun.","text":[{"en":"Subject: Following up from MedTech Europe: AIHEAR demo","tr":"Konu: MedTech Europe sonrası takip: AIHEAR demosu"},{"en":"Dear Sarah,","tr":"Sevgili Sarah,"},{"en":"It was a real pleasure meeting you at MedTech Europe yesterday, and thank you for such a candid conversation about the pressure on your waiting lists.","tr":"Dün MedTech Europe'ta sizinle tanışmak gerçekten büyük bir zevkti; bekleme listeleriniz üzerindeki baskı hakkındaki bu kadar açık sohbet için de teşekkür ederim."},{"en":"Having heard how long some of your patients wait for a basic hearing test, I came away convinced that this is exactly where our autonomous audiometer can make a difference.","tr":"Bazı hastalarınızın basit bir işitme testi için ne kadar beklediğini duyunca, otonom odyometremizin tam da burada fark yaratabileceğine ikna oldum."},{"en":"As promised, I've attached a short presentation outlining how the system works and what our clinical study showed.","tr":"Söz verdiğim gibi, sistemin nasıl çalıştığını ve klinik çalışmamızın neler gösterdiğini özetleyen kısa bir sunum ekledim."},{"en":"Rather than take up more of your time over email, I'd be glad to walk you and your team through a short online demo.","tr":"E-postayla daha fazla vaktinizi almak yerine, size ve ekibinize kısa bir çevrimiçi demoyla sistemi adım adım göstermekten memnuniyet duyarım."},{"en":"Would next Tuesday or Wednesday afternoon suit you, or feel free to suggest a time that fits around your schedule.","tr":"Gelecek salı veya çarşamba öğleden sonra size uyar mı; değilse programınıza uyan bir zaman önermekten çekinmeyin."},{"en":"Should you have any questions in the meantime, I'd be happy to answer them.","tr":"Bu arada herhangi bir sorunuz olursa, yanıtlamaktan memnuniyet duyarım."},{"en":"I look forward to continuing the conversation.","tr":"Sohbetimizi sürdürmeyi dört gözle bekliyorum."},{"en":"Kind regards, {name}","tr":"Saygılarımla, {name}"}],"vocab":[{"en":"candid","tr":"açık sözlü, samimi","ex":"Thank you for such a candid conversation.","def":"honest and direct, even about difficult things"},{"en":"come away convinced","tr":"ikna olmuş olarak ayrılmak","ex":"I came away convinced that we can help.","def":"to leave a meeting or event feeling sure about something"},{"en":"make a difference","tr":"fark yaratmak","ex":"Our audiometer can make a difference in busy clinics.","def":"to have a real, positive effect"},{"en":"outline","tr":"ana hatlarıyla anlatmak","ex":"The presentation outlines how the system works.","def":"to describe the main points of something"},{"en":"take up someone's time","tr":"birinin vaktini almak","ex":"I don't want to take up more of your time.","def":"to use some of someone's time"},{"en":"walk someone through","tr":"birine bir şeyi adım adım göstermek","ex":"I'd be glad to walk you through a demo.","def":"to explain or show something step by step"},{"en":"fit around","tr":"...e göre ayarlanmak, ...e uymak","ex":"Suggest a time that fits around your schedule.","def":"to be arranged so that it does not clash with other plans"},{"en":"in the meantime","tr":"bu arada","ex":"In the meantime, feel free to read the presentation.","def":"in the period before something planned happens"},{"en":"continue the conversation","tr":"sohbeti sürdürmek","ex":"I look forward to continuing the conversation.","def":"to talk more about a topic you started discussing"},{"en":"Kind regards","tr":"Saygılarımla, sevgiyle","ex":"Kind regards, Sarah","def":"a polite and slightly warm way to end a formal email"}],"grammar":{"title":"Formal conditional inversion: Should you …","tr":"'If you have any questions' yerine 'Should you have any questions' demek, resmî yazışmalarda daha zarif ve profesyonel durur. 'If' düşer ve 'should' cümlenin başına gelir.","examples":["Should you have any questions, I'd be happy to answer them.","Should Tuesday not suit you, feel free to suggest another time.","Should your team be interested, we can arrange a trial."]},"questions":[{"q":"What is the overall tone of the email?","options":["Formal but warm","Cold and distant","Overly casual","Pushy"],"a":0},{"q":"Why does the writer mention what they 'came away convinced' of?","options":["To complain about the conference","To show the device answers a problem Sarah actually described","To ask Sarah for an investment"],"a":1},{"q":"Besides how the system works, what does the presentation cover?","options":["Prices for the UK market","A list of competitors","What the clinical study showed"],"a":2},{"q":"Why does the writer propose a demo 'rather than take up more of your time over email'?","options":["To respect Sarah's time and show the product live","Because the presentation is incomplete","Because email is not secure"],"a":0},{"q":"What does 'feel free to suggest a time that fits around your schedule' imply?","options":["Sarah must cancel other meetings","The writer is flexible about the timing","The writer is only free on Tuesday"],"a":1}],"gaps":[{"s":"I came ___ convinced that this is exactly where we can help.","a":"away","hint":"...den ayrılmak"},{"s":"I've attached a short presentation ___ how the system works.","a":"outlining","hint":"ana hatlarıyla anlatan"},{"s":"I'd be glad to walk you ___ a short online demo.","a":"through","hint":"adım adım göstermek"},{"s":"___ you have any questions in the meantime, I'd be happy to answer them.","a":"Should","hint":"...olursa (resmî)"}],"order":[{"a":"I look forward to continuing the conversation."},{"a":"Feel free to suggest a time that fits around your schedule."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Herhangi bir sorunuz olursa, yanıtlamaktan memnuniyet duyarım.","en":"Should you have any questions, I'd be happy to answer them.","keys":["should you have","happy to answer"]},{"tr":"Size sistemi kısa bir demoyla adım adım göstermek isterim.","en":"I'd be glad to walk you through the system in a short demo.","keys":["walk you through","short demo"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Sarah (by email)","personaTr":"Sarah (e-posta ile)","scene":"Sarah ilgiyle cevap veriyor; demo ayrıntılarını resmî ama sıcak bir dille netleştiriyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"Hi {name}, thanks for the follow-up and the slides. The study results were particularly interesting.","aiTr":"Merhaba {name}, takip e-postası ve slaytlar için teşekkürler. Çalışma sonuçları özellikle ilginçti.","hint":"I'm glad you found them useful; I'd be happy to walk you and your team through a short online demo.","keys":["walk you","through","demo"]},{"ai":"That would be great. What timing did you have in mind?","aiTr":"Harika olur. Nasıl bir zaman düşünüyordunuz?","hint":"Would next Tuesday or Wednesday afternoon suit you, or feel free to suggest a time that fits around your schedule.","keys":["suit you","fits around","Tuesday","Wednesday"]},{"ai":"Wednesday at 2 pm works. Who would you recommend we bring in from our side?","aiTr":"Çarşamba 14:00 uygun. Bizim taraftan kimi dahil etmemizi önerirsiniz?","hint":"I'd recommend your clinic manager and one of your audiologists, as they'd get the most out of seeing it in action.","keys":["clinic manager","audiologists","in action"]},{"ai":"Perfect, I'll keep the slot free.","aiTr":"Mükemmel, o saati boş tutacağım.","hint":"Thank you; I'll send a calendar invitation shortly, and should you have any questions before then, just let me know.","keys":["calendar invitation","should you have","let me know"]}]}},"fu-01":{"intro":"Bir sağlık teknolojisi konferansındaki panelde, şüpheci bir doktorun sorusunu, yapay zekânın klinisyenleri güçlendirmesi gerektiğini savunarak incelikli bir dille yanıtlıyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Dr. Weber","en":"Let me play devil's advocate: if an algorithm can read a scan faster than I can, what exactly is left for doctors to do?","tr":"Şeytanın avukatlığını yapayım: bir algoritma bir taramayı benden hızlı okuyabiliyorsa, doktorlara tam olarak ne kalıyor?"},{"who":"Me","en":"It's a fair challenge, but I think it rests on a false choice between humans and machines.","tr":"Haklı bir itiraz, ama bence insanlar ile makineler arasında yanlış bir ikileme dayanıyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"What AI should do is support clinicians, not stand in for them.","tr":"Yapay zekânın yapması gereken şey klinisyenleri desteklemek, onların yerine geçmek değil."},{"who":"Me","en":"Granted, its strengths are hard to argue with: it's fast, it's consistent, and it doesn't flag at three in the morning the way we all do.","tr":"Kabul, güçlü yanlarına itiraz etmek zor: hızlı, tutarlı ve hepimizin yaptığı gibi gece üçte gücü tükenmiyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"Yet it still makes mistakes, and it's only ever as good as the data it's been trained on.","tr":"Yine de hata yapıyor ve her zaman ancak eğitildiği veri kadar iyi."},{"who":"Me","en":"Feed it skewed or incomplete data, and it will reproduce those blind spots at scale, often without anyone noticing.","tr":"Ona çarpık ya da eksik veri verirseniz, bu kör noktaları geniş ölçekte, çoğu zaman kimse fark etmeden çoğaltır."},{"who":"Me","en":"Not only does that make human oversight essential, but it also means accountability can't simply be handed over to software.","tr":"Bu yalnızca insan denetimini zorunlu kılmakla kalmıyor, hesap verebilirliğin öylece yazılıma devredilemeyeceği anlamına da geliyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"There's also the question of trust: patients want someone who can weigh up the evidence, explain the trade-offs and stand behind the decision.","tr":"Bir de güven meselesi var: hastalar kanıtları tartabilen, artıları ve eksileri açıklayabilen ve kararın arkasında durabilen birini ister."},{"who":"Me","en":"Our own audiometer is a case in point: it runs a full hearing test in under ten minutes, with no expert in the room.","tr":"Kendi odyometremiz buna iyi bir örnek: odada uzman olmadan, tam bir işitme testini on dakikadan kısa sürede yapıyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"Far from sidelining audiologists, it frees them to focus on the complex cases where their expertise genuinely makes a difference.","tr":"Odyologları kenara itmek bir yana, uzmanlıklarının gerçekten fark yarattığı karmaşık vakalara odaklanmalarını sağlıyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"So no, I don't think AI will replace doctors, though doctors who embrace it may end up replacing those who don't.","tr":"Yani hayır, yapay zekânın doktorların yerini alacağını düşünmüyorum; ama onu benimseyen doktorlar, benimsemeyenlerin yerini alabilir."}],"vocab":[{"en":"play devil's advocate","tr":"şeytanın avukatlığını yapmak","ex":"Let me play devil's advocate for a moment.","def":"to argue the opposite view in order to test an idea"},{"en":"a false choice","tr":"yanlış ikilem","ex":"Humans versus machines is a false choice.","def":"a situation presented as having only two options when there are more"},{"en":"stand in for","tr":"yerine geçmek","ex":"AI shouldn't stand in for clinicians.","def":"to take someone's place"},{"en":"flag","tr":"gücü tükenmek, yorulmak","ex":"Unlike us, AI doesn't flag at night.","def":"to become tired or less energetic"},{"en":"skewed","tr":"çarpık","ex":"Skewed data leads to skewed results.","def":"not accurate because it favours one side"},{"en":"blind spot","tr":"kör nokta","ex":"Every dataset has blind spots.","def":"an area where you fail to see problems"},{"en":"at scale","tr":"geniş ölçekte","ex":"AI can repeat an error at scale.","def":"in large numbers or across a large system"},{"en":"human oversight","tr":"insan denetimi","ex":"Human oversight is essential in medicine.","def":"people checking and controlling a process"},{"en":"accountability","tr":"hesap verebilirlik","ex":"Accountability can't be handed over to software.","def":"being responsible for decisions and their consequences"},{"en":"a case in point","tr":"tam bir örnek","ex":"Our audiometer is a case in point.","def":"a clear example of what you are talking about"}],"grammar":{"title":"Cleft sentences: 'What AI should do is…'","tr":"'What … is …' yapısı cümlenin bir bölümünü öne çıkarır ve konuşmacının asıl vurgusunu netleştirir. Panellerde karşı görüşe cevap verirken çok doğal duyulur.","examples":["What AI should do is support clinicians, not stand in for them.","What patients want is someone who can stand behind the decision.","What worries me is skewed data, not fast algorithms."]},"questions":[{"q":"Why does Dr. Weber say 'Let me play devil's advocate'?","options":["To signal a deliberately provocative question","To admit defeat","To change the topic"],"a":0},{"q":"What does the speaker mean by 'a false choice'?","options":["Doctors must choose between two devices","It is wrong to frame the issue as humans versus machines","AI always chooses badly"],"a":1},{"q":"What risk does the speaker associate with skewed data?","options":["The device becomes slower","Patients stop coming","Errors are repeated at scale, often unnoticed","The test costs more"],"a":2},{"q":"What is the speaker's overall attitude towards AI?","options":["Dismissive","Uncritically enthusiastic","Fearful","Optimistic but cautious"],"a":3},{"q":"What does the final sentence imply?","options":["Doctors who use AI well will have an advantage","AI will eventually replace all doctors","Doctors should avoid AI"],"a":0}],"gaps":[{"s":"Let me play devil's ___.","a":"advocate","hint":"avukat"},{"s":"Feed it skewed data, and it will reproduce those blind ___ at scale.","a":"spots","hint":"noktalar"},{"s":"Our own audiometer is a case in ___.","a":"point","hint":"tam bir örnek (deyim)"},{"s":"Accountability can't simply be handed ___ to software.","a":"over","hint":"devretmek"}],"order":[{"a":"What AI should do is support clinicians."},{"a":"Patients want someone who can explain the trade-offs."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Yapay zekânın yapması gereken şey klinisyenleri desteklemek, onların yerine geçmek değil.","en":"What AI should do is support clinicians, not stand in for them.","keys":["what ai should do","support clinicians"]},{"tr":"Bu yalnızca insan denetimini zorunlu kılmakla kalmıyor, hesap verebilirliğin yazılıma devredilemeyeceği anlamına da geliyor.","en":"Not only does that make human oversight essential, but it also means accountability can't be handed over to software.","keys":["not only does","human oversight","accountability"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Skeptical doctor on the panel","personaTr":"Paneldeki şüpheci doktor","scene":"Panelde deneyimli ve şüpheci bir doktor, iddialarını tek tek sorguluyor. Dengeli ama kararlı bir şekilde yanıt veriyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"Let's be candid: isn't 'AI will support doctors' just a polite way of saying 'AI will replace them eventually'?","aiTr":"Açık konuşalım: 'Yapay zekâ doktorları destekleyecek' demek, 'eninde sonunda yerlerini alacak' demenin kibar bir yolu değil mi?","hint":"I'd push back on that: what AI should do is support clinicians, not stand in for them.","keys":["push back","support clinicians","stand in for"]},{"ai":"Fine, but algorithms don't get tired, they don't take holidays, and they're cheaper than I am.","aiTr":"Peki ama algoritmalar yorulmaz, tatile çıkmaz ve benden daha ucuzdur.","hint":"Granted, but they still make mistakes, and they're only ever as good as the data they've been trained on.","keys":["granted","make mistakes","only ever as good as","data"]},{"ai":"So when something goes wrong, who's accountable?","aiTr":"Peki bir şey ters gittiğinde hesabını kim verecek?","hint":"A human, always; accountability can't simply be handed over to software, which is why human oversight is essential.","keys":["accountability","human oversight","handed over"]},{"ai":"What does that look like in practice, with your own device?","aiTr":"Kendi cihazınızda bu pratikte nasıl görünüyor?","hint":"Our audiometer handles the routine tests in under ten minutes, which frees audiologists to focus on the complex cases.","keys":["routine tests","under ten minutes","complex cases"]}]}},"ab-01":{"intro":"Berlin'de bir daireyi görüyorsun ve ev sahibiyle kira, depozito ve sözleşme koşullarını kibarca pazarlık ederek konuşuyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Landlord","en":"Do come in—having renovated the kitchen and bathroom last spring, I'm rather proud of how the place has turned out.","tr":"Buyurun girin; geçen bahar mutfakla banyoyu yeniledikten sonra dairenin aldığı halden epey gururluyum."},{"who":"Me","en":"I can see why; it's far brighter than the photos suggested.","tr":"Nedenini anlıyorum; fotoğrafların gösterdiğinden çok daha aydınlık."},{"who":"Me","en":"Before I get carried away, though, could you walk me through what the €1,200 actually covers?","tr":"Ama kendimi kaptırmadan önce, 1.200 avronun tam olarak neleri kapsadığını adım adım anlatır mısınız?"},{"who":"Landlord","en":"Heating and water are included, whereas the internet is down to you, so you'd have to sort out a provider yourself.","tr":"Isınma ve su dahil; internet ise size kalmış, yani bir sağlayıcıyı kendiniz ayarlamanız gerekir."},{"who":"Landlord","en":"As for the deposit, it's the standard three months' rent, so €3,600 in total.","tr":"Depozitoya gelince, standart üç aylık kira; toplamda 3.600 avro."},{"who":"Me","en":"That's entirely fair, although, having just shipped my life over from Istanbul, I'd find it much easier to pay it in three monthly instalments.","tr":"Gayet adil, ama hayatımı daha yeni İstanbul'dan buraya taşımışken, üç aylık taksitte ödemek benim için çok daha kolay olur."},{"who":"Landlord","en":"Not only is that fine, it's actually what most of my tenants opt for.","tr":"Bu sadece olur değil, aslında kiracılarımın çoğu da bunu tercih ediyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"Brilliant—and is the two-year minimum set in stone, or is there any flexibility?","tr":"Harika; peki iki yıllık asgari süre kesin mi, yoksa biraz esneklik var mı?"},{"who":"Landlord","en":"The two years aren't negotiable, I'm afraid, but the flat is yours from 1 November if you want it.","tr":"Korkarım iki yıl pazarlığa açık değil, ama isterseniz daire 1 Kasım'dan itibaren sizin."},{"who":"Landlord","en":"What I'll need from you is your passport and some proof of income—company papers will do if you don't have payslips.","tr":"Sizden ihtiyacım olan şey pasaportunuz ve bir gelir belgesi; maaş bordronuz yoksa şirket belgeleri de yeterli olur."},{"who":"Me","en":"That's a weight off my mind, since as a founder I've yet to pay myself a proper salary.","tr":"İçim rahatladı, çünkü kurucu olarak kendime henüz doğru dürüst bir maaş ödemedim."}],"vocab":[{"en":"turn out","tr":"sonuçlanmak, ortaya çıkmak","ex":"I'm proud of how the place has turned out.","def":"to develop or end in a particular way"},{"en":"get carried away","tr":"kendini kaptırmak","ex":"Before I get carried away, could you explain the costs?","def":"to become so excited that you stop thinking clearly"},{"en":"walk someone through","tr":"adım adım anlatmak","ex":"Could you walk me through what the rent covers?","def":"to explain something to someone slowly, step by step"},{"en":"be down to someone","tr":"birinin sorumluluğunda olmak","ex":"The internet is down to you.","def":"to be someone's responsibility"},{"en":"sort out","tr":"halletmek, ayarlamak","ex":"You'd have to sort out a provider yourself.","def":"to organise or deal with something"},{"en":"opt for","tr":"tercih etmek","ex":"Most tenants opt for monthly instalments.","def":"to choose one thing from several possibilities"},{"en":"set in stone","tr":"kesin, değiştirilemez","ex":"Is the two-year minimum set in stone?","def":"fixed and impossible to change"},{"en":"negotiable","tr":"pazarlığa açık","ex":"The two years aren't negotiable.","def":"able to be changed through discussion"},{"en":"will do","tr":"yeterli olmak, iş görmek","ex":"Company papers will do if you don't have payslips.","def":"to be good enough or acceptable"},{"en":"a weight off my mind","tr":"içimin rahatlaması","ex":"Knowing that is a weight off my mind.","def":"a great relief from worry"}],"grammar":{"title":"Inversion after 'Not only'","tr":"Vurgu için 'Not only' cümle başına gelince yardımcı fiil özneden önce gelir: 'Not only is that fine…'. Kibar ama güçlü bir onay ya da vurgu yaratır.","examples":["Not only is that fine, it's what most of my tenants opt for.","Not only is the flat bright, it's also quiet at the back.","Not only have I renovated the kitchen, I've also redone the bathroom."]},"questions":[{"q":"What is the landlord's attitude towards the flat?","options":["Indifferent","Proud of the renovation","Apologetic about its condition","Worried about its price"],"a":1},{"q":"How does the speaker make the instalment request sound reasonable?","options":["By mentioning the cost of moving from Istanbul","By threatening to look elsewhere","By offering a higher rent"],"a":0},{"q":"What does 'the internet is down to you' imply?","options":["It is very slow","It is broken","The tenant must arrange it"],"a":2},{"q":"Which point does the landlord refuse to negotiate?","options":["The deposit","The two-year minimum","The documents","The move-in date"],"a":1},{"q":"Why is the speaker relieved at the end?","options":["Dogs are allowed after all","The internet is free","Company papers will be accepted instead of payslips"],"a":2}],"gaps":[{"s":"Could you walk me ___ what the €1,200 actually covers?","a":"through","hint":"baştan sona (anlatmak)"},{"s":"Not only ___ that fine, it's actually what most of my tenants opt for.","a":"is","hint":"devrik yapı: yardımcı fiil önce"},{"s":"Is the two-year minimum set in ___?","a":"stone","hint":"taş (kesin, değişmez)"},{"s":"That's a weight off my ___.","a":"mind","hint":"akıl (içim rahatladı)"}],"order":[{"a":"I'm afraid the two years aren't negotiable."},{"a":"Most of my tenants opt for monthly instalments."}],"translate":[{"tr":"İnternet size kalmış, yani bir sağlayıcıyı kendiniz ayarlamanız gerekir.","en":"The internet is down to you, so you'd have to sort out a provider yourself.","keys":["down to you","sort out","provider"]},{"tr":"Maaş bordronuz yoksa şirket belgeleri de yeterli olur.","en":"Company papers will do if you don't have payslips.","keys":["will do","payslips"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Landlord","personaTr":"Ev sahibi","scene":"Daireyi gezdin ve çok beğendin. Ev sahibi Bayan Becker son kez sorularını soruyor; sen de kibar ama net konuşuyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"So, now that you've had a proper look round, how does it compare with the other places you've seen?","aiTr":"Evet, doğru dürüst bir göz attınız; gördüğünüz diğer yerlerle karşılaştırınca nasıl?","hint":"Honestly, it's in a different league—it's far brighter, and the renovated kitchen is a real selling point.","keys":["different league","brighter","selling point"]},{"ai":"I should mention I'm not keen on dogs, though cats are fine. Would that be a problem?","aiTr":"Belirtmeliyim, köpeklere pek sıcak bakmıyorum ama kedi olur. Bu bir sorun olur mu?","hint":"Not in the slightest—I don't have any pets, and with my working hours, I couldn't look after one anyway.","keys":["not in the slightest","don't have any pets","no pets"]},{"ai":"Is there anything that's giving you second thoughts?","aiTr":"Sizi tereddüde düşüren bir şey var mı?","hint":"Only the noise, really—how lively does it get at night, especially at weekends?","keys":["noise","at night","lively"]},{"ai":"The bedroom faces the courtyard, so it's pretty quiet, but the bar on the corner does get rowdy on Fridays. Can you live with that?","aiTr":"Yatak odası avluya bakıyor, o yüzden oldukça sessiz; ama köşedeki bar cuma günleri gerçekten gürültülü oluyor. Buna katlanabilir misiniz?","hint":"Given that it's only on Fridays and the bedroom is at the back, I'm sure I can live with it.","keys":["live with","only on Fridays","at the back"]}]}},"ab-02":{"intro":"Berlin'de bankadasın; kişisel ve ticari hesap arasındaki farkı, ücretleri ve süreci akıcı ve doğal bir dille konuşuyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Clerk","en":"Good morning—I take it you're here about opening an account?","tr":"Günaydın; anladığım kadarıyla hesap açmak için geldiniz?"},{"who":"Me","en":"That's right; having just relocated to Berlin to set up my company's European office, I'm after both a personal and a business account.","tr":"Doğru; şirketimin Avrupa ofisini kurmak için Berlin'e yeni taşındım ve hem kişisel hem ticari bir hesap istiyorum."},{"who":"Clerk","en":"What we'll need to see first is your registration certificate, as without a registered address our hands are tied.","tr":"Önce görmemiz gereken şey adres kayıt belgeniz, çünkü kayıtlı bir adres olmadan elimiz kolumuz bağlı."},{"who":"Me","en":"I sorted that out at the citizens' office last week, so here it is, together with my passport and residence permit.","tr":"Onu geçen hafta Bürgeramt'ta hallettim; işte burada, pasaportum ve oturma iznimle birlikte."},{"who":"Clerk","en":"Excellent—that covers the personal account, which comes free of charge as long as at least €1,000 lands in it each month.","tr":"Mükemmel; bu kişisel hesap için yeterli, her ay en az 1.000 avro yattığı sürece hesap ücretsiz."},{"who":"Clerk","en":"Should it fall short, there's a modest fee of €5 a month.","tr":"Bu tutarın altında kalırsa, aylık 5 avroluk makul bir ücret var."},{"who":"Me","en":"And what exactly sets the business account apart, beyond the price?","tr":"Peki fiyatı dışında ticari hesabı tam olarak farklı kılan ne?"},{"who":"Clerk","en":"It's geared towards company transactions and keeps them ring-fenced from your personal finances, though at €15 a month it's noticeably pricier.","tr":"Şirket işlemlerine yönelik ve onları kişisel paranızdan ayrı tutuyor, ama aylık 15 avroyla belirgin şekilde daha pahalı."},{"who":"Clerk","en":"Not until your company appears in the commercial register, however, can we open it.","tr":"Ancak şirketiniz ticaret siciline girmeden onu açamayız."},{"who":"Me","en":"I'm told that's a matter of days rather than weeks, so I'll pencil in another appointment for next week.","tr":"Bana bunun haftalar değil günler meselesi olduğu söylendi, o yüzden gelecek hafta için şimdiden bir randevu not edeyim."},{"who":"Clerk","en":"Meanwhile, your debit card will be posted to you, with the PIN following in a separate letter as a precaution.","tr":"Bu arada banka kartınız size postalanacak, şifreniz de önlem olarak ayrı bir mektupla ardından gelecek."},{"who":"Me","en":"Two letters for one card—that's German thoroughness for you.","tr":"Bir kart için iki mektup; işte tam Alman titizliği."}],"vocab":[{"en":"I take it","tr":"anladığım kadarıyla, sanırım","ex":"I take it you're here about an account?","def":"used to say you think something is true"},{"en":"be after something","tr":"bir şey istemek, peşinde olmak","ex":"I'm after a business account.","def":"to want or be looking for something"},{"en":"our hands are tied","tr":"elimiz kolumuz bağlı","ex":"Without a registered address, our hands are tied.","def":"we cannot act because of rules or circumstances"},{"en":"free of charge","tr":"ücretsiz","ex":"The personal account comes free of charge.","def":"costing nothing"},{"en":"fall short","tr":"eksik kalmak, yetmemek","ex":"If payments fall short, there's a fee.","def":"to be less than the amount needed"},{"en":"set apart","tr":"farklı kılmak, ayırt etmek","ex":"What sets the business account apart?","def":"to make something different from others"},{"en":"ring-fenced","tr":"ayrı tutulan, korumaya alınmış","ex":"Company money is ring-fenced from personal money.","def":"kept separate and protected for one purpose"},{"en":"pencil in","tr":"geçici olarak plana yazmak","ex":"I'll pencil in an appointment for next week.","def":"to arrange something that may be changed later"},{"en":"as a precaution","tr":"önlem olarak","ex":"The PIN is sent separately as a precaution.","def":"in order to prevent something bad from happening"},{"en":"that's … for you","tr":"işte tam ...'e özgü","ex":"Two letters for one card—that's German thoroughness for you.","def":"used to say something is typical of a person or place"}],"grammar":{"title":"Inversion after 'Not until' and 'Should'","tr":"'Not until' cümle başına gelince ana cümlede yardımcı fiil özneden önce gelir: 'Not until … can we open it.' 'Should it fall short' ise 'If it falls short' demenin resmi halidir.","examples":["Not until your company appears in the register can we open it.","Not until the PIN arrives can you use the card.","Should it fall short, there's a fee of €5."]},"questions":[{"q":"What does the clerk mean by 'our hands are tied'?","options":["The bank is closed","The bank cannot act without a registered address","The clerk is too busy"],"a":1},{"q":"How does the clerk describe the €5 fee?","options":["As modest","As unfair","As temporary"],"a":0},{"q":"What is implied about the business account?","options":["It is cheaper than the personal one","It can be opened immediately","It keeps company money separate but costs more"],"a":2},{"q":"How confident is the speaker about the commercial register?","options":["Fairly confident it will happen within days","Very worried it will take months","Unsure whether the company exists"],"a":0},{"q":"What is the speaker's attitude in the last line?","options":["Angry at the bank","Gently amused by German thoroughness","Confused about the PIN"],"a":1}],"gaps":[{"s":"Without a registered address, our hands are ___.","a":"tied","hint":"bağlı"},{"s":"Not until your company appears in the commercial register ___ we open it.","a":"can","hint":"devrik yapı: yardımcı fiil önce"},{"s":"I'll ___ in another appointment for next week.","a":"pencil","hint":"geçici olarak plana yazmak"},{"s":"The PIN follows in a separate letter as a ___.","a":"precaution","hint":"önlem"}],"order":[{"a":"It's a matter of days rather than weeks."},{"a":"That covers the personal account."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Onu geçen hafta Bürgeramt'ta hallettim.","en":"I sorted that out at the citizens' office last week.","keys":["sorted that out","citizens' office"]},{"tr":"Şirketiniz ticaret siciline girmeden hesabı açamayız.","en":"Not until your company appears in the commercial register can we open the account.","keys":["not until","commercial register","can we open"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Bank clerk","personaTr":"Banka memuru","scene":"Bankadasın. Memur güler yüzlü ve hızlı konuşuyor; sen de rahat ve akıcı cevap veriyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"Morning! I take it you're here to open an account—is it personal or business?","aiTr":"Günaydın! Anladığım kadarıyla hesap açmaya geldiniz; kişisel mi, ticari mi?","hint":"Both, ideally, but I gather the business account will have to wait until my company is registered.","keys":["both","business account","registered"]},{"ai":"That's right, I'm afraid. Have you got your registration certificate handy?","aiTr":"Maalesef doğru. Adres kayıt belgeniz yanınızda mı?","hint":"I have—I sorted it out at the citizens' office last week, and here's my passport and residence permit too.","keys":["sorted it out","citizens' office","residence permit"]},{"ai":"Lovely. Do you intend to bank mostly online, or would you rather come into the branch?","aiTr":"Çok iyi. Bankacılık işlerinizi çoğunlukla internetten mi yapmayı düşünüyorsunuz, yoksa şubeye gelmeyi mi tercih edersiniz?","hint":"Online, without a doubt—with the hours I keep, branch opening times are rather a luxury.","keys":["online","without a doubt","app"]},{"ai":"In that case, you'll get a temporary password by text message to log into the app. Is there anything else I can help with?","aiTr":"O halde uygulamaya girmek için kısa mesajla geçici bir şifre alacaksınız. Yardımcı olabileceğim başka bir şey var mı?","hint":"That's everything for now, thank you—I'll be back next week once the company is on the register.","keys":["that's everything","be back","thank you"]}]}},"ab-04":{"intro":"Komşun Lena ve iş arkadaşın Tom'la sıcak, esprili ve doğal bir sohbet ediyorsun; deyimleri ve nüansları rahatça kullanıyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Lena","en":"Ah, you must be the mystery tenant from the third floor—I'm Lena, the one clomping about directly above you.","tr":"Aa, üçüncü kattaki gizemli kiracı sen olmalısın; ben Lena, tam üstünde güm güm yürüyen kişi."},{"who":"Me","en":"Lovely to finally put a face to the footsteps—I'm {name}, and apologies if my moving boxes kept you up last week.","tr":"Sonunda ayak seslerinin sahibini görmek çok güzel; ben {name}, geçen hafta taşınma kutularım seni uyutmadıysa özür dilerim."},{"who":"Lena","en":"Don't give it a second thought—and isn't it glorious to see the sun, even if it's bitterly cold?","tr":"Hiç kafana takma; hem dondurucu soğuk olsa da güneşi görmek harika değil mi?"},{"who":"Me","en":"After a week of solid rain, I was starting to wonder whether Berlin had a sun at all.","tr":"Bir hafta aralıksız yağmurdan sonra Berlin'in güneşi olup olmadığını merak etmeye başlamıştım."},{"who":"Lena","en":"So, what's lured you to Berlin, of all places?","tr":"Peki onca yer varken seni Berlin'e ne çekti?"},{"who":"Me","en":"I'm from Istanbul, and I'm here to set up the European office of my health-tech startup, which is as thrilling as it is terrifying.","tr":"İstanbulluyum; sağlık teknolojisi girişimimin Avrupa ofisini kurmak için buradayım, bu da ne kadar heyecan vericiyse o kadar korkutucu."},{"who":"Me","en":"What's won me over is how green the city is, though I learned the hard way, with an empty fridge, that everything shuts on Sundays.","tr":"Beni asıl kazanan şehrin bu kadar yeşil olması, ama pazar günleri her şeyin kapandığını boş bir buzdolabıyla acı tecrübeyle öğrendim."},{"who":"Lena","en":"Well, if you can bear the cold, we're having a barbecue in the courtyard on Sunday—the last one before winter sets in.","tr":"Soğuğa dayanabilirsen pazar günü avluda mangal yapıyoruz; kış bastırmadan önceki son mangal."},{"who":"Tom","en":"Morning—so, how did your first proper weekend in Berlin treat you?","tr":"Günaydın; Berlin'deki ilk gerçek hafta sonun nasıl geçti bakalım?"},{"who":"Me","en":"Surprisingly well, actually; the neighbours roped me into a barbecue, and contrary to the stereotype, they couldn't have been warmer.","tr":"Aslında şaşırtıcı derecede iyi; komşular beni bir mangala dahil etti ve klişenin aksine, daha sıcak olamazlardı."},{"who":"Tom","en":"Berliners are a bit like coconuts—hard on the outside, soft on the inside—and speaking of which, fancy a drink on Friday after work?","tr":"Berlinliler biraz hindistancevizine benzer: dışı sert, içi yumuşak; hazır lafı açılmışken, cuma iş çıkışı bir şeyler içmeye ne dersin?"},{"who":"Me","en":"Count me in, provided you let me get the first round.","tr":"Ben de varım, yeter ki ilk içkileri ben ısmarlayayım."}],"vocab":[{"en":"put a face to","tr":"(adını/sesini bildiğin birinin) yüzünü görmek","ex":"It's nice to put a face to the name.","def":"to finally meet someone you have only heard of"},{"en":"keep someone up","tr":"uyutmamak","ex":"I hope the noise didn't keep you up.","def":"to stop someone from going to sleep"},{"en":"don't give it a second thought","tr":"hiç kafana takma","ex":"The boxes? Don't give it a second thought.","def":"don't worry about it at all"},{"en":"lure","tr":"cezbetmek, çekmek","ex":"What's lured you to Berlin?","def":"to attract someone to a place or activity"},{"en":"of all places","tr":"onca yer varken","ex":"Why Berlin, of all places?","def":"used to show surprise at someone's choice of place"},{"en":"win someone over","tr":"birinin gönlünü kazanmak","ex":"The parks have won me over.","def":"to make someone like or support something"},{"en":"set in","tr":"bastırmak, başlamak","ex":"It's the last barbecue before winter sets in.","def":"to begin and seem likely to continue"},{"en":"rope someone into","tr":"birini bir işe dahil etmek","ex":"My neighbours roped me into a barbecue.","def":"to persuade someone to take part in something"},{"en":"count me in","tr":"ben de varım","ex":"A drink on Friday? Count me in.","def":"include me in your plans"},{"en":"get the first round","tr":"ilk içkileri ısmarlamak","ex":"Let me get the first round.","def":"to pay for the first drinks for a group"}],"grammar":{"title":"'As … as it is …': balancing two qualities","tr":"'X as it is Y' kalıbı bir şeyin aynı anda iki (çoğu zaman zıt) özelliğe eşit ölçüde sahip olduğunu zarifçe vurgular: 'as thrilling as it is terrifying' = ne kadar heyecan vericiyse o kadar korkutucu.","examples":["It's as thrilling as it is terrifying.","Berlin is as friendly as it is direct.","The weather was as sunny as it was cold."]},"questions":[{"q":"What is the tone of Lena describing herself as 'clomping about'?","options":["Self-deprecating and playful","Angry","Formal"],"a":0},{"q":"What does 'put a face to the footsteps' imply?","options":["The speaker dislikes Lena","The speaker had heard Lena before meeting her","The speaker had seen photos of Lena"],"a":1},{"q":"How does the speaker feel about opening the European office?","options":["Purely excited","Purely nervous","Excited and nervous at the same time"],"a":2},{"q":"What does Tom's coconut comparison suggest about Berliners?","options":["They seem reserved at first but are warm underneath","They love tropical food","They are friendly at first but cold later"],"a":0},{"q":"What does 'provided you let me get the first round' show about the speaker?","options":["They don't drink","They want to return the kindness","They are reluctant to go"],"a":1}],"gaps":[{"s":"Lovely to finally put a ___ to the footsteps.","a":"face","hint":"yüz"},{"s":"What's ___ me over is how green the city is.","a":"won","hint":"kazanmak"},{"s":"The neighbours ___ me into a barbecue.","a":"roped","hint":"dahil etmek"},{"s":"Count me ___, provided you let me get the first round.","a":"in","hint":"ben de varım"}],"order":[{"a":"I learned the hard way that everything shuts on Sundays."},{"a":"They couldn't have been warmer."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Onca yer varken seni Berlin'e ne çekti?","en":"What's lured you to Berlin, of all places?","keys":["lured","of all places"]},{"tr":"Bu iş ne kadar heyecan vericiyse o kadar da korkutucu.","en":"It's as thrilling as it is terrifying.","keys":["as thrilling as it is terrifying"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Neighbour (Lena)","personaTr":"Komşu (Lena)","scene":"Cumartesi sabahı merdivende üst kattaki esprili komşun Lena ile karşılaşıyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"Ah, the mystery tenant at last! I'm Lena—I'm the one clomping about above you.","aiTr":"Aa, sonunda gizemli kiracı! Ben Lena; üstünde güm güm yürüyen benim.","hint":"Lovely to put a face to the footsteps—I'm {name}, and I hope my moving boxes didn't keep you up.","keys":["put a face","moving boxes","keep you up"]},{"ai":"Not in the least. So what's lured you to Berlin, of all places?","aiTr":"Hiç de değil. Peki onca yer varken seni Berlin'e ne çekti?","hint":"I'm setting up the European office of my health-tech startup, which is as thrilling as it is terrifying.","keys":["European office","startup","thrilling"]},{"ai":"And has the city won you over yet, or is the jury still out?","aiTr":"Peki şehir gönlünü kazandı mı, yoksa hâlâ karar vermedin mi?","hint":"It's well on its way—I adore the parks, though the Sunday closing hours caught me off guard.","keys":["parks","Sunday","caught me off guard"]},{"ai":"Well, we're having a barbecue in the courtyard on Sunday, cold permitting—fancy joining us?","aiTr":"Peki, soğuk izin verirse pazar günü avluda mangal yapıyoruz; bize katılmak ister misin?","hint":"Count me in, and I'll bring some baklava so you can sample a bit of Istanbul.","keys":["count me in","baklava","Istanbul"]}]}},"ab-03":{"intro":"Randevu alıyor ve doktora belirtilerini kesin ve doğal bir dille anlatıyorsun; doktor tedaviyi ve yaşam tarzı tavsiyelerini açıklıyor.","text":[{"who":"Receptionist","en":"Dr Hoffmann's practice, good morning—what can I do for you?","tr":"Dr. Hoffmann'ın muayenehanesi, günaydın, sizin için ne yapabilirim?"},{"who":"Me","en":"I've had a nagging pain in my lower back for about three weeks now, and I was hoping the doctor might be able to fit me in.","tr":"Yaklaşık üç haftadır belimde geçmek bilmeyen bir ağrı var; doktorun beni araya sıkıştırabileceğini umuyordum."},{"who":"Receptionist","en":"Unless it's an emergency, the earliest slot I've got is Thursday at 9:30—and do bring your health insurance card.","tr":"Acil değilse elimdeki en erken boşluk perşembe saat 9.30; sağlık sigortası kartınızı da mutlaka getirin."},{"who":"Doctor","en":"So, talk me through what's been happening.","tr":"Evet, neler olduğunu bana anlatın."},{"who":"Me","en":"What set it off, I think, was working twelve-hour days hunched over a laptop at my kitchen table while we wait for our office furniture.","tr":"Sanırım onu tetikleyen şey, ofis mobilyalarımızı beklerken mutfak masasında dizüstü bilgisayarın üzerine kamburlaşıp günde on iki saat çalışmaktı."},{"who":"Me","en":"It's a dull ache most of the time, but by the evening it's more like a six out of ten, and it flares up after long stretches of sitting.","tr":"Çoğu zaman hafif ama sürekli bir sızı, ama akşama doğru on üzerinden altı gibi oluyor ve uzun süre oturduktan sonra alevleniyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"Not only has it affected my back, but it's also wrecking my sleep—I wake at four and lie there with my mind racing.","tr":"Sadece belimi etkilemekle kalmıyor, uykumu da mahvediyor; dörtte uyanıyorum ve zihnim durmadan çalışırken öylece yatıyorum."},{"who":"Me","en":"I've been taking ibuprofen a few times a week, which takes the edge off but doesn't really solve anything.","tr":"Haftada birkaç kez ibuprofen alıyorum; ağrıyı biraz hafifletiyor ama aslında hiçbir şeyi çözmüyor."},{"who":"Doctor","en":"Having examined you, I can tell you the muscles are extremely tense, though there's nothing to suggest a nerve problem.","tr":"Sizi muayene ettikten sonra şunu söyleyebilirim: kaslarınız aşırı gergin, ama sinirle ilgili bir sorun olduğunu gösteren bir şey yok."},{"who":"Doctor","en":"I'll prescribe an anti-inflammatory gel, which any pharmacy can give you, but medication alone won't fix this.","tr":"İltihap giderici bir jel yazacağım, herhangi bir eczane verebilir; ama yalnızca ilaç bu sorunu çözmez."},{"who":"Doctor","en":"What will make the real difference is getting up every hour, walking for half an hour a day and keeping screens out of the bedroom after ten.","tr":"Asıl farkı yaratacak şey her saat kalkmak, günde yarım saat yürümek ve saat ondan sonra ekranları yatak odasından uzak tutmak."},{"who":"Me","en":"Ironically, I used to preach exactly that to my team, so I suppose I'd better start practising what I preach.","tr":"İşin ironik yanı, ekibime tam olarak bunu öğütlerdim; sanırım artık söylediğimi kendim de yapmaya başlasam iyi olur."}],"vocab":[{"en":"nagging pain","tr":"geçmek bilmeyen ağrı","ex":"I've had a nagging pain in my lower back.","def":"a pain that is not severe but continues for a long time"},{"en":"fit someone in","tr":"araya sıkıştırmak","ex":"Could the doctor fit me in this week?","def":"to find time to see someone in a busy schedule"},{"en":"set something off","tr":"tetiklemek, başlatmak","ex":"Long hours at the laptop set it off.","def":"to cause something to start"},{"en":"hunched over","tr":"üzerine kamburlaşmış","ex":"I spend all day hunched over a laptop.","def":"sitting with your back and shoulders bent forward"},{"en":"dull ache","tr":"hafif ama sürekli sızı","ex":"It's a dull ache most of the time.","def":"a pain that is not sharp but does not go away"},{"en":"flare up","tr":"alevlenmek, depreşmek","ex":"The pain flares up after long meetings.","def":"to suddenly become worse"},{"en":"mind racing","tr":"zihnin durmadan çalışması","ex":"I lie awake with my mind racing.","def":"thinking quickly about many things, so you cannot relax"},{"en":"take the edge off","tr":"hafifletmek, etkisini azaltmak","ex":"Ibuprofen takes the edge off the pain.","def":"to make something unpleasant less strong"},{"en":"medication","tr":"ilaç, ilaç tedavisi","ex":"Medication alone won't fix this.","def":"medicine that a doctor gives you"},{"en":"practise what you preach","tr":"başkasına öğütlediğini kendin de yapmak","ex":"I'd better start practising what I preach.","def":"to do what you tell other people to do"}],"grammar":{"title":"Cleft sentences: What … is/was …","tr":"Bir bilgiyi vurgulamak için cümleyi 'What … is/was …' ile böleriz: 'Long hours set it off' → 'What set it off was long hours.' Konuşmada önemli noktayı öne çıkarır.","examples":["What set it off was working twelve-hour days.","What will make the real difference is getting up every hour.","What worries me most is the lack of sleep."]},"questions":[{"q":"According to the speaker, what triggered the pain?","options":["A sports injury","Long days hunched over a laptop","An old mattress"],"a":1},{"q":"What does 'takes the edge off' suggest about the ibuprofen?","options":["It cures the problem","It has no effect","It reduces the pain a little but doesn't solve it"],"a":2},{"q":"What is the doctor's attitude towards medication?","options":["It helps but isn't enough on its own","It is the only solution","It is dangerous"],"a":0},{"q":"What does the doctor rule out?","options":["Tense muscles","Sleep problems","A nerve problem"],"a":2},{"q":"What is the tone of the speaker's last remark?","options":["Angry","Self-mocking","Fearful"],"a":1}],"gaps":[{"s":"I was hoping the doctor might be able to ___ me in.","a":"fit","hint":"araya sıkıştırmak"},{"s":"It ___ up after long stretches of sitting.","a":"flares","hint":"alevlenmek"},{"s":"Ibuprofen takes the ___ off but doesn't really solve anything.","a":"edge","hint":"kenar (hafifletmek)"},{"s":"I'd better start practising what I ___.","a":"preach","hint":"öğütlemek"}],"order":[{"a":"It's a dull ache most of the time."},{"a":"Medication alone won't fix this."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Onu tetikleyen şey mutfak masasında günde on iki saat çalışmaktı.","en":"What set it off was working twelve hours a day at my kitchen table.","keys":["what set it off","kitchen table"]},{"tr":"Uykumu da mahvediyor; saat dörtte uyanıyorum.","en":"It's also wrecking my sleep, and I wake at four.","keys":["wrecking my sleep","wake at four"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Doctor","personaTr":"Doktor","scene":"Dr. Hoffmann'ın muayene odasındasın. Belirtilerini kesin ve ayrıntılı anlatman gerekiyor.","turns":[{"ai":"Come in, have a seat—so what seems to be the trouble?","aiTr":"Girin, oturun; sorun ne gibi görünüyor?","hint":"I've had a nagging pain in my lower back for about three weeks, and it's starting to wreck my sleep.","keys":["nagging pain","lower back","three weeks"]},{"ai":"Is it a sharp pain, or more of a dull ache, and does anything make it worse?","aiTr":"Keskin bir ağrı mı, yoksa daha çok hafif bir sızı mı; onu kötüleştiren bir şey var mı?","hint":"It's more of a dull ache, but it flares up whenever I've been sitting for hours.","keys":["dull ache","flares up","sitting"]},{"ai":"And how exactly is your sleep affected?","aiTr":"Peki uykunuz tam olarak nasıl etkileniyor?","hint":"I tend to wake at four with my mind racing and simply can't get back to sleep.","keys":["wake at four","mind racing","get back to sleep"]},{"ai":"I'll prescribe a gel, but the real fix is regular movement. Is there anything you'd like to ask me?","aiTr":"Bir jel yazacağım, ama asıl çözüm düzenli hareket. Bana sormak istediğiniz bir şey var mı?","hint":"Just one thing—if it hasn't eased off in a fortnight, should I come back and see you?","keys":["come back","eased off","fortnight"]}]}},"li-03":{"intro":"Enerjiyi bir kaynak gibi yönetmeyi, ilk yılda yaşadığın tükenmişliği ve bugün uyguladığın kuralları incelikli bir dille anlatıyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Me","en":"In my first year as a founder, I was routinely working fourteen-hour days and running on five hours' sleep.","tr":"Kurucu olarak ilk yılımda günde on dört saat çalışmak ve beş saatlik uykuyla ayakta kalmak benim için olağandı."},{"who":"Me","en":"What I failed to notice, at least at first, was how quietly my judgement was deteriorating.","tr":"En azından başta fark edemediğim şey, muhakememin ne kadar sessizce kötüleştiğiydi."},{"who":"Me","en":"A tired brain isn't merely slower; it defaults to the easy answer rather than the right one.","tr":"Yorgun bir beyin sadece yavaşlamakla kalmaz; doğru cevap yerine otomatik olarak kolay cevaba yönelir."},{"who":"Me","en":"Only after a string of poor calls did I realise that energy, not time, was the real bottleneck.","tr":"Ancak bir dizi kötü karardan sonra asıl darboğazın zaman değil, enerji olduğunu fark ettim."},{"who":"Me","en":"Since then, I've built my week around three non-negotiable rules.","tr":"O zamandan beri haftamı pazarlığa kapalı üç kural etrafında kurdum."},{"who":"Me","en":"First, I protect at least seven hours of sleep, which means my inbox goes dark at 10 pm.","tr":"Birincisi, en az yedi saatlik uykumu koruyorum; bu da gelen kutumun gece 10'da kapanması demek."},{"who":"Me","en":"Second, I tackle my most important task first thing in the morning, before meetings start eating into the day.","tr":"İkincisi, en önemli işimi sabah ilk iş olarak, toplantılar günümü yemeye başlamadan hallediyorum."},{"who":"Me","en":"Third, I walk for thirty minutes every day, and it's on those walks that many of my best ideas surface.","tr":"Üçüncüsü, her gün otuz dakika yürüyorum ve en iyi fikirlerimin çoğu tam da bu yürüyüşlerde ortaya çıkıyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"Having seen what chronic exhaustion did to my decision-making, I no longer treat rest as a reward to be earned.","tr":"Kronik yorgunluğun karar verme becerime neler yaptığını gördükten sonra, dinlenmeyi artık hak edilmesi gereken bir ödül olarak görmüyorum."},{"who":"Me","en":"Not only does sleep sharpen my thinking, but it also makes me far easier to work with.","tr":"Uyku sadece düşüncemi keskinleştirmekle kalmıyor, benimle çalışmayı da çok daha kolay hale getiriyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"A startup is a marathon, not a sprint, and a founder who burns out tends to take the company down with them.","tr":"Girişim bir sprint değil, maratondur ve tükenen bir kurucu genellikle şirketi de kendisiyle birlikte batırır."}],"vocab":[{"en":"run on little sleep","tr":"az uykuyla ayakta kalmak","ex":"I was running on five hours' sleep.","def":"to keep going with very little rest"},{"en":"deteriorate","tr":"kötüleşmek","ex":"My judgement was deteriorating.","def":"to become gradually worse"},{"en":"default to","tr":"otomatik olarak ...e yönelmek","ex":"A tired brain defaults to the easy answer.","def":"to choose something automatically, without thinking"},{"en":"poor call","tr":"kötü karar","ex":"I made some poor calls that year.","def":"a bad decision, especially one made quickly"},{"en":"bottleneck","tr":"darboğaz","ex":"Energy, not time, was the real bottleneck.","def":"the one thing that slows down a whole process"},{"en":"non-negotiable","tr":"pazarlığa kapalı","ex":"Seven hours of sleep is non-negotiable for me.","def":"fixed and not open to discussion or change"},{"en":"eat into","tr":"...den yemek, azaltmak","ex":"Meetings start eating into the day.","def":"to use up part of something valuable, such as time"},{"en":"surface","tr":"ortaya çıkmak","ex":"My best ideas surface on long walks.","def":"to appear or become noticeable"},{"en":"burn out","tr":"tükenmek","ex":"A founder who burns out can sink the company.","def":"to become exhausted or ill from working too hard"},{"en":"a reward to be earned","tr":"hak edilmesi gereken bir ödül","ex":"Rest is not a reward to be earned.","def":"something you only get after you have worked hard enough"}],"grammar":{"title":"Inversion after 'Only after' and 'Not only'","tr":"Vurgu için sınırlayıcı ya da olumsuz bir ifadeyle (Only after, Not only) başlayan cümlelerde yardımcı fiil özneden önce gelir: 'Only after … did I realise', 'Not only does sleep …'.","examples":["Only after a string of poor calls did I realise that energy was the real bottleneck.","Not only does sleep sharpen my thinking, but it also makes me easier to work with.","Only then did I change my routine."]},"questions":[{"q":"What did the founder fail to notice at first?","options":["That the team was unhappy","That their judgement was slowly getting worse","That the market was changing"],"a":1},{"q":"What does the founder now see as the real bottleneck?","options":["Time","Money","Energy","Meetings"],"a":2},{"q":"What is implied by 'my inbox goes dark at 10 pm'?","options":["The founder stops dealing with email at 10 pm","The founder's laptop breaks every night","The founder reads emails in the dark"],"a":0},{"q":"How has the founder's attitude to rest changed?","options":["Rest is now a reward to be earned","Rest is still a waste of time","Rest is now treated as essential, not as a reward"],"a":2},{"q":"What is the tone of the final sentence?","options":["Light-hearted and joking","Cautionary","Sarcastic","Indifferent"],"a":1}],"gaps":[{"s":"A tired brain ___ to the easy answer rather than the right one.","a":"defaults","hint":"otomatik olarak yönelir"},{"s":"Energy, not time, was the real ___.","a":"bottleneck","hint":"darboğaz"},{"s":"Meetings start eating ___ the day.","a":"into","hint":"...den yemek"},{"s":"It's on those walks that many of my best ideas ___.","a":"surface","hint":"ortaya çıkar"}],"order":[{"a":"A tired brain isn't merely slower."},{"a":"My inbox goes dark at 10 pm."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Ancak bir dizi kötü karardan sonra enerjinin asıl darboğaz olduğunu fark ettim.","en":"Only after a string of poor calls did I realise that energy was the real bottleneck.","keys":["only after","did i realise","bottleneck"]},{"tr":"Artık dinlenmeyi hak edilmesi gereken bir ödül olarak görmüyorum.","en":"I no longer treat rest as a reward to be earned.","keys":["no longer","reward"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Young founder","personaTr":"Genç kurucu","scene":"Tükenmenin eşiğindeki genç bir kurucu, geri adım atmanın ekibi hayal kırıklığına uğratacağından korkuyor. Deneyiminden yola çıkarak onu ikna ediyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"Honestly, I'm running on fumes, but stepping back feels like letting the team down.","aiTr":"Açıkçası son damla benzinle gidiyorum ama geri çekilmek ekibi yüzüstü bırakmak gibi geliyor.","hint":"I know that feeling, but what really lets the team down is a founder whose judgement is deteriorating.","keys":["lets the team down","judgement","deteriorating"]},{"ai":"Fair point. Where would you even start?","aiTr":"Haklısın. Nereden başlardın ki?","hint":"With sleep: at least seven hours is non-negotiable for me, and my inbox goes dark at 10 pm.","keys":["non-negotiable","seven hours","inbox","10 pm"]},{"ai":"My days just get swallowed by meetings, though.","aiTr":"Ama günlerim toplantıların içinde kaybolup gidiyor.","hint":"Then ring-fence the first hours of the morning for your most important task, before meetings start eating into the day.","keys":["ring-fence","most important task","eating into"]},{"ai":"And how do you actually switch off?","aiTr":"Peki sen gerçekten nasıl kafanı boşaltıyorsun?","hint":"I walk for thirty minutes every day, and it's often on those walks that my best ideas surface.","keys":["walk","thirty minutes","best ideas","surface"]}]}},"ai-05":{"intro":"Satın alma direktörünün fiyat, veri koruma ve devreye alma kaygılarını ikna edici ve resmî bir dille karşılıyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Buyer","en":"I'll be candid: on paper, your audiometer looks expensive next to the conventional units we've been using for years.","tr":"Açık konuşacağım: Kâğıt üzerinde odyometreniz, yıllardır kullandığımız klasik cihazların yanında pahalı görünüyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"That's a fair point, and I'd rather address it head-on than gloss over it.","tr":"Haklı bir nokta ve bunu geçiştirmek yerine doğrudan ele almayı tercih ederim."},{"who":"Me","en":"The device itself is €4,000, with a software subscription of €99 per month per clinic.","tr":"Cihazın kendisi 4.000 euro, buna klinik başına ayda 99 euroluk yazılım aboneliği ekleniyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"What really shifts the economics, though, is that the test runs without an audiologist in the room.","tr":"Ancak ekonomik dengeyi asıl değiştiren şey, testin odada bir odyolog olmadan yapılabilmesi."},{"who":"Me","en":"Freed from routine screenings, your specialists can focus on the complex cases that genuinely require their expertise.","tr":"Rutin taramalardan kurtulan uzmanlarınız, gerçekten uzmanlıklarını gerektiren karmaşık vakalara odaklanabilir."},{"who":"Buyer","en":"Our data protection officer will have concerns about patient data leaving the building.","tr":"Veri koruma görevlimiz, hasta verilerinin binadan çıkması konusunda kaygılanacaktır."},{"who":"Me","en":"They needn't worry, since the AI runs entirely on the device and the system works offline.","tr":"Endişelenmelerine gerek yok, çünkü yapay zekâ tamamen cihaz üzerinde çalışıyor ve sistem internetsiz de çalışabiliyor."},{"who":"Buyer","en":"And how disruptive would the rollout be for our staff?","tr":"Peki devreye alma süreci personelimizin işini ne kadar aksatır?"},{"who":"Me","en":"Hardly at all: installation takes about an hour, and we train your team on the same day.","tr":"Neredeyse hiç: Kurulum yaklaşık bir saat sürüyor ve ekibinizi aynı gün eğitiyoruz."},{"who":"Me","en":"Should anything go wrong, you're covered by a two-year warranty, and most issues can be resolved remotely through a software update.","tr":"Bir sorun çıkarsa iki yıllık garanti kapsamındasınız ve çoğu sorun bir yazılım güncellemesiyle uzaktan çözülebiliyor."},{"who":"Buyer","en":"It all sounds compelling, but I'd need to see it working in our own setting before taking it to the board.","tr":"Hepsi ikna edici görünüyor ama yönetim kuruluna götürmeden önce cihazı kendi ortamımızda çalışırken görmem gerekir."},{"who":"Me","en":"Which is exactly why we offer a free one-month trial, so you can judge it on your own patients rather than on our word.","tr":"Tam da bu yüzden bir aylık ücretsiz deneme sunuyoruz; böylece bizim sözümüze göre değil, kendi hastalarınızla değerlendirebilirsiniz."}],"vocab":[{"en":"be candid","tr":"açık sözlü olmak","ex":"I'll be candid with you about the price.","def":"to speak honestly and directly"},{"en":"address something head-on","tr":"bir konuyu doğrudan ele almak","ex":"I'd rather address the price head-on.","def":"to deal with a problem directly, without avoiding it"},{"en":"gloss over","tr":"geçiştirmek, üstünkörü geçmek","ex":"I don't want to gloss over your concerns.","def":"to avoid dealing with something by treating it as unimportant"},{"en":"shift the economics","tr":"ekonomik dengeyi değiştirmek","ex":"Removing the need for an expert shifts the economics.","def":"to change how costs and benefits compare"},{"en":"routine screening","tr":"rutin tarama","ex":"Your specialists are freed from routine screenings.","def":"a standard test done on many people to find problems early"},{"en":"data protection officer","tr":"veri koruma görevlisi","ex":"Our data protection officer will ask about patient data.","def":"the person responsible for how an organization handles personal data"},{"en":"rollout","tr":"devreye alma, yaygınlaştırma","ex":"The rollout will take less than a day.","def":"the process of introducing a new product or system"},{"en":"disruptive","tr":"işleri aksatan","ex":"How disruptive would the installation be?","def":"causing problems that interrupt normal activity"},{"en":"compelling","tr":"ikna edici","ex":"It all sounds compelling.","def":"very convincing"},{"en":"take something to the board","tr":"bir şeyi yönetim kuruluna götürmek","ex":"I'd need to see it working before taking it to the board.","def":"to present a proposal to the people who make final decisions"}],"grammar":{"title":"Inverted conditionals: Should anything go wrong…","tr":"Resmî dilde 'If anything goes wrong' yerine 'Should anything go wrong' denebilir: 'if' düşer, 'should' başa gelir ve fiil yalın kalır. Kibar ve profesyonel bir tondur.","examples":["Should anything go wrong, you're covered by a two-year warranty.","Should you need more training, we can arrange it remotely.","Should the trial go well, we can discuss a full rollout."]},"questions":[{"q":"How does the founder respond to the price objection?","options":["By offering an immediate discount","By acknowledging it and reframing the costs","By changing the subject","By criticizing other audiometers"],"a":1},{"q":"What does the founder imply about specialists' time today?","options":["Much of it goes on routine tests the device could handle","It is cheaper than the device","It won't be affected by the device"],"a":0},{"q":"Why should the data protection officer be reassured?","options":["The data is encrypted in the cloud","The hospital doesn't need to store any results","The AI runs on the device and the system works offline"],"a":2},{"q":"What is the buyer's attitude by the end of the conversation?","options":["Dismissive","Annoyed","Fully convinced","Interested but cautious"],"a":3},{"q":"What does 'rather than on our word' suggest?","options":["The founder doesn't trust the buyer","The founder is confident the product can prove itself","The trial will cost extra","The founder has no data"],"a":1}],"gaps":[{"s":"I'd rather address it ___ than gloss over it.","a":"head-on","hint":"doğrudan"},{"s":"___ anything go wrong, you're covered by a two-year warranty.","a":"Should","hint":"olur da (devrik koşul)"},{"s":"___ from routine screenings, your specialists can focus on complex cases.","a":"Freed","hint":"kurtulan, serbest kalan"},{"s":"How ___ would the rollout be for our staff?","a":"disruptive","hint":"işleri aksatan"}],"order":[{"a":"Installation takes about an hour."},{"a":"The AI runs entirely on the device."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Kâğıt üzerinde odyometreniz pahalı görünüyor.","en":"On paper, your audiometer looks expensive.","keys":["on paper","looks expensive"]},{"tr":"Ekonomik dengeyi asıl değiştiren şey, testin odada bir uzman olmadan yapılabilmesi.","en":"What really shifts the economics is that the test runs without an expert in the room.","keys":["what really shifts","without an expert"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Head of Procurement","personaTr":"Satın alma direktörü","scene":"Uluslararası bir özel hastane grubunun satın alma direktörü, teklifini yönetim kuruluna götürmeden önce sorguluyor.","turns":[{"ai":"I'll be candid: next to conventional audiometers, your price is hard to justify. Convince me.","aiTr":"Açık konuşacağım: Klasik odyometrelerin yanında fiyatınızı savunmak zor. Beni ikna edin.","hint":"That's a fair point, but what really shifts the economics is that the test runs without an audiologist in the room, so your specialists can focus on complex cases.","keys":["shifts the economics","without an audiologist","complex cases"]},{"ai":"Our data protection officer will ask where patient data goes. What do I tell them?","aiTr":"Veri koruma görevlimiz hasta verilerinin nereye gittiğini soracak. Ona ne söyleyeyim?","hint":"Tell them the AI runs entirely on the device and the system works offline, so patient data never has to leave the building.","keys":["on the device","offline","leave the building"]},{"ai":"How reliable are the results compared with a human audiologist?","aiTr":"Sonuçlar bir odyologla karşılaştırıldığında ne kadar güvenilir?","hint":"In a blind study at two university hospitals, our results matched a trained audiologist's in 94% of cases.","keys":["94","blind study","matched"]},{"ai":"Supposing we went ahead, what would you propose as a first step?","aiTr":"Diyelim ki ilerlemeye karar verdik, ilk adım olarak ne önerirsiniz?","hint":"I'd propose a free one-month trial, so you can judge it in your own setting before taking it to the board.","keys":["trial","own setting","board"]}]}},"li-02":{"intro":"Bir 'hayır'ın ardındaki gerçek nedenleri çözümleyip itirazları nasıl fırsata çevirdiğini incelikli bir dille anlatıyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Me","en":"If there's one thing I've learned from selling, it's that a 'no' is rarely about the product.","tr":"Satış yaparken öğrendiğim bir şey varsa, o da bir 'hayır'ın nadiren ürünle ilgili olduğudur."},{"who":"Me","en":"More often than not, it comes down to one of three things: trust, understanding or timing.","tr":"Çoğu zaman mesele üç şeyden birine dayanır: güven, anlama ya da zamanlama."},{"who":"Me","en":"Trust is rarely won in a single meeting; it accumulates through small signals, like a clean website, a prompt reply or a customer willing to vouch for you.","tr":"Güven nadiren tek bir toplantıda kazanılır; derli toplu bir web sitesi, hızlı bir cevap ya da size kefil olmaya hazır bir müşteri gibi küçük işaretlerle birikir."},{"who":"Me","en":"Understanding, meanwhile, hinges on clarity.","tr":"Anlaşılmak ise netliğe bağlıdır."},{"who":"Me","en":"Should a buyer need an engineer to decipher your pitch, you've already lost them.","tr":"Bir alıcı sunumunuzu çözmek için mühendise ihtiyaç duyuyorsa, onu çoktan kaybetmişsinizdir."},{"who":"Me","en":"Timing is the hardest to read, because what ultimately drives change is pain.","tr":"Zamanlamayı okumak en zorudur, çünkü değişimi asıl tetikleyen şey sıkıntıdır."},{"who":"Me","en":"People rarely abandon a familiar process until it becomes more painful to keep it than to replace it.","tr":"İnsanlar alışık oldukları bir süreci, onu sürdürmek değiştirmekten daha zahmetli hale gelene kadar nadiren bırakır."},{"who":"Me","en":"Before every meeting, then, I put three questions to myself: why should they trust me, will they grasp this in a minute, and where does it hurt today?","tr":"Bu yüzden her toplantıdan önce kendime üç soru sorarım: bana neden güvensinler, bunu bir dakikada kavrayabilirler mi ve bugün canlarını sıkan ne?"},{"who":"Me","en":"Last year, a clinic that had seemed genuinely keen turned us down.","tr":"Geçen yıl, gerçekten istekli görünen bir klinik bizi geri çevirdi."},{"who":"Me","en":"Having stayed in touch, we asked again three months later, by which point their waiting list had spiralled and the timing was finally right.","tr":"İletişimi koparmadığımız için üç ay sonra tekrar sorduk; o noktada bekleme listeleri kontrolden çıkmıştı ve zamanlama nihayet doğruydu."},{"who":"Me","en":"Not only does a 'no' rarely mean 'never', but it often tells you exactly what to fix.","tr":"Bir 'hayır' nadiren 'asla' anlamına gelmekle kalmaz, çoğu zaman tam olarak neyi düzeltmeniz gerektiğini de söyler."},{"who":"Me","en":"A 'no' today, in other words, is very often just a 'not yet'.","tr":"Başka bir deyişle, bugünkü bir 'hayır' çoğu zaman sadece bir 'henüz değil'dir."}],"vocab":[{"en":"come down to","tr":"özünde ...e dayanmak","ex":"Most refusals come down to trust, understanding or timing.","def":"to be mainly about one particular thing"},{"en":"vouch for","tr":"kefil olmak","ex":"A customer willing to vouch for you is worth more than an advert.","def":"to say that someone is reliable or good"},{"en":"hinge on","tr":"...e bağlı olmak","ex":"Understanding hinges on clarity.","def":"to depend completely on something"},{"en":"decipher","tr":"çözmek, sökmek","ex":"No buyer should have to decipher your pitch.","def":"to work out the meaning of something hard to understand"},{"en":"abandon a process","tr":"bir süreci bırakmak","ex":"People rarely abandon a familiar process.","def":"to stop using a way of working completely"},{"en":"grasp","tr":"kavramak","ex":"Will they grasp this in a minute?","def":"to understand something fully"},{"en":"keen","tr":"istekli, hevesli","ex":"The clinic seemed genuinely keen at first.","def":"very interested and eager"},{"en":"spiral","tr":"kontrolden çıkmak, hızla artmak","ex":"Their waiting list had spiralled.","def":"to increase quickly and get out of control"},{"en":"turn down","tr":"geri çevirmek","ex":"A clinic turned us down last year.","def":"to refuse an offer"},{"en":"more often than not","tr":"çoğu zaman","ex":"More often than not, the real problem is timing.","def":"usually; in more than half of cases"}],"grammar":{"title":"Inversion for emphasis and conditions","tr":"Resmî ve vurgulu konuşmada yardımcı fiil özneden önce gelir. 'Should a buyer need…' = 'If a buyer needs…' anlamındadır; 'Not only does…' ise olumsuz bir ifadeyle başlayan vurgulu bir yapıdır.","examples":["Should a buyer need an engineer to decipher your pitch, you've already lost them.","Not only does a 'no' rarely mean 'never', but it often tells you what to fix.","Rarely is trust won in a single meeting."]},"questions":[{"q":"According to the speaker, what usually lies behind a 'no'?","options":["A weak product","Trust, understanding or timing","An unrealistic price","Bad luck"],"a":1},{"q":"What does the speaker imply about trust?","options":["It builds up gradually through small details","It depends mainly on a big marketing budget","It can be won in one strong meeting"],"a":0},{"q":"Why did the clinic eventually say yes?","options":["The device became cheaper","A competitor closed down","Their waiting list had spiralled, so the timing was right"],"a":2},{"q":"What is the speaker's attitude towards rejection?","options":["Bitter and defensive","Indifferent","Anxious","Pragmatic and patient"],"a":3},{"q":"What does 'you've already lost them' suggest about complicated pitches?","options":["The buyer stops listening before the pitch is over","Engineers are difficult buyers","The price must be lowered"],"a":0}],"gaps":[{"s":"More often than not, a refusal comes ___ to trust, understanding or timing.","a":"down","hint":"özünde ...e dayanır"},{"s":"A customer willing to ___ for you is a powerful signal.","a":"vouch","hint":"kefil olmak"},{"s":"Understanding ___ on clarity.","a":"hinges","hint":"bağlıdır"},{"s":"By then, their waiting list had ___.","a":"spiralled","hint":"kontrolden çıkmıştı"}],"order":[{"a":"Trust is rarely won in a single meeting."},{"a":"What ultimately drives change is pain."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Güven tek bir toplantıda nadiren kazanılır.","en":"Trust is rarely won in a single meeting.","keys":["rarely won","single meeting"]},{"tr":"Değişimi asıl tetikleyen şey sıkıntıdır.","en":"What really drives change is pain.","keys":["drives change","pain"]},{"tr":"Bugünkü bir 'hayır' çoğu zaman sadece 'henüz değil' demektir.","en":"A 'no' today is often just a 'not yet'.","keys":["not yet","often"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Hesitant clinic owner","personaTr":"Kararsız klinik sahibi","scene":"İlgili ama temkinli bir klinik sahibi kararı erteliyor. Asıl itirazı nazikçe ortaya çıkarmalı, riski azaltmalı ve kapıyı açık bırakmalısın.","turns":[{"ai":"I'm genuinely impressed by the device, but I can't help feeling the timing isn't quite right for us.","aiTr":"Cihazdan gerçekten etkilendim ama zamanlamanın bizim için pek uygun olmadığını hissetmeden edemiyorum.","hint":"I appreciate your honesty. Would you mind telling me what's weighing on you most at the moment?","keys":["appreciate","weighing on you","at the moment","honesty"]},{"ai":"Our patients are waiting six weeks for a hearing test, yet overhauling our workflow feels like a gamble.","aiTr":"Hastalarımız işitme testi için altı hafta bekliyor; yine de iş akışımızı baştan değiştirmek kumar gibi geliyor.","hint":"That's understandable. What if you trialled it free for a month alongside your current process, so there's nothing to lose?","keys":["free for a month","alongside","nothing to lose"]},{"ai":"And what happens if my audiologists don't take to it?","aiTr":"Peki odyologlarım ısınamazsa ne olacak?","hint":"Then you walk away at the end of the month, and in the meantime our remote support team will help them settle in.","keys":["walk away","remote support","settle in"]},{"ai":"Let me sleep on it and talk it through with the team.","aiTr":"Bir gece düşüneyim ve ekiple konuşayım.","hint":"Of course, take your time. I'll send a short summary for your team and follow up next week.","keys":["take your time","summary","follow up","next week"]}]}},"st-04":{"intro":"Açık sözlü bir distribütörle, ilişkiyi zedelemeden sınırlarını koruyarak müzakere ediyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Partner","en":"To be upfront with you, our standard commission is 25%, and that's what we'd normally expect.","tr":"Açık konuşayım, standart komisyonumuz yüzde 25 ve normalde beklediğimiz de bu."},{"who":"Me","en":"I appreciate your candour, and I'll be equally direct: at 25%, the numbers simply don't work for us.","tr":"Açık sözlülüğünüz için teşekkürler, ben de aynı şekilde net olayım: yüzde 25'te rakamlar bizim için tutmuyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"Given what each device costs us to build, anything above 15% would leave us too thin a margin to reinvest.","tr":"Her cihazın bize üretim maliyeti düşünüldüğünde, yüzde 15'in üzerindeki her oran yeniden yatırım yapmak için bize çok ince bir marj bırakır."},{"who":"Partner","en":"Fifteen barely covers our marketing spend, let alone the cost of building a sales network in a new category.","tr":"On beş, yeni bir kategoride satış ağı kurmanın maliyeti şöyle dursun, pazarlama harcamamızı bile zor karşılar."},{"who":"Me","en":"Then let me suggest a middle ground: 20% for the first year, with a formal review after twelve months.","tr":"O zaman bir orta yol önereyim: ilk yıl yüzde 20, on iki ay sonra da resmî bir değerlendirme."},{"who":"Me","en":"Should the volumes justify it, we'd be more than willing to revisit the terms.","tr":"Satış hacimleri bunu haklı çıkarırsa şartları yeniden ele almaya fazlasıyla hazırız."},{"who":"Partner","en":"That's workable, though only if we're granted exclusive rights in Germany.","tr":"Bu uygulanabilir, ama ancak bize Almanya'da münhasır haklar verilirse."},{"who":"Me","en":"Exclusivity is very much on the table, but it would need to be tied to a minimum sales target.","tr":"Münhasırlık kesinlikle masada, ama bir minimum satış hedefine bağlanması gerekir."},{"who":"Me","en":"What we can't do is lock up a market as important as Germany with a partner who isn't moving units.","tr":"Yapamayacağımız şey, Almanya kadar önemli bir pazarı ürün satamayan bir ortağa bağlamak."},{"who":"Partner","en":"Fair enough; let's have our lawyers draft the terms and aim to sign next week.","tr":"Makul; avukatlarımız şartları taslak haline getirsin ve gelecek hafta imzalamayı hedefleyelim."},{"who":"Me","en":"Sounds good, and I'm glad we've found an arrangement that works for both sides.","tr":"Kulağa iyi geliyor; iki taraf için de işe yarayan bir düzenleme bulduğumuza sevindim."}],"vocab":[{"en":"be upfront","tr":"baştan açık sözlü olmak","ex":"To be upfront with you, our commission is 25%.","def":"to be honest and clear from the start"},{"en":"candour","tr":"açık sözlülük","ex":"I appreciate your candour.","def":"honesty in what you say, even when it is uncomfortable"},{"en":"thin margin","tr":"ince (düşük) kâr marjı","ex":"That would leave us too thin a margin.","def":"a very small profit on each sale"},{"en":"let alone","tr":"...şöyle dursun","ex":"It barely covers marketing, let alone a sales network.","def":"used to say the second thing is even less possible than the first"},{"en":"middle ground","tr":"orta yol","ex":"Let me suggest a middle ground.","def":"a compromise between two positions"},{"en":"revisit the terms","tr":"şartları yeniden ele almak","ex":"We'd be willing to revisit the terms.","def":"to discuss the conditions of a deal again"},{"en":"on the table","tr":"masada, görüşülebilir","ex":"Exclusivity is very much on the table.","def":"available to be discussed or offered"},{"en":"be tied to","tr":"...e bağlı olmak","ex":"It would need to be tied to a sales target.","def":"to depend on a particular condition"},{"en":"move units","tr":"ürün satmak","ex":"We need a partner who is moving units.","def":"(informal) to sell products in good numbers"},{"en":"lock up a market","tr":"bir pazarı tek bir tarafa bağlamak","ex":"We can't lock up Germany with the wrong partner.","def":"to give one partner control of a market so nobody else can sell there"}],"grammar":{"title":"Inversion with 'Should': Should the volumes justify it…","tr":"'If' yerine 'Should' ile başlayan devrik yapı koşulu daha resmî ve nazik kılar: 'Should the volumes justify it' = 'If the volumes justify it'. Müzakerede esnek ama kontrollü görünmeni sağlar.","examples":["Should the volumes justify it, we'd be more than willing to revisit the terms.","Should you reach the target, exclusivity is yours.","Should anything change, we can talk again."]},"questions":[{"q":"How does the speaker respond to the distributor's frankness?","options":["By matching it with equal directness","By ending the meeting","By ignoring the offer"],"a":0},{"q":"According to the speaker, why is anything above 15% a problem?","options":["The distributor is new","The margin would be too thin to reinvest","They have a better offer elsewhere"],"a":1},{"q":"What does 'let alone' imply in the distributor's reply?","options":["Building a sales network is cheap","Marketing costs are falling","If 15% doesn't even cover marketing, a sales network is out of the question"],"a":2},{"q":"What attitude does the speaker show toward exclusivity?","options":["Flatly opposed to it","Open to it, but only on performance-based terms","Indifferent to it"],"a":1},{"q":"What does the speaker imply with 'a partner who isn't moving units'?","options":["They don't want to give a key market to an underperforming partner","They think the distributor is lazy","They want to sell in Germany themselves right now"],"a":0}],"gaps":[{"s":"I appreciate your ___.","a":"candour","hint":"açık sözlülük"},{"s":"It barely covers our marketing spend, let ___ a sales network.","a":"alone","hint":"...şöyle dursun"},{"s":"Exclusivity is very much on the ___.","a":"table","hint":"masa (görüşülebilir)"},{"s":"Let me suggest a middle ___.","a":"ground","hint":"orta yol"}],"order":[{"a":"Let me suggest a middle ground."},{"a":"Exclusivity is very much on the table."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Satış hacimleri bunu haklı çıkarırsa şartları yeniden ele almaya fazlasıyla hazırız.","en":"Should the volumes justify it, we'd be more than willing to revisit the terms.","keys":["revisit the terms","volumes"]},{"tr":"Münhasırlığın bir minimum satış hedefine bağlanması gerekir.","en":"Exclusivity would need to be tied to a minimum sales target.","keys":["tied to","minimum sales target"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Distributor","personaTr":"Distribütör","scene":"Almanya pazarını iyi tanıyan, açık sözlü bir Hollandalı distribütörle şartları masaya yatırıyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"To be upfront with you, our standard commission is 25%.","aiTr":"Açık konuşayım, standart komisyonumuz yüzde 25.","hint":"I appreciate your candour, and I'll be equally direct: at 25%, the numbers simply don't work for us.","keys":["candour","direct","don't work"]},{"ai":"Fifteen barely covers our marketing spend, let alone building a sales network.","aiTr":"On beş, satış ağı kurmak şöyle dursun, pazarlama harcamamızı bile zor karşılar.","hint":"Then let me suggest a middle ground: 20% for the first year, with a formal review after twelve months.","keys":["middle ground","20%","review"]},{"ai":"And if sales turn out better than expected?","aiTr":"Peki satışlar beklenenden iyi giderse?","hint":"Should the volumes justify it, we'd be more than willing to revisit the terms.","keys":["should the volumes","revisit","willing"]},{"ai":"We'd need exclusive rights in Germany to make the investment worthwhile.","aiTr":"Yatırımı değerli kılmak için Almanya'da münhasır haklara ihtiyacımız olur.","hint":"Exclusivity is very much on the table, but it would need to be tied to a minimum sales target.","keys":["on the table","tied to","sales target"]}]}},"st-05":{"intro":"Bir şikayeti nasıl ele aldığını, nüanslı ve profesyonel bir dille anlatıyorsun.","text":[{"en":"Yesterday we had a call from a hospital in Izmir, one of our paying customers, and it wasn't a happy one.","tr":"Dün, ücret ödeyen müşterilerimizden biri olan İzmir'deki bir hastaneden bir telefon aldık ve pek hoş bir konuşma değildi."},{"en":"Halfway through a hearing test, their audiometer had frozen, leaving the screen completely black and a patient sitting there with headphones on.","tr":"Odyometreleri bir işitme testinin ortasında donmuş, ekran tamamen kararmış ve hasta kulaklıklar başında öylece kalmıştı."},{"en":"The doctor, with a waiting room full of patients, was understandably furious.","tr":"Bekleme salonu hasta dolu olan doktor, haklı olarak çok öfkeliydi."},{"en":"What I did first was simply apologise and thank her for raising it straight away instead of quietly losing faith in us.","tr":"İlk yaptığım şey sadece özür dilemek ve bize sessizce güvenini kaybetmek yerine sorunu hemen dile getirdiği için ona teşekkür etmek oldu."},{"en":"Rather than jumping to conclusions, I asked a few targeted questions to pin down exactly what had gone wrong.","tr":"Aceleyle sonuca varmak yerine, tam olarak neyin yanlış gittiğini saptamak için birkaç hedefli soru sordum."},{"en":"It quickly became clear that we were dealing with a software bug, not a hardware fault.","tr":"Kısa sürede bir donanım arızasıyla değil, bir yazılım hatasıyla karşı karşıya olduğumuz netleşti."},{"en":"Our engineer pushed an update remotely, and within two hours the device was back up and running.","tr":"Mühendisimiz uzaktan bir güncelleme gönderdi ve iki saat içinde cihaz yeniden çalışır hâle geldi."},{"en":"I then made a point of calling the doctor back myself to make sure everything was working properly.","tr":"Ardından her şeyin düzgün çalıştığından emin olmak için doktoru bizzat geri aramaya özen gösterdim."},{"en":"Not only does a follow-up call close the loop, but it also shows the customer that someone is genuinely accountable.","tr":"Takip araması yalnızca süreci kapatmakla kalmaz, müşteriye birinin gerçekten sorumluluğu üstlendiğini de gösterir."},{"en":"Handled badly, a complaint like this can quietly end a relationship.","tr":"Kötü yönetilen böyle bir şikayet, bir ilişkiyi sessizce bitirebilir."},{"en":"Handled well, it can actually leave the relationship stronger than it was before.","tr":"İyi yönetildiğinde ise ilişkiyi eskisinden bile güçlü bırakabilir."}],"vocab":[{"en":"raise an issue","tr":"(bir sorunu) dile getirmek","ex":"Thank you for raising it straight away.","def":"to mention a problem so that it can be dealt with"},{"en":"lose faith in","tr":"...e güvenini kaybetmek","ex":"Customers quietly lose faith in suppliers who don't respond.","def":"to stop trusting or believing in someone"},{"en":"jump to conclusions","tr":"aceleyle sonuca varmak","ex":"Don't jump to conclusions before you have the facts.","def":"to decide something too quickly without knowing all the facts"},{"en":"pin down","tr":"kesin olarak saptamak","ex":"We asked targeted questions to pin down the cause.","def":"to find out exactly what something is"},{"en":"hardware fault","tr":"donanım arızası","ex":"It wasn't a hardware fault after all.","def":"a problem with the physical parts of a device"},{"en":"push an update","tr":"(uzaktan) güncelleme göndermek","ex":"Our engineer pushed an update remotely.","def":"to send new software to a device from a distance"},{"en":"back up and running","tr":"yeniden çalışır hâlde","ex":"Within two hours, the device was back up and running.","def":"working normally again after a problem"},{"en":"make a point of","tr":"...e özen göstermek","ex":"I made a point of calling her back myself.","def":"to make a special effort to do something"},{"en":"close the loop","tr":"süreci tamamlamak, geri dönüş yapmak","ex":"A follow-up call closes the loop with the customer.","def":"to finish a process by confirming the result with the people involved"},{"en":"accountable","tr":"hesap verebilir, sorumlu","ex":"Customers want to know that someone is accountable.","def":"responsible for something and ready to explain it"}],"grammar":{"title":"Participle clauses: Handled well, ...","tr":"Participle clause (V3 ya da -ing ile başlayan yan cümle) cümleyi kısaltır ve daha akıcı yapar. 'Handled well' = 'If it is handled well'. Yan cümlenin öznesi ana cümleninkiyle aynı olmalı.","examples":["Handled badly, a complaint can quietly end a relationship.","Handled well, it can leave the relationship stronger.","The audiometer froze, leaving the screen completely black."]},"questions":[{"q":"What does 'it wasn't a happy one' suggest about the call?","options":["The doctor was calling to complain","The doctor wanted to order more devices","The phone line was bad"],"a":0},{"q":"Why does the speaker thank the doctor?","options":["For paying on time","For raising the problem instead of quietly losing faith","For fixing the device herself"],"a":1},{"q":"What does 'rather than jumping to conclusions' imply about the speaker?","options":["They were in a hurry","They blamed the engineer","They prefer to get the facts before acting"],"a":2},{"q":"According to the speaker, what is the main value of a follow-up call?","options":["It lets you sell more products","It shows that someone is accountable","It replaces the need for an update"],"a":1},{"q":"What is the speaker's overall attitude to complaints?","options":["They should be avoided at all costs","They are a sign the product has failed","They are mainly the engineers' problem","They can be a chance to strengthen a relationship"],"a":3}],"gaps":[{"s":"Rather than jumping to ___, I asked a few targeted questions.","a":"conclusions","hint":"aceleyle sonuca varmak"},{"s":"I asked questions to pin ___ exactly what had gone wrong.","a":"down","hint":"saptamak"},{"s":"I made a ___ of calling the doctor back myself.","a":"point","hint":"özen göstermek"},{"s":"___ well, a complaint can leave the relationship stronger.","a":"Handled","hint":"yönetildiğinde"}],"order":[{"a":"We were dealing with a software bug."},{"a":"Within two hours the device was back up and running."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Sorunu hemen dile getirdiğiniz için teşekkürler.","en":"Thank you for raising it straight away.","keys":["raising it","straight away"]},{"tr":"Kötü yönetilirse, bir şikayet bir ilişkiyi bitirebilir.","en":"Handled badly, a complaint can end a relationship.","keys":["handled badly","end a relationship"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Angry doctor","personaTr":"Kızgın doktor","scene":"İzmir'deki bir hastanenin doktoru, cihazı geri göndermeyi düşündüğünü söylüyor.","turns":[{"ai":"I'll be honest, I'm close to sending the whole thing back, because it froze mid-test with a patient sitting right there.","aiTr":"Açık konuşayım, her şeyi geri göndermeye çok yakınım; tam bir hasta oradayken test ortasında dondu.","hint":"I completely understand, and I'm sorry you've been put in that position. Thank you for raising it straight away.","keys":["sorry","raising it","understand"]},{"ai":"The screen's gone black and it won't reboot, so is this a hardware problem?","aiTr":"Ekran karardı ve yeniden başlamıyor; bu bir donanım sorunu mu?","hint":"From what you're describing, it sounds more like a software bug than a hardware fault, which means we can fix it remotely.","keys":["software bug","hardware fault","remotely"]},{"ai":"Remotely is all very well, but I've got a full waiting room, so what's the realistic timeline?","aiTr":"Uzaktan güzel de, bekleme salonum dolu; gerçekçi süre ne?","hint":"Our engineer can push an update within two hours, and I'll call you myself once it's back up and running.","keys":["within two hours","push an update","back up and running"]},{"ai":"And how do I know this isn't going to keep happening?","aiTr":"Peki bunun sürekli tekrarlanmayacağını nereden bileceğim?","hint":"That's a fair concern. We're getting to the bottom of what caused it, and I'll personally keep you in the loop.","keys":["bottom of","in the loop","caused"]}]}},"co-03":{"intro":"Fiyatı yarıya indirme önerisine diplomatik ama kararlı bir dille itiraz ediyor, tartışmayı veriye taşıyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Partner","en":"I'd like to put something on the table: if we brought the price down to 2,000 euros, I think deals would close a lot faster.","tr":"Bir öneri getirmek istiyorum: fiyatı 2.000 euroya indirirsek bence satışlar çok daha hızlı kapanır."},{"who":"Me","en":"I take your point, and I agree we need to shorten the sales cycle, but I'm not sure halving the price is the way to do it.","tr":"Söylediğin mantıklı, satış döngüsünü kısaltmamız gerektiğine de katılıyorum, ama bunun yolunun fiyatı yarıya indirmek olduğundan emin değilim."},{"who":"Me","en":"Given that each unit costs us 1,500 euros to build, we'd be cutting our gross margin from around 60 percent to a mere 25.","tr":"Her cihazın üretiminin bize 1.500 euroya mal olduğunu düşünürsek, brüt marjımızı yüzde 60 civarından yüzde 25 gibi cılız bir seviyeye indirmiş oluruz."},{"who":"Me","en":"Not only would that squeeze our cash flow, but it would also be very hard to raise the price again later.","tr":"Bu hem nakit akışımızı sıkıştırır hem de fiyatı daha sonra yeniden yükseltmeyi çok zorlaştırır."},{"who":"Partner","en":"I hear you, but the feedback from clinics is pretty consistent: the device is too expensive.","tr":"Seni anlıyorum ama kliniklerden gelen geri bildirim oldukça tutarlı: cihaz çok pahalı."},{"who":"Me","en":"That's a fair concern, though what I'm hearing in those conversations is something slightly different.","tr":"Bu haklı bir endişe, ama o görüşmelerde benim duyduğum şey biraz farklı."},{"who":"Me","en":"What clinics are really struggling with isn't the price itself, but the fact that they can't yet see the return on it.","tr":"Kliniklerin asıl zorlandığı şey fiyatın kendisi değil, bu paranın karşılığını henüz görememeleri."},{"who":"Me","en":"Framed in terms of monthly savings, the same 4,000 euros starts to look like a sensible investment rather than a cost.","tr":"Aylık tasarruf üzerinden sunulduğunda aynı 4.000 euro bir maliyet değil, mantıklı bir yatırım gibi görünmeye başlıyor."},{"who":"Partner","en":"That's a fair point, so how do you propose we make those savings tangible?","tr":"Haklı bir nokta; peki bu tasarrufu nasıl somutlaştırmayı öneriyorsun?"},{"who":"Me","en":"We could put together a simple ROI calculator showing, for instance, that a clinic running 100 tests a month saves 1,500 euros.","tr":"Örneğin ayda 100 test yapan bir kliniğin 1.500 euro tasarruf ettiğini gösteren basit bir yatırım getirisi hesaplayıcısı hazırlayabiliriz."},{"who":"Partner","en":"All right, let's give it two months before we touch the pricing.","tr":"Peki, fiyatlandırmaya dokunmadan önce buna iki ay verelim."},{"who":"Me","en":"Sounds like a plan, and I appreciate you hearing me out on this.","tr":"Anlaştık; bu konuda beni dinlediğin için de teşekkür ederim."}],"vocab":[{"en":"put something on the table","tr":"bir öneriyi masaya koymak, gündeme getirmek","ex":"I'd like to put a new idea on the table.","def":"to suggest an idea so that people can discuss it"},{"en":"I take your point","tr":"söylediğini kabul ediyorum","ex":"I take your point, but I see it differently.","def":"I accept that what you say is partly true (often said before disagreeing)"},{"en":"shorten the sales cycle","tr":"satış döngüsünü kısaltmak","ex":"We need to shorten the sales cycle.","def":"to reduce the time between first contact and a finished sale"},{"en":"squeeze cash flow","tr":"nakit akışını sıkıştırmak","ex":"A big price cut would squeeze our cash flow.","def":"to reduce the money a company has available to run day to day"},{"en":"return (on something)","tr":"getiri, karşılık","ex":"Clinics can't yet see the return on the device.","def":"the money or benefit you get back from what you spend"},{"en":"frame something in terms of","tr":"bir şeyi ... üzerinden sunmak","ex":"Framed in terms of savings, the price looks reasonable.","def":"to present an idea in a particular way so people see it differently"},{"en":"a sensible investment","tr":"mantıklı bir yatırım","ex":"The device is a sensible investment for a busy clinic.","def":"money spent in a reasonable way that is likely to pay off"},{"en":"make something tangible","tr":"bir şeyi somutlaştırmak","ex":"A calculator makes the savings tangible.","def":"to make something real and easy to see or understand"},{"en":"put together","tr":"hazırlamak, bir araya getirmek","ex":"We could put together a simple ROI calculator.","def":"to create or prepare something by combining parts"},{"en":"Sounds like a plan.","tr":"Anlaştık. / İyi plan.","ex":"Two months of testing? Sounds like a plan.","def":"an informal way to agree to a proposal"}],"grammar":{"title":"Inversion after 'Not only'","tr":"'Not only' cümle başına gelince soru düzeni kullanılır (yardımcı fiil + özne). İkinci kısım 'but ... also' ile gelir. Bu yapı itirazına ağırlık ve resmiyet katar.","examples":["Not only would that squeeze our cash flow, but it would also be hard to raise the price later.","Not only does the device save time, but it also removes the need for an expert in the room.","Not only is the price high, but the value is also hard to see."]},"questions":[{"q":"Why does the speaker object to halving the price?","options":["It would damage the brand's image","It would cut the gross margin to about 25 percent","Competitors would do the same","The distributor would refuse"],"a":1},{"q":"What does the speaker imply about raising the price later?","options":["It would be easy to do","It would require investor approval","It would be very difficult"],"a":2},{"q":"According to the speaker, what are clinics really struggling with?","options":["Seeing the return on the device","Understanding the software","Finding space for the device"],"a":0},{"q":"How would you describe the speaker's tone throughout?","options":["Dismissive and impatient","Uncertain and apologetic","Sarcastic","Firm but respectful"],"a":3},{"q":"What does the partner's final line suggest?","options":["They have rejected the price cut for good","They are willing to postpone the price decision","They want to raise the price immediately"],"a":1}],"gaps":[{"s":"I take your ___, but I'm not sure halving the price is the way to do it.","a":"point","hint":"görüş, nokta"},{"s":"Not only would that ___ our cash flow, but it would also be hard to raise the price later.","a":"squeeze","hint":"sıkıştırmak"},{"s":"How do you propose we make those savings ___?","a":"tangible","hint":"somut"},{"s":"Let's give it two months before we touch the ___.","a":"pricing","hint":"fiyatlandırma"}],"order":[{"a":"We need to shorten the sales cycle."},{"a":"Let's give it two months before we touch the pricing."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Fiyatı yarıya indirmenin doğru yol olduğundan emin değilim.","en":"I'm not sure halving the price is the way to do it.","keys":["not sure","halving the price"]},{"tr":"Kliniklerin asıl zorlandığı şey fiyatın kendisi değil.","en":"What clinics are really struggling with isn't the price itself.","keys":["struggling with","price itself"]},{"tr":"Bu konuda beni dinlediğin için teşekkür ederim.","en":"I appreciate you hearing me out on this.","keys":["appreciate","hearing me out"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Business partner","personaTr":"İş ortağı","scene":"Ortağın donanımı bedava verip tüm geliri abonelikten elde etmeyi öneriyor. Sen diplomatik ama net biçimde itiraz edip pilot uygulama öneriyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"I've been thinking: why don't we give the hardware away and make all our money on subscriptions?","aiTr":"Düşünüyordum da: neden donanımı ücretsiz verip tüm paramızı aboneliklerden kazanmıyoruz?","hint":"I take your point, but given that each unit costs us 1,500 euros to build, we'd be funding every sale out of our own pocket.","keys":["take your point","given that","1,500 euros"]},{"ai":"Surely the subscriptions would make up for that over time, though?","aiTr":"Ama zamanla abonelikler bunu telafi etmez mi?","hint":"In theory, yes, but not only would it take years to break even, it would also squeeze our cash flow.","keys":["not only","break even","cash flow"]},{"ai":"So what's really holding clinics back, in your view?","aiTr":"Sence klinikleri asıl geri tutan ne?","hint":"What's really holding them back is that they can't see the return yet, so we need to make the savings tangible.","keys":["holding them back","return","tangible"]},{"ai":"Fair enough. How would you like to move forward?","aiTr":"Peki. Nasıl ilerlemek istersin?","hint":"I'd propose piloting both models with a handful of clinics for two months and letting the numbers decide.","keys":["piloting","both models","two months","numbers"]}]}},"in-01":{"intro":"Sahnede, etkileyici bir açılış ve güçlü bir kapanışla üç dakikalık bir sunum yapıyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Me","en":"Good afternoon — I'm {name}, founder of AIHEAR.","tr":"İyi günler — ben {name}, AIHEAR'ın kurucusuyum."},{"who":"Me","en":"Here's a number worth sitting with: roughly one in five people on the planet lives with some degree of hearing loss.","tr":"Üzerinde biraz düşünmeye değer bir rakam: dünyada her beş kişiden yaklaşık biri bir dereceye kadar işitme kaybıyla yaşıyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"That's well over a billion people, and the overwhelming majority of them will never be tested.","tr":"Bu, bir milyarı rahatlıkla aşan bir insan sayısı demek ve bunların ezici çoğunluğu hiçbir zaman test edilmeyecek."},{"who":"Me","en":"It isn't for lack of demand; it's because there simply aren't enough audiologists, and in smaller towns the wait for an appointment can stretch to months.","tr":"Sebebi talep eksikliği değil; yeterince odyolog yok ve küçük şehirlerde randevu bekleme süresi aylara uzayabiliyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"So we asked ourselves a simple question: what if the test didn't need an expert in the room at all?","tr":"Biz de kendimize basit bir soru sorduk: Ya test için odada bir uzmana hiç gerek olmasaydı?"},{"who":"Me","en":"The result is an autonomous, AI-assisted audiometer: the patient puts on headphones, presses a button whenever they hear a tone, and the AI adapts the test in real time.","tr":"Ortaya çıkan şey otonom, yapay zekâ destekli bir odyometre: hasta kulaklığı takıyor, bir ses duyduğunda düğmeye basıyor ve yapay zekâ testi gerçek zamanlı olarak uyarlıyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"In under ten minutes, it produces a full audiogram.","tr":"On dakikadan kısa sürede eksiksiz bir odyogram çıkarıyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"Not only is it fast, but in a blind study at two university hospitals it matched a trained audiologist in 94% of cases.","tr":"Üstelik yalnızca hızlı değil; iki üniversite hastanesinde yapılan kör bir çalışmada vakaların %94'ünde eğitimli bir odyologla aynı sonucu verdi."},{"who":"Me","en":"We monetise through device sales and a monthly software subscription, which gives us a healthy stream of recurring revenue.","tr":"Gelirimizi cihaz satışları ve aylık yazılım aboneliğinden elde ediyoruz; bu da bize sağlıklı bir tekrarlayan gelir akışı sağlıyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"We're already on our third prototype, with five paying customers and a team of six spanning engineering, medicine and business.","tr":"Şimdiden üçüncü prototipimizdeyiz; beş ödeme yapan müşterimiz ve mühendislik, tıp ve iş alanlarını kapsayan altı kişilik bir ekibimiz var."},{"who":"Me","en":"We're raising €500,000 to take us through CE certification and into the European market.","tr":"Bizi CE sertifikasyonundan geçirip Avrupa pazarına taşıyacak 500.000 € yatırım topluyoruz."},{"who":"Me","en":"Hearing care will never scale one audiologist at a time — and with your support, it won't have to.","tr":"İşitme sağlığı hiçbir zaman tek tek odyologlarla ölçeklenemez — sizin desteğinizle buna gerek de kalmayacak."}],"vocab":[{"en":"worth sitting with","tr":"üzerinde düşünmeye değer","ex":"Here's a number worth sitting with.","def":"worth pausing to think about carefully"},{"en":"the overwhelming majority","tr":"ezici çoğunluk","ex":"The overwhelming majority are never tested.","def":"almost all of a group"},{"en":"for lack of","tr":"...eksikliğinden","ex":"It isn't for lack of demand.","def":"because there is not enough of something"},{"en":"stretch to","tr":"...e uzamak","ex":"The wait can stretch to months.","def":"to continue for a long time"},{"en":"adapt something in real time","tr":"bir şeyi gerçek zamanlı uyarlamak","ex":"The AI adapts the test in real time.","def":"to change something instantly as needed"},{"en":"blind study","tr":"kör çalışma","ex":"In a blind study, the results matched in 94% of cases.","def":"a study where the people comparing results don't know which is which"},{"en":"monetise","tr":"gelire dönüştürmek, para kazanmak","ex":"We monetise through device sales and subscriptions.","def":"to earn money from a product"},{"en":"recurring revenue","tr":"tekrarlayan gelir","ex":"The subscription brings in recurring revenue.","def":"income that comes in regularly"},{"en":"span","tr":"kapsamak","ex":"Our team spans engineering, medicine and business.","def":"to cover a range of areas"},{"en":"scale","tr":"ölçeklenmek","ex":"Hearing care will never scale one audiologist at a time.","def":"to grow quickly without costs growing as fast"}],"grammar":{"title":"Inversion after 'Not only'","tr":"'Not only' cümle başına gelince yardımcı fiil özneden önce gelir (Not only is it fast...). İkinci kısım genellikle 'but (also)' ile tamamlanır ve sunumda etkileyici bir vurgu yaratır.","examples":["Not only is it fast, but it matched a trained audiologist in 94% of cases.","Not only do we sell the device, but we also earn a monthly fee.","Not only is the market huge, but it is also underserved."]},"questions":[{"q":"What point does the founder make with 'It isn't for lack of demand'?","options":["People don't want hearing tests","The problem is the supply of experts, not patients' interest","The device is too expensive"],"a":1},{"q":"What is the purpose of the question 'what if the test didn't need an expert in the room at all?'","options":["To introduce the core idea behind the product","To criticise audiologists","To ask the investors for advice"],"a":0},{"q":"Why does the founder mention the blind study?","options":["To show the device is cheap","To explain the team structure","To prove the results are clinically credible"],"a":2},{"q":"What does the founder imply about the business model?","options":["It depends only on one-off sales","It combines device sales with steady subscription income","It is still undecided"],"a":1},{"q":"What is the tone of the closing line?","options":["Confident and visionary","Apologetic and cautious","Angry and critical"],"a":0}],"gaps":[{"s":"The ___ majority of them will never be tested.","a":"overwhelming","hint":"ezici"},{"s":"It isn't for ___ of demand.","a":"lack","hint":"eksiklik"},{"s":"We ___ through device sales and a monthly software subscription.","a":"monetise","hint":"gelir elde etmek"},{"s":"Hearing care will never ___ one audiologist at a time.","a":"scale","hint":"ölçeklenmek"}],"order":[{"a":"In under ten minutes it produces a full audiogram."},{"a":"We're already on our third prototype."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Bu, talep eksikliğinden değil.","en":"It isn't for lack of demand.","keys":["for lack of demand"]},{"tr":"Sadece hızlı değil, aynı zamanda doğru.","en":"Not only is it fast, but it is also accurate.","keys":["not only is it fast","accurate"]},{"tr":"Bekleme süresi aylara uzayabiliyor.","en":"The wait can stretch to months.","keys":["stretch to months"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"VC partner","personaTr":"Risk sermayesi fonu ortağı","scene":"Sunumdan sonra bir VC ortağı seni sıkıştırıyor; kısa, net ve kendinden emin cevaplar ver.","turns":[{"ai":"You've picked a big problem, but why hasn't anyone cracked this already?","aiTr":"Büyük bir sorun seçmişsiniz, ama neden bunu daha önce kimse çözemedi?","hint":"Because until now the test needed an expert in the room, and what we've done is make it fully autonomous.","keys":["expert in the room","autonomous","what we've done"]},{"ai":"Autonomous is a bold claim — how do you know it's accurate?","aiTr":"Otonom iddialı bir söz — doğru olduğunu nereden biliyorsunuz?","hint":"In a blind study at two university hospitals, it matched a trained audiologist in 94% of cases.","keys":["blind study","94","matched"]},{"ai":"Walk me through how you monetise.","aiTr":"Nasıl gelir elde ettiğinizi bana adım adım anlatın.","hint":"We sell the device and charge a monthly software subscription, which gives us recurring revenue.","keys":["subscription","recurring revenue","sell the device"]},{"ai":"And what does this round get you?","aiTr":"Peki bu yatırım turu size ne kazandıracak?","hint":"The €500,000 takes us through CE certification and into the European market.","keys":["CE certification","European market","500,000"]}]}},"ai-03":{"intro":"Prototipini, riskleri de açıkça kabul ederek ikna edici ve olgun bir dille sunuyorsun.","text":[{"en":"Thanks for making the time, and what I'd like to do is show you the device rather than just talk about it.","tr":"Zaman ayırdığınız için teşekkürler; yapmak istediğim, cihazdan sadece bahsetmek değil, size onu göstermek."},{"en":"This is an AI-assisted audiometer, built to make hearing tests faster and far more accessible without sacrificing clinical accuracy.","tr":"Bu, klinik doğruluktan ödün vermeden işitme testlerini daha hızlı ve çok daha erişilebilir kılmak için yapılmış, yapay zekâ destekli bir odyometre."},{"en":"What you're holding is our third iteration, and the first was, quite literally, a laptop and a pair of headphones.","tr":"Elinizde tuttuğunuz üçüncü sürümümüz; ilki ise kelimenin tam anlamıyla bir dizüstü bilgisayar ve bir kulaklıktı."},{"en":"Having completed the core development phase, we're now de-risking the product rather than inventing it.","tr":"Temel geliştirme aşamasını tamamladığımız için artık ürünü icat etmiyor, risklerini azaltıyoruz."},{"en":"We validated it in a blind study across two university hospitals, comparing it head-to-head with trained audiologists on 200 participants aged 18 to 75.","tr":"Cihazı iki üniversite hastanesinde, 18-75 yaş arası 200 katılımcı üzerinde eğitimli odyologlarla birebir karşılaştırarak kör bir çalışmada doğruladık."},{"en":"The results matched in 94% of cases, and where they didn't, the discrepancies were minor and never altered the diagnosis.","tr":"Sonuçlar vakaların %94'ünde eşleşti; eşleşmediği durumlarda ise farklar küçüktü ve tanıyı hiçbir zaman değiştirmedi."},{"en":"Those findings were published in a medical journal last spring.","tr":"Bu bulgular geçen bahar bir tıp dergisinde yayımlandı."},{"en":"Our main focus now is securing the CE mark, which, as a Class IIa device, we can't sell in Europe without.","tr":"Şu anki ana odağımız CE işaretini almak; Sınıf IIa bir cihaz olarak bu işaret olmadan Avrupa'da satış yapamayız."},{"en":"We've brought in an experienced regulatory consultant, and the target is certification by the end of next year.","tr":"Deneyimli bir mevzuat danışmanıyla çalışmaya başladık ve hedefimiz gelecek yılın sonuna kadar sertifika almak."},{"en":"I won't pretend there's no risk, because certification timelines have a habit of slipping, and we've built that into our plans.","tr":"Risk yokmuş gibi yapmayacağım; sertifikasyon takvimleri kaymaya meyillidir ve bunu planlarımıza dahil ettik."},{"en":"Not only would the €500,000 carry us through certification, but it would also fund our entry into the European market.","tr":"500.000 € bizi yalnızca sertifikasyonun sonuna kadar taşımakla kalmayacak, Avrupa pazarına girişimizi de finanse edecek."}],"vocab":[{"en":"iteration","tr":"sürüm, yineleme","ex":"This is our third iteration.","def":"one version of a product in a series of improvements"},{"en":"quite literally","tr":"kelimenin tam anlamıyla","ex":"The first prototype was, quite literally, a laptop.","def":"used to stress that something is exactly true"},{"en":"de-risk","tr":"riskini azaltmak","ex":"We are now de-risking the product.","def":"to reduce the risks of a project or investment"},{"en":"head-to-head","tr":"birebir (karşılaştırma)","ex":"We compared the device head-to-head with audiologists.","def":"in direct comparison or competition"},{"en":"discrepancy","tr":"tutarsızlık, fark","ex":"The discrepancies were minor.","def":"a difference between things that should be the same"},{"en":"alter the diagnosis","tr":"tanıyı değiştirmek","ex":"None of the differences altered the diagnosis.","def":"to change what doctors decide is wrong with a patient"},{"en":"secure the CE mark","tr":"CE işaretini almak","ex":"Our focus is securing the CE mark.","def":"to succeed in getting something after a lot of effort"},{"en":"bring in","tr":"(dışarıdan) dahil etmek, işe almak","ex":"We decided to bring in an experienced regulatory consultant.","def":"to involve someone with special skills"},{"en":"have a habit of","tr":"...meyilli olmak","ex":"Certification timelines have a habit of slipping.","def":"to tend to happen often"},{"en":"carry someone through","tr":"birini ...sonuna kadar taşımak","ex":"The round would carry us through certification.","def":"to provide enough support to reach the end of something"}],"grammar":{"title":"Inversion after 'Not only'","tr":"'Not only' cümle başında olunca yardımcı fiil özneden önce gelir: Not only would the money... Yatırımcı sunumunda iki faydayı güçlü biçimde vurgular. İkinci kısım genelde 'but ... also' ile gelir.","examples":["Not only would the €500,000 carry us through certification, but it would also fund our entry into Europe.","Not only did the results match in 94% of cases, but none of the differences altered the diagnosis.","Not only is the device faster, but it is also more accessible."]},"questions":[{"q":"What does the speaker mean by 'de-risking the product rather than inventing it'?","options":["The technology still needs to be invented","The core technology works, and now they are reducing the remaining risks","They are planning to sell the company"],"a":1},{"q":"What happened in the cases where the results didn't match?","options":["The discrepancies were minor and never altered the diagnosis","The device missed serious hearing loss","The audiologists made mistakes"],"a":0},{"q":"Why can't the company sell in Europe yet?","options":["It has no distributor","The price is too high","It doesn't have the CE mark yet"],"a":2},{"q":"What is the speaker's attitude to the certification risk?","options":["They deny it exists","They are openly realistic about it","They blame the consultant"],"a":1},{"q":"Why does the speaker say 'quite literally' about the first prototype?","options":["To apologise for the old design","To suggest the laptop is still used","To make a joke about headphones","To stress how basic the first version really was"],"a":3}],"gaps":[{"s":"What you're holding is our third ___.","a":"iteration","hint":"sürüm"},{"s":"The discrepancies were minor and never ___ the diagnosis.","a":"altered","hint":"değiştirdi"},{"s":"Certification timelines have a ___ of slipping.","a":"habit","hint":"eğilim"},{"s":"Not ___ would the money carry us through certification, but it would also fund our entry into Europe.","a":"only","hint":"sadece"}],"order":[{"a":"The first was quite literally a laptop and headphones."},{"a":"We have brought in an experienced regulatory consultant."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Farklar küçüktü ve tanıyı hiç değiştirmedi.","en":"The discrepancies were minor and never altered the diagnosis.","keys":["minor","diagnosis"]},{"tr":"Hedefimiz gelecek yılın sonuna kadar sertifika almak.","en":"Our target is certification by the end of next year.","keys":["certification","end of next year"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Investor","personaTr":"Yatırımcı","scene":"Londra'da seçici bir sağlık teknolojisi yatırımcısı, rakamlara geçmeden önce seni zorlayıcı sorularla sınıyor.","turns":[{"ai":"Before we get into numbers, convince me this is more than a clever demo.","aiTr":"Rakamlara geçmeden önce, bunun akıllıca bir demodan fazlası olduğuna beni ikna edin.","hint":"Fair enough. We validated it in a blind study at two university hospitals, and it matched trained audiologists in 94% of cases.","keys":["blind study","94","matched"]},{"ai":"And the remaining 6%, should that worry me?","aiTr":"Peki ya kalan %6; bu beni endişelendirmeli mi?","hint":"Not really: the discrepancies were minor and never altered the diagnosis, which is what clinicians care about.","keys":["discrepancies","minor","diagnosis"]},{"ai":"Regulation is where most medtech start-ups come unstuck, so where are you on that?","aiTr":"Medikal teknoloji girişimlerinin çoğu mevzuatta çuvallar; siz bu konuda neredesiniz?","hint":"We've brought in an experienced regulatory consultant and we're targeting the CE mark by the end of next year, though timelines do have a habit of slipping.","keys":["regulatory consultant","CE mark","habit of slipping"]},{"ai":"So what exactly does my €500,000 buy?","aiTr":"Peki 500.000 €'m tam olarak neyi satın alıyor?","hint":"Not only would it carry us through certification, but it would also fund our entry into the European market.","keys":["carry us through","certification","European market"]}]}},"in-02":{"intro":"Birim ekonomisini ve gelir akışlarını bir VC'ye ikna edici ve akıcı biçimde anlatıyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Me","en":"Sooner or later, every investor conversation I have comes down to the same deceptively simple question: how does this business actually make money?","tr":"Er ya da geç, yaptığım her yatırımcı görüşmesi göründüğünden daha zor olan aynı soruya varıyor: Bu iş aslında nasıl para kazanıyor?"},{"who":"Me","en":"The short answer is that we have two revenue streams, and they do very different jobs.","tr":"Kısa cevap şu: iki gelir akışımız var ve bunlar çok farklı işlevler görüyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"The first is the device itself, which we sell for €4,000 and which costs us around €1,500 to build.","tr":"Birincisi cihazın kendisi; onu 4.000 €'ya satıyoruz ve üretimi bize yaklaşık 1.500 €'ya mal oluyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"That gives us a gross margin of roughly 60 percent — comfortably healthy by hardware standards.","tr":"Bu bize yaklaşık yüzde 60'lık bir brüt marj sağlıyor — donanım standartlarına göre rahatlıkla sağlıklı bir oran."},{"who":"Me","en":"What really interests investors, though, is the second stream: a €99 monthly software fee paid by every clinic.","tr":"Yine de yatırımcıları asıl ilgilendiren ikinci akış: her kliniğin ödediği aylık 99 €'luk yazılım ücreti."},{"who":"Me","en":"Modest as it looks, that fee is recurring, predictable and sticky, which is precisely what makes the business fundable.","tr":"Göründüğü kadar mütevazı olsa da bu ücret düzenli, öngörülebilir ve kalıcı; işi yatırım alabilir kılan da tam olarak bu."},{"who":"Me","en":"Scale it to 1,000 clinics, and the subscriptions alone would generate roughly €1.2 million a year.","tr":"Bunu 1.000 kliniğe ölçeklendirin, yalnızca abonelikler yılda yaklaşık 1,2 milyon € gelir yaratır."},{"who":"Me","en":"We're not there yet, of course: we currently have five paying customers, so the bulk of that growth lies ahead.","tr":"Elbette henüz orada değiliz: şu anda beş ödeme yapan müşterimiz var, yani bu büyümenin büyük bölümü önümüzde."},{"who":"Me","en":"On the cost side, salaries, certification and marketing account for the lion's share of our spending.","tr":"Maliyet tarafında harcamalarımızın aslan payını maaşlar, sertifikasyon ve pazarlama oluşturuyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"Certification in particular is front-loaded, which is why our early years are the most cash-hungry.","tr":"Özellikle sertifikasyon maliyetleri en başta yoğunlaşıyor; ilk yıllarımızın en çok nakit tüketen dönem olmasının nedeni de bu."},{"who":"Me","en":"Even so, our model shows us turning profitable in year three.","tr":"Yine de modelimiz üçüncü yılda kâra geçeceğimizi gösteriyor."}],"vocab":[{"en":"deceptively simple","tr":"göründüğünden daha zor","ex":"It's a deceptively simple question.","def":"seeming easy but actually more difficult"},{"en":"revenue stream","tr":"gelir akışı","ex":"We have two revenue streams.","def":"one source of income for a business"},{"en":"by ... standards","tr":"...standartlarına göre","ex":"Sixty percent is healthy by hardware standards.","def":"compared with what is normal in that area"},{"en":"sticky","tr":"kalıcı (müşteri ya da gelir)","ex":"Software fees are sticky because clinics rarely cancel.","def":"describing customers or revenue that rarely leave"},{"en":"fundable","tr":"yatırım alabilir","ex":"Recurring revenue is what makes the business fundable.","def":"attractive enough for investors to fund"},{"en":"the bulk of","tr":"...nin büyük kısmı","ex":"The bulk of our growth lies ahead.","def":"most of something"},{"en":"account for","tr":"...yi oluşturmak","ex":"Salaries account for much of our spending.","def":"to form a part or amount of something"},{"en":"the lion's share","tr":"aslan payı","ex":"Salaries take the lion's share of our budget.","def":"the largest part"},{"en":"front-loaded","tr":"en başta yoğunlaşan (maliyet)","ex":"Certification costs are front-loaded.","def":"happening mostly at the beginning"},{"en":"turn profitable","tr":"kâra geçmek","ex":"We expect to turn profitable in year three.","def":"to start making more money than you spend"}],"grammar":{"title":"Concession with 'as': Modest as it looks…","tr":"'Sıfat + as + özne + fiil' yapısı 'although' anlamı taşır ama daha akıcı ve etkileyicidir: 'Modest as it looks' = 'Mütevazı görünse de'.","examples":["Modest as it looks, that fee is recurring and predictable.","Small as we are, we already have paying customers.","Expensive as certification is, it is unavoidable."]},"questions":[{"q":"What does 'deceptively simple' suggest about the investors' question?","options":["It can be answered in one word","It is a polite way to end a meeting","It sounds easy but requires a careful answer"],"a":2},{"q":"According to the speaker, what makes the business fundable?","options":["The high device price","Recurring, predictable and sticky software revenue","The number of employees"],"a":1},{"q":"What is the speaker's attitude to the 60% margin?","options":["Satisfied, but not treating it as the main selling point","Embarrassed by it","Unsure whether it is accurate"],"a":0},{"q":"Why are the early years described as 'cash-hungry'?","options":["Salaries will fall later","Certification costs come mostly at the beginning","Customers pay late"],"a":1},{"q":"What does 'We're not there yet, of course' signal?","options":["Frustration with the team","Doubt about the product","Honesty about the company's current stage"],"a":2}],"gaps":[{"s":"Modest ___ it looks, that fee is recurring and predictable.","a":"as","hint":"-se de (as)"},{"s":"Salaries, certification and marketing account for the lion's ___ of our spending.","a":"share","hint":"pay"},{"s":"Certification in particular is front-___.","a":"loaded","hint":"en başta yoğunlaşan"},{"s":"Our model shows us turning ___ in year three.","a":"profitable","hint":"kârlı"}],"order":[{"a":"We have two revenue streams that do very different jobs."},{"a":"The bulk of that growth lies ahead."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Mütevazı görünse de bu ücret tekrarlayan bir gelir.","en":"Modest as it looks, that fee is recurring revenue.","keys":["modest as it looks","recurring revenue"]},{"tr":"Harcamalarımızın aslan payını maaşlar oluşturuyor.","en":"Salaries account for the lion's share of our spending.","keys":["account for","lion's share"]},{"tr":"Üçüncü yılda kâra geçmeyi bekliyoruz.","en":"We expect to turn profitable in year three.","keys":["turn profitable","year three"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"VC associate doing due diligence","personaTr":"Ön inceleme yapan VC analisti","scene":"Bir VC analisti finansal modelini ayrıntılı olarak sorguluyor; rakamları akıcı ve güvenle savun.","turns":[{"ai":"Let's get into the unit economics — what does a single device actually earn you?","aiTr":"Birim ekonomisine girelim — tek bir cihaz size aslında ne kazandırıyor?","hint":"We sell it for €4,000 and it costs around €1,500 to build, which gives us a gross margin of roughly 60 percent.","keys":["gross margin","60 percent","1,500"]},{"ai":"Hardware margins don't usually excite investors — why should they here?","aiTr":"Donanım marjları genelde yatırımcıları heyecanlandırmaz — burada neden heyecanlandırsın?","hint":"What really matters is the €99 monthly fee, which is recurring, predictable and sticky.","keys":["what really matters","recurring","sticky"]},{"ai":"Where is most of the money going right now?","aiTr":"Şu anda paranın çoğu nereye gidiyor?","hint":"Salaries, certification and marketing account for the lion's share, and certification is front-loaded.","keys":["lion's share","front-loaded","account for"]},{"ai":"So when do you see the business turning a profit?","aiTr":"Peki işin ne zaman kâra geçeceğini öngörüyorsunuz?","hint":"Our model shows us turning profitable in year three.","keys":["year three","turning profitable","third year"]}]}},"in-04":{"intro":"Yatırımcının en sert sorularını savunmaya geçmeden, net ve özgüvenli bir şekilde yanıtlıyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Investor","en":"I'll be blunt: this space already has well-funded incumbents, so why would anyone need you?","tr":"Açık konuşacağım: bu alanda zaten iyi finanse edilmiş yerleşik şirketler var, o hâlde size neden ihtiyaç olsun?"},{"who":"Me","en":"The incumbents make excellent audiometers, but every one of them still relies on a trained audiologist in the room.","tr":"Yerleşik şirketler mükemmel odyometreler yapıyor ama hepsi hâlâ odada eğitimli bir odyoloğun bulunmasına dayanıyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"That's exactly the bottleneck we remove, because our device runs the whole test autonomously in under ten minutes.","tr":"Bizim ortadan kaldırdığımız darboğaz tam olarak bu, çünkü cihazımız tüm testi on dakikadan kısa sürede otonom olarak yapıyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"As for the consumer apps, none of them are certified medical devices, so no clinic can build a diagnosis on their results.","tr":"Tüketici uygulamalarına gelince, hiçbiri sertifikalı tıbbi cihaz değil, bu yüzden hiçbir klinik sonuçlarına dayanarak teşhis koyamaz."},{"who":"Investor","en":"Fine, but what's to stop one of those incumbents from simply replicating your approach?","tr":"Peki, ama o yerleşik şirketlerden birinin yaklaşımınızı basitçe taklit etmesini ne engelleyecek?"},{"who":"Me","en":"What they can't replicate quickly is our data, since the model has been trained on thousands of real clinical tests.","tr":"Hızla taklit edemeyecekleri şey verimiz, çünkü model binlerce gerçek klinik testle eğitildi."},{"who":"Me","en":"Not only is that data hard to come by, but it also took close partnerships with hospitals to collect.","tr":"Bu veriyi bulmak hem zor hem de toplamak için hastanelerle yakın iş birlikleri gerekti."},{"who":"Me","en":"Being a team of six, we can also iterate in weeks on decisions that would take a large manufacturer a year.","tr":"Altı kişilik bir ekip olarak, büyük bir üreticinin bir yılını alacak kararlarda haftalar içinde yenileme yapabiliyoruz."},{"who":"Investor","en":"And what's the one thing that keeps you up at night?","tr":"Peki sizi geceleri uyutmayan o tek şey ne?"},{"who":"Me","en":"Candidly, it's certification, since Class IIa timelines have a way of slipping no matter how well you plan.","tr":"Açık söylemek gerekirse sertifikasyon, çünkü Sınıf IIa takvimleri ne kadar iyi planlarsanız planlayın kayma eğiliminde."},{"who":"Me","en":"Having anticipated that, we started the process early and brought in a regulatory consultant with a strong CE track record.","tr":"Bunu öngördüğümüz için sürece erken başladık ve CE konusunda güçlü bir geçmişe sahip bir mevzuat danışmanıyla çalışmaya başladık."},{"who":"Investor","en":"That's refreshingly honest; most founders insist they have no real risks at all.","tr":"Bu insanı ferahlatan bir dürüstlük, çünkü çoğu kurucu hiçbir gerçek riskleri olmadığında ısrar eder."}],"vocab":[{"en":"incumbent","tr":"yerleşik şirket, pazardaki köklü oyuncu","ex":"The incumbents make excellent audiometers.","def":"a company that already holds a strong position in a market"},{"en":"bottleneck","tr":"darboğaz","ex":"The shortage of audiologists is the real bottleneck.","def":"a point where a process slows down because of a limit"},{"en":"build a diagnosis on","tr":"teşhisi ... üzerine kurmak","ex":"No clinic can build a diagnosis on an uncertified app.","def":"to use something as the basis for a medical decision"},{"en":"replicate","tr":"taklit etmek, aynısını yapmak","ex":"They can't replicate our data quickly.","def":"to copy something exactly"},{"en":"hard to come by","tr":"bulunması zor","ex":"Clinical data is hard to come by.","def":"difficult to find or get"},{"en":"iterate","tr":"yinelemeli olarak geliştirmek","ex":"A small team can iterate in weeks.","def":"to improve something by repeating cycles of changes"},{"en":"keep someone up at night","tr":"birini geceleri uyutmamak","ex":"Certification is what keeps me up at night.","def":"to worry someone a lot"},{"en":"have a way of doing something","tr":"...me eğiliminde olmak","ex":"Timelines have a way of slipping.","def":"to often happen in a certain way, usually an annoying one"},{"en":"track record","tr":"geçmiş başarı kaydı","ex":"Our consultant has a strong CE track record.","def":"the record of someone's past successes or failures"},{"en":"refreshingly honest","tr":"insanı ferahlatacak kadar dürüst","ex":"Her answer was refreshingly honest.","def":"honest in a pleasant and unusual way"}],"grammar":{"title":"Participle clauses: Being …, Having done …","tr":"Cümleyi kısaltmak ve sebep ya da zaman ilişkisini zarifçe göstermek için '-ing' ile başlayan yan cümle kullanılır. 'Having + V3' ana eylemden önce olan bir eylemi anlatır.","examples":["Having anticipated that, we started the process early.","Being a team of six, we can iterate in weeks.","Having seen the clinical data, the investor relaxed."]},"questions":[{"q":"What is the investor's tone at the start?","options":["Blunt and challenging","Warm and supportive","Confused","Apologetic"],"a":0},{"q":"According to the founder, what is the real bottleneck in hearing testing?","options":["The price of headphones","Slow internet in clinics","The need for a trained audiologist in the room","The lack of apps"],"a":2},{"q":"Why does the founder say clinics can't rely on consumer apps?","options":["They are too expensive","They aren't certified medical devices","They need an expert to run them"],"a":1},{"q":"What does the founder imply by saying Class IIa timelines 'have a way of slipping'?","options":["Delays are common even with good planning","Certification will probably be cancelled","The founder has already missed a deadline"],"a":0},{"q":"What does the investor's final remark suggest?","options":["They think the founder is naive","They doubt the clinical data","They want to end the meeting","They see the founder's candour as a strength"],"a":3}],"gaps":[{"s":"Every one of them still ___ on a trained audiologist in the room.","a":"relies","hint":"dayanmak"},{"s":"That's exactly the ___ we remove.","a":"bottleneck","hint":"darboğaz"},{"s":"That kind of data is hard to come ___.","a":"by","hint":"bulmak"},{"s":"We brought in a consultant with a strong CE track ___.","a":"record","hint":"geçmiş başarı"}],"order":[{"a":"What they can't replicate quickly is our data."},{"a":"Most founders insist they have no real risks at all."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Sizi geceleri uyutmayan tek şey ne?","en":"What's the one thing that keeps you up at night?","keys":["keeps you up at night"]},{"tr":"Bu tür verileri bulmak zor.","en":"That kind of data is hard to come by.","keys":["hard to come by"]},{"tr":"Sertifikasyon takvimleri, ne kadar iyi planlarsanız planlayın kayma eğilimindedir.","en":"Certification timelines have a way of slipping, no matter how well you plan.","keys":["have a way of slipping","no matter how"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Experienced angel investor","personaTr":"Deneyimli melek yatırımcı","scene":"Deneyimli bir yatırımcı sert ve doğrudan sorular soruyor; savunmaya geçmeden net cevaplar ver.","turns":[{"ai":"This space already has well-funded incumbents. Why would anyone need you?","aiTr":"Bu alanda zaten iyi finanse edilmiş yerleşik şirketler var. Size neden ihtiyaç olsun?","hint":"The incumbents all rely on a trained audiologist in the room, and that's exactly the bottleneck we remove.","keys":["incumbents","bottleneck","audiologist"]},{"ai":"And the consumer apps? Some of them are free.","aiTr":"Peki tüketici uygulamaları? Bazıları ücretsiz.","hint":"None of them are certified medical devices, so no clinic can build a diagnosis on their results.","keys":["certified","medical devices","diagnosis"]},{"ai":"What's to stop an incumbent from replicating your approach?","aiTr":"Yerleşik bir şirketin yaklaşımınızı taklit etmesini ne engelleyecek?","hint":"What they can't replicate quickly is our data, and being a team of six, we iterate far faster than they do.","keys":["replicate","data","iterate","faster"]},{"ai":"What keeps you up at night?","aiTr":"Sizi geceleri ne uyutmuyor?","hint":"Candidly, certification, so having anticipated delays, we started early and brought in an experienced regulatory consultant.","keys":["certification","started early","consultant","candidly"]}]}},"fu-02":{"intro":"Bir gazeteciyle sağlık verilerinin mülkiyeti, onam ve gizlilik ile yapay zekâ performansı arasındaki gerilim üzerine derinlikli bir röportaj yapıyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Journalist","en":"With health data now being traded like a commodity, who, in your view, actually owns it?","tr":"Sağlık verileri artık bir emtia gibi alınıp satılırken, sizce gerçekte kime ait?"},{"who":"Me","en":"It's the patient who owns it, and ownership only means something if it comes with genuine control over who uses it and why.","tr":"Sahibi hastadır ve sahiplik ancak onu kimin, neden kullandığı üzerinde gerçek bir kontrolle birlikte gelirse bir anlam taşır."},{"who":"Me","en":"Hence the importance of informed consent, which should be specific, written in plain language and, crucially, revocable.","tr":"Bilgilendirilmiş onamın önemi de buradan gelir; onam belirli olmalı, sade bir dille yazılmalı ve en önemlisi geri alınabilmeli."},{"who":"Me","en":"Consent buried on page twelve of a contract isn't consent at all; it's a liability waiver in disguise.","tr":"Bir sözleşmenin on ikinci sayfasına gömülmüş onam, onam değildir; kılık değiştirmiş bir sorumluluk feragatnamesidir."},{"who":"Me","en":"Where data is used for research, it has to be properly anonymised, since stripping out names alone rarely prevents re-identification.","tr":"Veriler araştırmada kullanılıyorsa gerçekten anonimleştirilmeli, çünkü yalnızca isimleri silmek yeniden kimliklendirmeyi nadiren önler."},{"who":"Me","en":"In Europe, GDPR classifies health data as a special category, so the bar for processing it is deliberately high.","tr":"Avrupa'da GDPR sağlık verilerini özel nitelikli kategori olarak sınıflandırıyor; bu yüzden onları işlemenin çıtası bilinçli olarak yüksek."},{"who":"Me","en":"Rather than treat compliance as a box-ticking exercise, we built privacy into the architecture: our AI runs on the device, so test data never leaves the clinic.","tr":"Uyumluluğu göstermelik bir formalite olarak görmek yerine gizliliği mimarinin içine yerleştirdik: yapay zekâmız cihazın üzerinde çalışıyor, bu yüzden test verileri klinikten hiç çıkmıyor."},{"who":"Journalist","en":"Doesn't that leave you at a disadvantage against competitors who hoover up every scrap of data they can get?","tr":"Bu sizi ele geçirebildikleri her veri kırıntısını silip süpüren rakiplere karşı dezavantajlı duruma düşürmüyor mu?"},{"who":"Me","en":"To some extent, yes, and I won't pretend the trade-off isn't real: more data generally means better models, but every additional dataset widens the attack surface.","tr":"Bir ölçüde evet ve bu ödünleşim gerçek değilmiş gibi yapmayacağım: daha fazla veri genellikle daha iyi modeller demek, ama her ek veri seti saldırı yüzeyini genişletiyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"Having weighed the two, we chose to improve the model only with anonymised data from clinical studies whose participants gave explicit consent.","tr":"İkisini tarttıktan sonra modeli yalnızca katılımcılarının açık onay verdiği klinik çalışmalardan gelen anonim verilerle geliştirmeyi seçtik."},{"who":"Me","en":"Not only is that the right thing to do, but in a sector built on trust, it's also a competitive advantage.","tr":"Bu sadece doğru olan şey değil; güven üzerine kurulu bir sektörde aynı zamanda bir rekabet avantajı."}],"vocab":[{"en":"commodity","tr":"emtia, ticari mal","ex":"Health data is being traded like a commodity.","def":"a product that can be bought and sold"},{"en":"revocable","tr":"geri alınabilir","ex":"Consent should always be revocable.","def":"able to be cancelled or taken back"},{"en":"in plain language","tr":"sade bir dille","ex":"Consent forms should be written in plain language.","def":"using simple, clear words"},{"en":"liability waiver","tr":"sorumluluk feragatnamesi","ex":"Hidden consent is really a liability waiver.","def":"a document that protects a company from legal responsibility"},{"en":"re-identification","tr":"yeniden kimliklendirme","ex":"Removing names alone rarely prevents re-identification.","def":"working out who a person is from data that was meant to be anonymous"},{"en":"the bar is high","tr":"çıta yüksek","ex":"The bar for processing health data is high.","def":"the standard you must reach is difficult"},{"en":"build something into","tr":"...in içine yerleştirmek","ex":"We built privacy into the architecture.","def":"to make something a basic part of a design from the start"},{"en":"box-ticking exercise","tr":"göstermelik formalite","ex":"Compliance shouldn't be a box-ticking exercise.","def":"doing something only to satisfy formal rules, not because it helps"},{"en":"hoover up","tr":"silip süpürmek, toplamak","ex":"Some companies hoover up every scrap of data.","def":"to collect large amounts of something, often greedily"},{"en":"attack surface","tr":"saldırı yüzeyi","ex":"Every extra dataset widens the attack surface.","def":"all the points where a system could be attacked or leak data"}],"grammar":{"title":"Cleft sentences: 'It's … who/that …'","tr":"'It is + vurgulanan öğe + who/that' yapısı cümlenin bir parçasını öne çıkarır. Röportajlarda asıl mesajı netleştirmek ve karşı görüşü düzeltmek için kullanılır.","examples":["It's the patient who owns it.","It's trust, not data, that gives us an advantage.","It's the architecture that protects patients, not a policy document."]},"questions":[{"q":"According to the speaker, when does ownership of data 'mean something'?","options":["When it comes with genuine control over its use","When the data is sold","When a doctor signs it"],"a":0},{"q":"What does the speaker imply about consent 'buried on page twelve'?","options":["It is the most legal form of consent","It protects the company rather than the patient","It is easy for patients to read"],"a":1},{"q":"Why does removing names alone not go far enough?","options":["GDPR does not allow it","It slows down the AI","People can often still be re-identified"],"a":2},{"q":"What is the speaker's attitude to the trade-off?","options":["Dismissive","Confused","Defensive and evasive","Candid about its costs"],"a":3},{"q":"What does the final sentence suggest?","options":["Privacy can also be good for business","The company regrets its choice","Competitors will soon fail"],"a":0}],"gaps":[{"s":"Consent should be specific, written in plain language and ___.","a":"revocable","hint":"geri alınabilir"},{"s":"Stripping out names alone rarely prevents ___.","a":"re-identification","hint":"yeniden kimliklendirme"},{"s":"We built privacy ___ the architecture.","a":"into","hint":"içine"},{"s":"Every additional dataset widens the attack ___.","a":"surface","hint":"yüzey"}],"order":[{"a":"It's the patient who owns the data."},{"a":"Our AI runs on the device itself."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Uyumluluğu göstermelik bir formalite olarak görmek yerine gizliliği mimarinin içine yerleştirdik.","en":"Rather than treat compliance as a box-ticking exercise, we built privacy into the architecture.","keys":["box-ticking exercise","built privacy into"]},{"tr":"Bu sadece doğru olan şey değil, aynı zamanda bir rekabet avantajı.","en":"Not only is that the right thing to do, but it's also a competitive advantage.","keys":["not only is","competitive advantage"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Journalist","personaTr":"Gazeteci","scene":"Deneyimli bir sağlık muhabiri, şirketinin veri politikasını sorguluyor. Net, dürüst ve ikna edici yanıtlar veriyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"Health data is being traded like any other commodity; who, in your view, really owns it?","aiTr":"Sağlık verileri diğer emtialar gibi alınıp satılıyor; sizce gerçekte kime ait?","hint":"It's the patient who owns it, and that only means something if it comes with genuine control over who uses it.","keys":["patient who owns","genuine control"]},{"ai":"Isn't informed consent largely a fiction, though, given that nobody reads the small print?","aiTr":"Ama kimse ince yazıları okumadığına göre bilgilendirilmiş onam büyük ölçüde bir kurgu değil mi?","hint":"It often is, which is why consent should be specific, written in plain language and revocable.","keys":["plain language","revocable","specific"]},{"ai":"What stops your own company from quietly hoovering up patient data?","aiTr":"Sizin şirketinizi hasta verilerini sessizce toplamaktan alıkoyan ne?","hint":"The architecture itself: our AI runs on the device, so test data never leaves the clinic.","keys":["architecture","runs on the device","never leaves the clinic"]},{"ai":"Surely that puts you at a disadvantage against less scrupulous competitors?","aiTr":"Bu sizi daha az titiz rakiplere karşı dezavantajlı duruma düşürmüyor mu?","hint":"To some extent, but we only use anonymised data from consenting study participants, and in a sector built on trust that's an advantage.","keys":["to some extent","anonymised","built on trust"]}]}},"in-03":{"intro":"Yatırımcının ilk teklifini nazik ama kararlı biçimde geri çeviriyor, seyrelme ve değerleme üzerine ince bir pazarlık yürütüyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Investor","en":"Having followed your progress closely, we're keen to come in with €500,000 for a 25 percent stake.","tr":"İlerlemenizi yakından takip ettikten sonra, yüzde 25'lik bir hisse için 500.000 euroyla girmeye hevesliyiz."},{"who":"Me","en":"I appreciate the confidence, but that would value the business at just two million post-money, which doesn't reflect where we are today.","tr":"Güveninizi takdir ediyorum ama bu, şirketi yatırım sonrası sadece iki milyon olarak değerler ve bugün geldiğimiz noktayı yansıtmaz."},{"who":"Me","en":"Not only do we have a working third-generation prototype, but five clinics are already paying for it.","tr":"Hem çalışan üçüncü nesil bir prototipimiz var hem de beş klinik şimdiden bunun için ödeme yapıyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"What really sets us apart, though, is a peer-reviewed study showing 94 percent agreement with trained audiologists.","tr":"Ama bizi asıl farklı kılan, eğitimli odyologlarla yüzde 94 uyum gösteren hakemli bir çalışma."},{"who":"Me","en":"We've also secured a €250,000 European innovation grant, which means our clinical validation was funded without giving away any equity.","tr":"Ayrıca 250.000 euroluk bir Avrupa inovasyon hibesi aldık; yani klinik doğrulamamız hiç hisse vermeden finanse edildi."},{"who":"Investor","en":"All fair points, but until you have the CE mark, we're essentially pricing in regulatory risk.","tr":"Hepsi yerinde noktalar ama CE işaretini alana kadar esasen düzenleyici riski fiyata yansıtıyoruz."},{"who":"Me","en":"That's precisely what this round is for: closing out certification and laying the groundwork for our European launch.","tr":"Bu tur tam da bunun için: sertifikasyonu tamamlamak ve Avrupa lansmanımızın zeminini hazırlamak."},{"who":"Me","en":"Given that, I'd propose €2.5 million post-money for 20 percent, which keeps dilution manageable while still giving you meaningful upside.","tr":"Bunu göz önüne alarak yüzde 20 için yatırım sonrası 2,5 milyon öneriyorum; bu, seyrelmeyi makul tutarken size de anlamlı bir getiri potansiyeli sağlar."},{"who":"Investor","en":"We could get comfortable with that, provided we take a board seat.","tr":"Yönetim kurulunda bir koltuk almamız şartıyla buna ısınabiliriz."},{"who":"Me","en":"I'd actually welcome that, since what we need is a hands-on partner rather than just capital.","tr":"Aslında bunu memnuniyetle karşılarım, çünkü ihtiyacımız olan şey sadece sermaye değil, işin içinde olan bir ortak."},{"who":"Investor","en":"Then let's get a term sheet over to you this week.","tr":"O zaman bu hafta size bir ön anlaşma metni gönderelim."}],"vocab":[{"en":"come in with","tr":"(bir miktarla) yatırıma girmek","ex":"The fund is keen to come in with €500,000.","def":"to invest a particular amount in a funding round"},{"en":"set apart","tr":"farklı kılmak, ayırt etmek","ex":"Our clinical data sets us apart.","def":"to make someone or something different from and better than others"},{"en":"peer-reviewed","tr":"hakemli","ex":"The results appeared in a peer-reviewed journal.","def":"checked by other experts before being published"},{"en":"give away equity","tr":"hisse vermek","ex":"The grant let us fund research without giving away equity.","def":"to hand over part of the ownership of a company"},{"en":"price in","tr":"fiyata yansıtmak","ex":"Investors price in regulatory risk.","def":"to include a possible risk or event in the price you pay"},{"en":"lay the groundwork","tr":"zemin hazırlamak","ex":"This round lays the groundwork for our European launch.","def":"to do the early work that makes later success possible"},{"en":"dilution","tr":"(hisse) seyrelme","ex":"We want to keep dilution manageable.","def":"the drop in existing owners' share when new shares are issued"},{"en":"upside","tr":"getiri potansiyeli","ex":"The deal still gives investors meaningful upside.","def":"the possible gain or benefit from a decision"},{"en":"hands-on","tr":"işin içinde olan, uygulamada aktif","ex":"We need a hands-on partner rather than just capital.","def":"actively involved in the work, not only watching"},{"en":"term sheet","tr":"ön anlaşma metni (yatırım şartları belgesi)","ex":"They will send a term sheet this week.","def":"a short document listing the main terms of an investment"}],"grammar":{"title":"Cleft sentences for emphasis: What … is …","tr":"'What + cümle + is …' yapısı, vurgulamak istediğin bilgiyi cümlenin sonuna taşır. Müzakerede en güçlü argümanını öne çıkarmak için kullanılır.","examples":["What really sets us apart is a peer-reviewed study.","What we need is a hands-on partner rather than just capital.","What worries investors most is regulatory risk."]},"questions":[{"q":"How does the founder respond to the first offer?","options":["Accepts it gratefully","Politely pushes back, arguing it undervalues the company","Rejects it angrily and walks away","Asks for a week to think"],"a":1},{"q":"Why does the founder mention the European grant?","options":["To ask the investor to repay it","To complain about bureaucracy","To show that key work was funded without dilution"],"a":2},{"q":"What does the investor imply by 'pricing in regulatory risk'?","options":["The lower offer reflects uncertainty around certification","They want a higher price for the device","They will pay the regulator directly"],"a":0},{"q":"What is the founder's attitude to giving the investor a board seat?","options":["Reluctant but resigned","Strongly against it","Indifferent","Genuinely positive"],"a":3},{"q":"What does 'let's get a term sheet over to you' suggest?","options":["The negotiation has failed","The investor is ready to formalise the deal","The founder must send more data first"],"a":1}],"gaps":[{"s":"What really sets us ___ is a peer-reviewed study.","a":"apart","hint":"farklı kılmak"},{"s":"Until you have the CE mark, we're essentially pricing ___ regulatory risk.","a":"in","hint":"fiyata yansıtmak"},{"s":"This keeps ___ manageable while still giving you meaningful upside.","a":"dilution","hint":"seyrelme"},{"s":"What we need is a ___ partner rather than just capital.","a":"hands-on","hint":"işin içinde olan"}],"order":[{"a":"What we need is a hands-on partner rather than just capital."},{"a":"That is precisely what this round is for."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Bu teklif şirketin bugünkü durumunu yansıtmıyor.","en":"This offer doesn't reflect where the company is today.","keys":["doesn't reflect","today"]},{"tr":"Bu, seyrelmeyi makul bir seviyede tutar.","en":"This keeps dilution manageable.","keys":["dilution","manageable"]},{"tr":"Sadece sermaye değil, işin içinde olan bir ortak istiyoruz.","en":"We want a hands-on partner, not just capital.","keys":["hands-on partner","capital"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Lead investor at a VC fund","personaTr":"Bir VC fonunun lider yatırımcısı","scene":"Fon turu yönetmek istiyor ama düşük bir değerleme öneriyor; kararlı ama yapıcı bir şekilde pazarlık ediyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"We'd like to come in with €500,000 for a 25 percent stake. How does that sound?","aiTr":"Yüzde 25'lik hisse için 500.000 euroyla girmek istiyoruz. Kulağa nasıl geliyor?","hint":"I appreciate the confidence, but that values us at just two million post-money, which doesn't reflect where we are today.","keys":["doesn't reflect","two million","post-money"]},{"ai":"Convince me. What justifies a higher number?","aiTr":"İkna edin beni. Daha yüksek bir rakamı ne haklı çıkarıyor?","hint":"Not only do five clinics already pay for our device, but our peer-reviewed study shows 94 percent agreement with audiologists.","keys":["not only","peer-reviewed","94 percent"]},{"ai":"Even so, without the CE mark we're carrying most of the regulatory risk.","aiTr":"Yine de CE işareti olmadan düzenleyici riskin çoğunu biz taşıyoruz.","hint":"That's precisely what this round is for: closing out certification and laying the groundwork for our European launch.","keys":["precisely","certification","groundwork"]},{"ai":"So what would you propose, and what's in it for us?","aiTr":"Peki ne önerirsiniz ve bizim için bunun getirisi ne?","hint":"I'd propose 2.5 million post-money for 20 percent, with a board seat for you, since what we need is a hands-on partner.","keys":["2.5 million","20 percent","board seat","hands-on"]}]}}};
